	 ('195932417','76561198021947841','2427430','20251230',3,1,0,0,10,'I''ll cut it short: I enjoyed this EE edition more than the vanilla one.
In fact, I never managed to push myself to complete the original, but I already got to quite satisfying endings in the Enhanced edition.

I did use a few content restoration mods available in the Workshop. Good enough to offer an enjoyable experience after just a week from the release, I guess.
Many people compare EE "vanilla" to the uber-modded original one filled with nostalgia PLUS 15 years of community time to tweak it - sounds a bit unfair to me for a release that''s been out 7 days at most. Especially if you consider that a few of those days included real life drone bombardments to the country of the devs. And besides that they still have pushed 2 hotfixes for all 3 games in a week - which is wild.

Also check the playtime of the negative reviews - 0.3 hours? That''s just ridiculous - they didn''t even get to a point where any of the changes they''re so mad about happened. That''s just review bombing - a smear campaign that''s destined to fade over time.

Afterall the team who''s been in charge of the three Enhanced Editions is not the original team, but a smaller "tech upgrade" team of just 7 people.

I believe they did a good job and you should just enjoy the game with an open mind, contextualising it in the bigger picture.

That''s it. Time for me to play Clear Sky now - I personally liked Shadow of Chornobyl more so far.
CoP is a step forward tech wise, refined gameplay and all, but in my opinion part of the atmosphere has been lost. There are only 3 main bigger zones in the game, and all felt quite flat to me. "Been there done that". Felt more like a spinoff.'),
