	 ('84121689','76561198094422940','1410000','20251230',6,0,0,0,10,'EDIT: 1/27/21
Was sent a steam key by Amir to try the updates that were pushed since I refunded. Physics are better but still not quite there. The wing actually surges now after pulling full brakes (still feels a bit off timing wise though).  The biggest thing to me is that there were updates. To me I still believe this would be classed as early access. I also understand that the main market is probably standalone hardware which is why the graphics are quite simple. I hope to see the game is given further updates but I still wouldn''t purchase the game at $10.  

Original Review:

After reading the descriptions here and on the website, my expectations were set far too high regarding the physics. This is a simulation game and the physics are what make or break this. I could excuse the bad GUI and environments if the flying physics were good. Unfortunately, neither are. People may claim this is the best VR skydive sim available to the general public (and it may be) but it is very unpolished. Not worth $10 to me but go ahead and find out for yourself if you must.

While diving and motoring wings are different, they do share some similarities. I have a touch over 20 hours flying a wing with my paramotor... To the creators credit (Amir Valinia) He was very fast to respond to my questions on Facebook and was very polite.'),
