	 ('26258167','76561197989724295','513320','20251230',17,0,0,0,9,'It''s a crying shame that this game doesn''t have more reviews!  I am very excited by this game''s story, setting, and tone.  It''s Alice in Wonderland reinterpreted to be a sci-fi puzzle-em-up adventure game.  What more could you want, eh? 

The puzzles are a little simple at the start, but I am assuming that is because the game wants to establish the basic mechanics/language for the puzzles and then will ramp difficulty.  As for the story, there more going on than what I have seen in my limited time playing, and I''m intrigued by the few snippets of over-arching plot that have been teased!

Overall, I have found ALICE VR to be an immersive, engaging, and beutiful game that I cannot wait to keep playing.  

I know some of the reviews mention graphics quality, but I think those issues have been patched already and, based on my anecdotal and limited experience, the concerns seemed limited to Vive users (the game looked amazing on my Oculus and when played in 2D).

If you''re curious to see how this game plays, take a look at the video below (there is a short clip of the game running on the Oculus headset towards the end):  https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EciWCcgoNYs'),
