	 ('22489150','76561197977444987','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I`ve always wanted a good single player poker game that actually played realistically with decent characters. This game does that.
It starts you off in a dark  underground pub or bar and introduces you to 4 characters, only two of which I recognised which was Ash, and not from the crappy tv series either.  I also recognised Max, while never having played the game, know by reputation. Or is he called sam? I get mixed up between the dog and bunny. However, the characters reveal their personalities as you play the game. It`s more slow a reveal than the first game, but nicely paced in my view.

The characterisations and how they play is really the best part of the game. Some of the jokes and stories are great.

You can buy drinks for your opponents to weaken their skills, a bit silly really and they never refuse. I would`ve preferred it without. Sexy bar lady though with an air of `can`t be be bothered` to her.

You also have a  female voiced robot that deals the cards. i prefrred when the cards where just dealth naturally in the 1st game. She can be also highly annoying both in attitude and voice. I preferred the original way without the dumb dealer robot.

Game feels a little easier to win. Maybe too easy. You can free extra tables and card design but there`s not much to free up.

My main wish would be for more choice in characters with just as much depth to play against. Make it about 10 with clothing variety so each game feels fresh. Yes, it would be a fair amount of work, but I`d pay £30 for it.

Anyway recommended.'),
	 ('116348279','76561198250505468','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'It''s pretty good.'),
	 ('19472988','76561198141549902','386990','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'I loved this game. The art is beautiful, and its a horrifyingly accurate depiction of mental illness. I would like to point out, while she never really has a diagnosis, it''s heavily implied that Sam has Depression. However, I think her actions and situation fit perfectly for someone who has Borderline Personality Disorder. If you felt you could identify with her feelings and struggles I would highly suggest looking into it for yourself. Very sucessful treatments are availaible!!! 

ANYWAY, Back to the game itself: I think I enjoyed it so much because it was freakishly similar to my own personal story- but with perspective and storytelling that comes with a game. It has helped feel better about my own situation. I cried so much, holy shit. Tip: if you can make it past the scenes in the coach, it gets much more interesting and involved, so don''t be afraid to stick it out even if the beginning bores you. 

Other than that, the dialouge is a bit posh and the time spent inbetween periods of action is extensive, so if you feel you can''t identify with the story you may not enjoy it. What makes the long dialouge bearable are the emotions you get from it. It''s very moving. I would have appreciated more character diversity in terms of body type and skin color but other than that I have no complaints. Also, every little desicion counts. As far as I can tell there are about 6-8 "Endings"- but there are actually only 3-4 scenes in which you make choices, which demonstrates how much each one matters. It makes the play simple but still significant, which I really liked. 

I played this instead of studying for a test... 10/10 would procrastinate again.'),
	 ('17259025','76561198164651871','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,2,'good game no regrets but there is a robot that insults you every five minuits 99/10'),
	 ('90427328','76561198053446725','234710','20251230',1,1,0,0,9,'A single-player poker game without redeeming qualities.

There are two main attractions of this game, game content unlocks & unique character dialogue. Neither of these provide much draw to the game nor make up for the game''s many flaws.

The game content unlocks (for Portal & Borderlands) personally drew me to the game years back. However, these games are significantly less popular than they were when I first purchased the game. Now, these provide little to no reward for the game. I personally see little value in these unlocks. I''d be hard to imagine a new player feeling any more excitement about them.

As for the character dialogue, you''d firstly have to be familiar with the characters before gleaning any enjoyment from the (tame) banter. Unfortunately, the dialogue becomes noticeably repetitive after a few hours of game play. 

These are the key draws to a game with horrifically slow & tedious game play, no multiplayer, and poor UI not to mention the mandatory internet connectivity. If you''re looking for a poker game I suggest looking elsewhere.'),
