	 ('14426970','76561198067073256','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'+ Unlockable ''stages'' add some variety and atmosphere
+ Slightly better AI
+ Even more funny dialogue
- Gameplay not that different from the first game

It''s Poker Night, only better! But actually, about the same.

     Poker Night 2 casts a whole new set of characters into the same roles as before. Brock Samson replaces Strong Bad as the somewhat aggressive player, Max replaces Tycho as the ultra-conservative player, Ash Williams of Evil Dead (odd choice, but okay) fills in for Heavy as the conservative yet crafty player, and Claptrap as the crazy, unpredictable one. You can select two styles of poker, Hold Em'' and Omaha. The new Omaha game seems to present slightly better odds, making it easier to decide whether to ante up or not. Ultimately, the game is a bit harder, but not by much. Very quickly you will find that this is the same game with a new coat of polish. 
     Unlockables have improved a bit, as unlocking an entire ''set'' (chips, table, and cards) can take you to a new arena that changes the atmosphere (one for each character).
     That''s it, really. It''s a basic poker game with some funny dialogue to listen to (until it gets repetative). Don''t think you''re going to train for the World Series of Poker with this game. 

75/100
Grab a cold one and relax. It''s Poker Night.'),
