	 ('171028215','76561198289200795','1302780','20251230',2,0,0,0,10,'This game is great, it feels super similar to a game I used to play online (pretty sure I played an old game from this franchise) and it is just as great as I remember for the most part.

There''s quite a lot of units with their own stats and some even have special powers, like piercing through up to 2 enemies, hitting all enemies, stun, aoe, your usual suspects for special powers.
There''s also badges to make them more powerful, by making them shoot faster, deal more damage, cost less, reduced cooldown times between placing or chance at double shot, this sounds fine [i]but we''ll get back to this[/i].
There''s 50 levels and I have beaten all of them. I think that is plenty for a game like this, though I wish there would be an endless level since I think that always makes things more interesting and will allow the player to get those final chievs while also providing a challenge.
There''s also plenty of enemies, most of em just basic enhanced versions of older zombies with more hp, more armor, but also some with special abilities like aoe heal for allies (your enemies ofc), aoe shield giving, becoming invisible, fun stuff.
The bosses also have abilities, but you have to pay attention to what they do from like boss 3 on out because they just start saying ability_desc_x with x just being an internal number used for assigning descriptions I suppose.
I do like how this game has achievements though, I love having things to do and achievements to get, so this is great, [b]if only they would be reasonable[/b].

Now for the less fun stuff.
I feel like lots of characters just become useless after you get better versions, this is usually the case in games like this and I feel like some sort of evolving or upgrading system would''ve helped remedy this. Like there is no reason to use an Aoe character when there is another more expensive version that deals more damage with chance to stun, once you get enough resource generation you don''t need the cheap alts anymore.
The badges are just awful. The tiny stat boost they give does not make it feel any better to use them, they are also super expensive to level up and there is no mass leveling, so everything is done manually, it sucks.
Like I said, the bosses don''t all have descriptions. In the discussions tab it was stated that this was unintentional, but that was about 4 years ago as of writing this, so yeah.
The grind. Like I said, badges are expensive to level, not only that, but you need lots of em if you wanna have any good stats on em. The achievements also seem like a pain. 2.5M damage with the laser? That is just straight up way too grindy and I''ve seen other people share the same sentiment. I like getting chievs after every level for dealing x damage, placing x units, killing x zombies, stuff that you do while playing, but forcing the player to use a unit for an insane amount of damage like that? No.

Overall, I think this game is still a fun experience. It''s really like those older games but with a new coat of paint. It has some questionable mechanics and choices, but still does a good job at being a fun little tower defense game for cheap :D'),
