	 ('558275','76561197972182252','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,' I''m no gambler, but even I can tell this is a terrible poker game. The character writing is funny though, and the scene changes when you use all the items in a set are fun.

If you have any knowledge of poker, stay the hell away from this game because the nonsensical betting will infuriate you. If you just want the unlocks, you may get them very fast, or you may NEVER get them, depending on which of the challenges you get. I got all the items but Glados'' in a couple hours, and I''m currently stuck having to win 3 hands in a row to unlock hers. That''s unlikely when the other players raise like retarded monkeys.

Winning tournaments is easy - fold on any opening less than two face cards (unless you''re the big blind and can get a ''free'' look at the flop) and let the idiots knock each other out of the game.

Winning multiple hands in a row  is just luck though. In the showdown, be prepared to have your blinds stolen a lot, unless you decide to play like a retarded monkey too.'),
	 ('109915971','76561199016371414','3330','20251230',1,0,0,0,5,'AH ZUMA'),
	 ('184986353','76561198194987527','3009850','20251230',29,21,0,0,0,'I shat my bed which caused a wanted status, in which I had to resort to defending myself... 40 in-game hours later I killed everyone in that room, I survived.. bloodied.. smelly.. and with one less arm. 

Having no witnesses, I was free.. but at what cost? Was being the poopoo stinky man really a crime? Did I have to murder all those inmates? Maybe... but the guy in the next room killed me with a wheelchair so I guess it didn''t really matter. 10/10'),
