	 ('84932966','76561197985219150','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'A fantastic sequel to a great original game. Worth playing, even if you''re not all that into Hold em, the dialogue will keep you in-game. Shame this was the end of the series, would have really liked to see a third game. They probably could have gotten some great characters, like Geralt from the Witcher to play the serious guy, Atreus to ask the other serious questions ("should I kill him?"), and Deadpool (Disneh slaps his face on everything) to encourage the boy. Who wouldn''t play that crossover poker game? And throw in Rick from Rick & Morty to lighten the mood which would be otherwise mostly dark humor (of course Rick is never dark...). There''s your million-dollar game that never was.

This game, more to the point, was good. Claptrap and Glados carry it. Love this game though, and the franchise (and publisher) died sleeping on brilliant ideas.'),
	 ('195323726','76561199009030258','2427430','20251230',4,1,0,0,10,'Honestly, this game needs more time.

Even as a remaster of a very old game, there are somehow bugs that I have never seen in the original, and the graphics looking a bit like the Source remake of Half Life 1, where it is barely any different, but now it looks more "shaded" and "realistic" than the release 16 years ago. Plus with all the Russia/USSR censorship makes me genuinely not think of touching either Clear Sky or Shadow of Chernobyl (not like I liked them at all)

But, to the main topic:
Is it worth buying right now?
No, it just isn''t, but buy the originals instead. The games too buggy, barely any workshop mods (the games been out for 1 day) and the graphics look pretty much the same, and in the og games with mods they would look much better than this official remaster.

If you got it for free, is it worth trying?
Yes, absolutely. Since I am one of those who got the game for free from owning the original trilogy, the game is not that bad. Achievements, workshop, hell even possibly trading cards hopefully coming out makes this game worth playing. But even though there are bugs, (like the bloodsuckers spawning out of the lair still asleep, and if you shoot one then the whole lair somehow gets alerted) but its still worth trying out.

In conclusion, this game needs more time to be polished, and get better overtime, (same with GSC''s new release as well but that''s just almost every video game released nowadays) but for now, those who got it for free, enjoy it and praise it, and those who bought it and played over the 2 hour limit without refunding, yall should have read the reviews and waited a bit before complaining about it! 

5.5/10 remaster'),
