	 ('36633656','76561198055356861','500670','20251230',0,0,0,0,0,'Keep Moving, Keep Shooting... It will feel unfair. You have one life and a single projectile or enemy attack will kill you. The screen is shaken by explosions as smoke, fire and blood obscure your view. You fight boss after boss all the while the terrain is shaped into a chaotic labrynth of destruction. But you keep moving, keep shooting. Then you start uncovering the hidden depth woven into the game. It''s not clear at first; you have much more power than you realize. The game feels unfair. Not helpless, but you can clearly see the odds are stacked against you. In some twisted way, it feels good. You could pause the game or reach a safezone, but the developers said FUCK THAT. Their design constantly puts you on edge, always balances you on the edge of your seat. There is no tutorial, no health regeneration, no allies. It''s just you and your sheer will to survive. And in my opinion, that''s pretty damn fair. So keep moving, keep shooting!'),
