	 ('39755077','76561198088380930','234710','20251230',5,0,0,0,10,'Poker Night 2 is a great follow up to the original Poker Night from Telltale Games. This time around you get an intro where you get to enter the Inventory through the door as oppose to the elevator like last time. The exploration of the facility showcases how much bigger the place is from only seeing the bar from last time. We get an introduction from each of the new opponents of the poker game. They are Brock Samson from the Adult Swim show Venture Bros., Claptrap from the Borderlands franchise, Ash Williams from the Evil Dead franchise, & Sam from the Sam & Max series. Max who was an opponent from the last game is present but is only see as a spectator this time. The rules of Texas Hold ‘Em remain the same only this time the stakes from each player is $20,000, and the match is over seen by GlaDos from the Portal games. She handles the card deal and raises the blinds according. As a bonus Omaha style poker is optional in case you’d like to change the gameplay. As you’d expect from the last game, there is lots of funny dialogue exchanges between the players. As well as different poker table felt and decks to unlock. Not as many choices like in the original, but the addition of Omaha style poker makes this sequel worth playing. I like how this game had a brief shot of a portrait of the former opponents from the last game: Heavy Weapons Guy, Strong Bad, & Tycho. It would of been great to see them had it not been for royalty rights. But I am glad this sequel got made regardless of what characters Telltale got permission to use. Crossover games are always fun to play, and I hope to see another visit to the Inventory sometime in the future.'),
