	 ('135236403','76561198242548172','3330','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'zuma might be the single greatest color-matching game, at least made by popcap. it''s completely simple in what it accomplishes, yet it nails every core foundation of what makes this type of game great:  gameplay (obviously), music, setting, and artstyle. in comparison to a similar color-matching game like bejeweled, zuma has significantly more interesting gameplay because there''s a larger variety of skillful ways to match colors by shooting through gaps and building combos around single or double color matches. not only that, but the visuals and music stand out because they work in tandem to support each other, sporting a wonderfully pleasant jungle-themed soundtrack while you explore ancient aztec (or something like that) temples, with dusty and surprisingly varied tracks. this is a striking comparison to bejeweled''s visuals because bejeweled is quite literally just gems on a board with a 2D background image of a fancy structure. basically buy zuma because it''s the goat'),
