	 ('181170880','76561198396214612','3110820','20251230',1,0,0,0,0,'I''ve only beaten 3 or 4 levels, but this is a very nice Mega Man-like so far. I like how it combines elements of both Mega Man Classic and Mega Man X. The graphics, music, and storyline are solid. I like how you''ve created your own lore.

I just have some nitpicks:
[strike]* As I said in the discussions, there are at least two areas where you can wall jump all the way up the side of buildings and walk on top of them offscreen, until you fall off the end of the level and die.[/strike] (Fixed by the dev)
* When a shot is fully charged, I wish the player character would start blinking or flashing. I dislike how the Mega Man games have a looping sound effect for charged shots because it can get annoying, but I think this game needs a visual indicator that a shot is charged.
* Some controls are not explained clearly during gameplay. I had to figure out how to dash on my own. Also, during cutscenes, I think there''s supposed to be a way to go to the next text box without skipping the whole cutscene, but I can''t figure out what it is. All I can do is press Start to skip each cutscene.
* In the Gallery, the small flavor text is very difficult to read. I know you''re working with pixel graphics, but there must be some way around this. Maybe you could make the flavor text window bigger to allow for a bigger font.
* If there is a boss weakness chain, it''s hard to figure out. Mega Man has the bosses named after their elements or weapons, but this game does not. It''s hard to figure out the bosses'' elements or weaknesses just from the pictures of them on the level select screen. I''m not saying you have to change their names, I just think there should be some other way to deliver hints on their weaknesses.'),
