	 ('9228899','76561198059774421','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,8,'There are so many things wrong with this game.  The dialogue gets old very quickly and there is no option to turn it off after a certain point.  No skill is required.  You win on blind luck which really takes away from the game considering it''s all about weighing the odds and trying to determine what cards the other players might have.  The only reason I bought this game was for the tournament prizes for Team Fortress 2 and Borderlands 2.  I enjoy playing cards but this game rubs me the wrong way.  It''s not a very well written poker game, it''s just a bunch of characters having an "I''m more witty than you" contest.  Was it worth the $5?  Not in my opinion.  The only reason I''m giving it any points is because you technically can play poker.  4/10'),
	 ('21262872','76561198046691883','244070','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'It reminds me of Blue Max, Dawn Patrol and Wings of War/ Wings of Glory boardgames or  Ace of Aces game books.

An easy to handle and quick to play turn per turn game, with a 2 players Hot Seat mode. Some additionnal stuff is available if you succeed to finish nations campaigns. If you expect a simulator like game, pass your way, this one is more based on tactics and strategy. A mission  can be played  in less than 30mn

Should you like previous boargames, you may wish that they had developped some add-ons with new planes, new WWI countries and more elaborate campaigns.'),
	 ('165694331','76561198167877769','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,4,'fun game, completed the adventure mode and finished all gauntlet levels on sun god rank.

the game starts off super chill and actually pretty relaxing to play, but don''t get too comfortable, the difficulty jumps very quick and the RNG of the powerups, marble order, etc. really makes the later stages here very difficult.'),
	 ('14581972','76561198063686667','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'This game made me rage so much that it is not funny. Mostly due to how pants-on-head-stupid I played it, constantly going all in and trying to bluff everyone into folding. But, unlike the first game, this does not work all the time. The AI is actually smarter this time around and, while I do miss the Heavy, the conversations between the characters are still a laugh to listen to and provide a lot of fanserive to those who know the franchises. 

