	 ('7903940','76561198067475836','234710','20251230',5,0,0,0,10,'If you enjoyed playing Poker Night at the Inventory, then your going to love it''s sequel. Taking place at the same old Inventory, only this time it''s a game of Texas Hold Em or Omaha against Brock Samson from Venture Bros, Claptrap from Borderlands 2, Ash Williams from Evil Dead, and Sam from Sam and Max, while the mechanical GLaDOS from Portal acts as the dealer in this game. The gameplay is more challenging this time with more money then the last game, and every so often the players will either try to raise the blinds or go all in, it''s a real gamble to see if your going to win or not. The game introduces the Inventory Tokens that act as your currency to buy beer for the players or to purchase Table Felts, Cards, and Chips, as their are 5 Table Sets. Buying drinks will sometimes help the player see their tells while unlocking the Table Sets from a specific theme will give the Inventory a new look, as well as some special dialogue for the characters along with some entertaining eliminations to the players. The exclusive items are back for both TF2 and Borderlands 2, by completing specific tasks, someone will place a Bounty Item on the table in which you have to win the tournament instead of knocking them out to win the item. I recommend playing Omaha to win the Bounty Items as you''ll have a better chance in getting a good hand most of the time. Just like it''s predecessor, the dialogue is wonderful to listen to, it''s not that often you see 3 video game characters, a TV show character and a Film character having a nice friendly and comical chat together. I only had a few issues with this game, mainly the missions you need to complete to unlock a bounty challenge, some of them are simple while others rely on luck to complete them, and that tends to be annoying. And once again, no Online play. But other then that, Poker Night 2 is an epic game and since it''s only $5.00 like it''s predecessor, it''s worth it. Especially when you can unlock Sam''s hat in TF2 which is awesome!'),
