	 ('55355345','76561198294880724','1086030','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'Short review for a short game:
At only 2.89 for a bit of somewhat trashy fun, I would recommend it! 

Longer short review:
I enjoyed the multiple endings and rate them from best to worst as
Odd>Neutral>Bad>Good>>>>Perfect
And the reason why I disliked perfect is it felt like the two characters only connected on a superficial level. I could see why Miley desired Emily but for Emily, who could choose from a pool of dozens of other partners for her entertainment, I was unconvinced. What makes Miley special for her to want to give up her lifestyle and start dating?
However, I got enjoyment out of all of the other endings, and the messier the night got the greater I was entertained (Odd ending is life!).
More on Emily - I feel like what Emily needs as a partner is either someone who is quiet and shy, or somebody to keep her in check and pull her back in a little (Possibly a bit of both), and that instead the game rewarded Miley with "better" endings for trying to match that energy and be a copy of Emily, rather than Miley just being herself. If we had learned a little more about Emily I think it would have helped, but I digress. 
Only other criticism is that I wasn''t a big fan of the soundtrack, but I turned it down. 
THE END.'),
