	 ('149159792','76561197988190262','386990','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Somehow I never wrote a review on this? Can''t believe it. Honestly one of my favorite Ebi-hime works. Its hard to say that I enjoyed it, the story is absolutely just melancholic to its very core with the happiest ending probably being one where you rely on your weird bestie and get over your love, but none of them really feel happy, and honestly, youre struck with that feeling of a byronic hero with the lead, someone who can never be happy. And it kinda works? These over dramatic queers and their extremely delightful extremely Romantic Lit style dialogue over everything. 

Ebi-hime''s best strength in my mind is evoking character and personality with text. Dialogue drips with whoevers speaking and prose soaks in Coleridges feelings. Asphyxia is all about this strength of hers. Though not exactly fun, its super memorable and left me laying on a couch thinking for a long long time and more than that FEELING these nebulous painful, uncomfortable feelings even longer. 

'),
