	 ('174642050','76561198034751875','3009850','20251230',59,3,0,0,10,'[h1] A disappointing sequel from the original [/h1]

Have to say, I am a little disappointed. As a long time fan of Mdickie, I was really hyped for this game, but this feel worse than original Hard Times (the 3D version on PC). This feels more like Hard Times 2D with a little more features

1. The atmosphere: Original Hard Times feels great. the prison was really big, each area is large and has things for you to do. The prison blocks were big with 2 floors, the yard actually feels like a yard with space to exercise, the shower room is private and guards rarely come, and other areas in the prison are similarly big. The prison in this one is tiny and doesn''t feel that great, and doesn''t really match the number of people you have in the prison
2. Interactions: Original Hard Times had a lot of things for you to do in different areas. For example, you can sit down and eat in the canteen (not pick up the food to eat, but actually sitting down and eat food from the tray on the table), you can study to improve skills in the library, you can lift weights in the yard to improve strength, you can work to make money in places such as hospital, workshop, canteen or library, all requiring enough stats to do it. 
3. The camera: Hard Times 3 (and the newer 3D games in general) feels really clunky. You have to adjust the camera all the time and a lot of times you cannot see yourself or other characters because the camera is really hard to control. It''s just bearable to play on controller but with keyboard it''s very annoying. The older 3D games camera is much easier to control.

With that said, it is not entirely bad. Some of the new things, such as guns are really fun to use. The ability to get released and have a life outside, and becoming guard are great. It was not in the original at all, and in Hard Times 2 it was very bare bone. 

Overall, a disappointing game compared to the original. Whereas remakes such as Old School, Wrestling Empire, or the 2D remakes of the 3D games such as Wrecked or The You Testament adds new features compared to the original, Hard Times 3 takes away many features instead. More things are added in this game, but the main focus of this game is the prison, and a lot of the things that made it cool in the original were removed here.

Edit: After a few more hours of gameplay my opinion remains the same. The free roam has a lot of areas but it''s very bare bone with not a lot of things for you to do. There''s nothing really that special or fun about being an officer either'),
