	 ('140141909','76561198032873045','73190','20251230',0,0,0,0,6,'If your into serious strategy, long games with the best realistic technologies and detailed (including pictures of allot of it) This game is one I have played off and on for years and I only wish they would make a PON II.  It is turn based and you won''t finish a game in one day, so patience and long term strategy is what your in for.
Do you want to hop in the seat of the USA, British Empire, Japan, China etc when the industrial revolution started and guide your development, research and global goals for the next 70 years... the game is a must have. 
The same company makes many turn based super indepth streategy games and I think they are the best at technical support and working on details for years after they make a game.  This game came out years ago and I could still go on their forums and get a reply from one of the developers usually in a day.  
Couldn''t say more positive things about the copany or the game ... but if you have a short attention span or hate strategically thinking and patience the game just wouldnt suit you.
Ive also got the Original Cival War game as well as the Cival War II they did... havent played the Cival War II yet but seems much the same.  They won me over with that first game with histories and actual pictures of most every real general in the war and all the attention to detal.

