	 ('199689162','76561198199824838','2427430','20251230',2,0,0,0,10,'100% Achievements | Hardest Difficulty
Rating: 10/10 – Long Live the Zone
Call of Pripyat – Enhanced Edition is hands down the best game of the original trilogy. It was great back in the day, but now it feels timeless — smoother, more polished, and still incredibly immersive. I beat it on the hardest difficulty, unlocked every achievement, and enjoyed every moment of it.
From the military storyline and grounded setting to the deep atmosphere and exploration, this game captures the feeling of a living, breathing Zone better than any other entry. The three regions are vast, dangerous, and filled with purpose. Every area feels handcrafted — rich with detail, smart encounters, and atmospheric storytelling. The pacing is tight, the characters are believable, and you feel like a real stalker — not just surviving, but solving a mystery and fulfilling your mission.
Performance-wise? Near perfect. I had maybe two crashes in over 35 hours of gameplay — that’s it. No scripting bugs, no broken quests, no stuttering. Just smooth, focused gameplay all the way through.
And this is coming from someone who beat Misery and Anomaly on their hardest settings — I know what a challenge looks like. But even after that, I can say with full confidence: vanilla Call of Pripyat doesn’t need mods to be great. It’s already challenging, immersive, and incredibly well-balanced. Mods can be fun, but nothing replaces the experience of a game crafted by experienced professionals.
Looking back after playing S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2, it’s obvious how much of that game was built on Call of Pripyat’s foundation. Sure, there are some small differences — in tone, in world logic, in layout — but that’s expected after over a decade of evolution. The heart is the same. And honestly, I find it hilarious seeing some loud voices online running anti-S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 campaigns, saying things like “Call of Pripyat was better” or “S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 can’t recapture the magic.” Like… did you even play both games properly? Call of Pripyat is still amazing — I’ve done five full playthroughs and it holds up incredibly well — but S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 is the next-gen Zone we were all waiting for.
Also, major respect to GSC Game World for removing all the outdated Soviet and Russian content. That was absolutely the right call. This is a Ukrainian game, built on Ukrainian land, tied to Ukrainian tragedy and resilience. In the context of the full-scale Russo-Ukrainian war, this move is not just appropriate — it’s essential. The Zone belongs to Ukraine.
P.S.
If you''re new to the series — start here.
If you''re a veteran stalker — you already know this is peak Zone.
No mods required, no tweaks needed — just you, your detector, and the ruins of Pripyat.
I recommend it HUGLY. Seriously.

P.S.S.
GSC gave all new versions to all players that had original games in library FOR FREE.
'),
	 ('174692126','76561199106027327','3009850','20251230',2,0,0,0,0,'The Game
