	 ('16409619','76561198083246612','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'If everything that is great in the world sat down to play poker

With a dog, a robot, a god among men, a badass, and another robot. 

Seriously though, five dollars is a fantastic bargain on Poker Night 2, especially if you know and love the characters like I do. The TF2 and Borderlands 2 unlocks are pretty awesome too! Enjoy hilarious dialogue between beloved characters and slam down a couple-a-beers. All around, it''s a pretty great time. there are a few gripes here though.
1. WARNING! THE BORDERLANDS 2 UNLOCKS DO NOT WORK AS THEY SHOULD. I HAD TO CONTACT GEARBOX SOFTWARE TO RECIEVE THEM. 
2. Dialogue loops. This happens quite often and unlike PN2s predecessor, this game has no option to lower the amount of poker table chatter or outright skip it. The jokes are hilarious, but can get grating. 
3. Ash isn''t voiced by Bruce Campbell. :P Not a serious complaint, as the VA does a good job, but I would''ve LOVED to see him reprise the role.

Wonderful game. The funniest I''ve played in years, the best crossover that isn''t Smash Bros i''ve seen, and getting the Max mask for the Mechromancer in Borderlands 2 is just awesome. I fully reccomend a full price purchase.'),
