	 ('176695840','76561198124878020','3009850','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'If you''re reading this you''re probably already familiar with MDickie games. There''s a certain kind of soul behind his games that is unique but familiar, and you can tell he put a lot of care into this one. The original Hard Time was a fun sandbox (that you can still get for free on his site), and this game elevates what made the original so fun. Not to mention the new mod support, which already has some great community made content even in the infancy of it''s addition.

The absurd moments that happen can make this the funniest game you''ve ever played, and the fact that it''s purely random makes it hit even harder. The best way I can describe it is carefully crafted and perfectly polished jank. This game isn''t buggy or broken, it just throws everything into a pot and lets you see what happens.

The most recent update added the old two floor prison cells, which is great to have back. I saw people mentioning missing the old layout in reviews, and it seems like MDickie actually read them and listened - and recreated them surprisingly fast. Hard Time has always felt like it lived in the shadow of his Wrestling games, but this time it feels like it''s finally being treated as an equal, and it''s great to see and even better to play.

If you like story driven games, this isn''t for you. But if you like games that give you everything you need to make your own story, then buy this immediately. You''ll inevitably end up feuding with a five foot tall bald 18 year old, having a psychotic breakdown and starting a prison riot because an inmate teased you for drinking milk, or accidentally giving the death sentence to a random civilian with no arms and only one leg who rolled into you with a wheelchair.

I wish that the character editor and officer/civilian roles were available from the start so everyone could experience these new options, but in the grand scheme of everything this game has to offer that is an extremely minor complaint. I cannot recommend this game enough. I hope we see MDickie continue to add more to this game and keep making more 3D titles down the line.'),
