	 ('201044905','76561197969244340','2427430','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'This enhanced edition is fine for those who just want to experience the vanilla game, but have it work on modern systems for the most part.  Call of Pripyat includes the quality of life changes from Clear Sky, as well adding the ability to sleep to skip time which is helpful if you want to skip playing at night.  The main story, and even the side stuff,  is unique and the way the player completes them does effect how the story turns out, increasing replay-ability.  The 3 zones included in the game are interesting, fairly massive compared to the previous games, and fun to explore.  All and all, CoP is my personal favorite out of Shadows of Chernobyl and Clear Sky, and definitely worth checking out.'),
