	 ('11327638','76561198045784396','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Now when I played the first Poker Night, I really liked it.  I got to play with some of my favorite video game characters and such. It was a neat idea, and I managed to grab all the rewards from it.  And then I saw there was a sequel to it.

The main reason why I wanted to buy this game was becaue it had my two favorite robots, Claptrap, and most certainly GLaDOS (best villain btw).  And as always, there was rewards that came with it to put on my TF2 players.  Now the good things about this game; the humor.  I was laughing left and right whether it be the dumb remarks coming from Claptrap, or the really sarcastic humor coming from GLaDOS. Either way, I was surprised on how funny it was, because I wasn''t aiming high. There were a few problems though.

As you would imagine, the lines would get really repetitive. Seeing two characters talk inbetween hands and such is cute at first, but then later on it just gets annoying hearing the same story over and over again. Not to mention they say the same line whenever you go All-In most of the time.  There was one bug I found that if you manage to click one of the "Call" or "Fold" buttons really quickly as soon as your turn pops up, it tends to close the menu and keep me stationary limbo.  It got really annoying considering I was about to win a tournament.  A little tip is if you want to try and get all of the special items really fast, play Omaha.  

Overall, this game lives up to it''s first one, and I do enjoy playing it.  Despite the repetiveness and a game breaking bug I found, it''s still a very enjoyable game with a surprising amount of humor in it.

Pros:
-Really Funny
-Addicting
-Special items to unlock for TF2 or another game
-Customizable table, chips, and cards
-GLaDOS being GLaDOS
-Games can last up to almost an hour

Cons:
-Lines get repeated a lot
-Game Breaking bug that''s easy to get
-Gets awkward sometimes when they just talk in general'),
