	 ('31431698','76561198079428037','3330','20251230',6,0,0,0,10,'My dad got this game when I was little. Why he decided to get it, I don''t know, but I''m glad he did. We played this game religously (he especially played it a lot); it was honestly a part of my childhood gaming experience. For years, I completely forgot this game existed, but just a few days ago, I remembered it. Imagine how happy I was to find out that it was on Steam. 

Starting it up, everything was familiar. The pseudo-Mayincatec music. The cute but dated graphics. The sound effects. The level design. I could recall everything. The gameplay is super simple, but it''s fun and addicting. 

Anyway, maybe it''s the nostalgia talking, but you should totally get it. It''s a fun little time waster.'),
