	 ('8509999','76561197960605360','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,6,'I tried Poker Night 1 and 2, and 1 is the more-fun game. The personalities in 2 are a little annoying, and the gameplay isn''t balanced among the players (Ash won the first 8 pots I played, usually bluffing, but he had the nuts every time he was called down).  This might just be because I''m more familiar with the characters in Poker Night 1, but I didn''t have as much fun with the characters in 2.  Claptrap was annoying, and GLaDOS actually became somewhat annoying quickly just by playing off of Claptrap.  Another weird fault was clicking the + and - buttons in the raise screen was not smooth: I would have to click maybe twice per click that is actually registered.  Clicking up a few hundred dollars feels like button mashing until I get there, while in 1, I just click a few times.  I recommend sticking to Poker Night 1.'),
