	 ('1915172','76561197999674187','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I was psyched for Brock... but his dialouge doesn''t match his facial expressions, and he goes from being cool and relaxed to murderous like he''s bi-polar. Ash is as cocky as ever, and I didn''t even notice the voice was someone elses. Claptrap makes me wish Tycho decided to show back up and take his chair. Sam is so bland they had to bring in Max just to make him seem lively. 

I like the more options in Poker Night 2, but most of them seem pointless except for the option to play Omaha Hold''em. Buying drinks to show "tells", having to have certain combinations to trigger events, and completeting check-lists, just seem to take away from the game your supposed to be playing in front of you.

Poker Night at the inventory seemed more fleshed out and original. Not to mention the best bounty items, and yes, it was a pain to showdown with the certain characters, but I liked that system better then this weird, Poker Night 2 check-list. The first also didn''t have this "Tell" system, everybody had their poker-face on. They also would conversate in any setting, on any table or deck, no need for tedious combinations. Everything had a fair chance of being triggered.'),
