	 ('39066487','76561198046444335','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Got this game on sale for a dollar and it is surprisingly a hard game to put down. That said I will list some pros and cons for those on the fence of buying it.

Cons

- Not a lot of meat to the game, no character customization and altering the tables, cards and over all enviornment is limited to the playable characters respective universes (i.e the ablility to set the game to a borderlands theme because claptrap is an opponent in the game).

- Only 2 different poker games, texas hold ''em and the Omaha variant. If you are looking for a poker game with more play options THIS IS NOT FOR YOU!

- After you unlock all of the bounties from Brock, Ash, Claptrap, and Sam as well as unlock all of the themes for the game, there isn''t really a reason to keep playing as that is all there is to unlock.

Now that we got what it isn''t out of the way lets talk about what it is.

Pros

- Great dialog between the characters, it makes it feel like you are actually playing poker with them and the references to there shows and sometimes the actors and voice actors that potray them make for a great treat if you are familiar with the characters, there actors or voice actors or the visual mediums they come from (films, tv shows and video games). 

- While it doesn''t offer a lot what it does offer is done incredibly well, it is a solid game that is very straight forward as to what it is for better or worse. 

- Changing the themes will change the dialog of certain characters based on the theme which is quite amusing ( Steve will shoot rockets at busted out players if the borderlands theme is chosen for example and there will be interchanable dialog between him and claptrap). 

I give the game a 8/10 and recommend it, it doesn''t offer a lot but it is cheap and a solid game. If you like poker and want  a poker game with personality, this is the game for you.'),
	 ('67958399','76561198069485923','234710','20251230',2,0,0,0,9,'After playing for years I wanted to write a review and this fucking game isn''t even for sale.  Are you serious?  It is one of the best games I''ve ever played, I automatically put it on when non-gaming guests are around.  It blows everyone''s mind with the breadth of dialogue, even I have not heard it all.  I feel very sorry for anyone into poker who can''t buy this, it''s my favorite game.  You can play it laying in bed with a controller with one hand while you massage your girlfriend.  This is real shit put the fucking game back on!'),
	 ('21363139','76561198067527386','386990','20251230',3,0,0,0,10,'Well, I am thinking about what i should give this game, a yes or a no. First thing I hugely dislike about this game is the art of the characters. My grandma used to own dolls like these and put them in het living room. I was ( at 4 years of age) terrified of them. Seeing these characters still give me shivers down my back. 
Secondly, there is a HUGE amount of reading involved and very few choices to be made. So you will be reading huge amounts of text between making choices, that must definatly be something you like.

Pro''s:
+ Nice, relaxing music
+ Best skip options ever ( comes in handy when you want all the achievements)

Con''s:
- Creepy doll art
- Huge amounts of text

'),
	 ('74462339','76561197964232046','1302780','20251230',5,1,0,0,3,'Too easy and too short, and with no replay value it should have been 2 or 3 dollars. At 5 dollars it feels a bit like a ripoff. I don''t mind the simple mechanics, but there are more "towers" (units) here than there are hours of gameplay... and that''s just silly.

Oh, and the interface, graphics, and strategy designs are all a complete ripoff of/tribute to Ironhide Games (Kingdom Rush, Iron Marines). Except for the bad translations, numerous mistakes, and total lack of replay value, you could easily mistake it for an Ironhide game. 

