	 ('174983705','76561198033009372','3009850','20251230',2,1,0,0,0,'It''s cute for an hour, but it begins to really set in that you spent $11.99/$14.99 on the 3D replication of a mobile game released in 2013. The sound effects, graphics, and a majority of the programming follow from the mobile game. It''s some of the worst combat, dialogue, and camera movement I''ve seen in a game.

The combat is so BAD. You spend a majority of the time mashing buttons, only to get locked into an inescapable grapple by your opponent where you will inevitably die. If you get lucky, you''re able to kill (or nearly kill) your opponent, only to be greeted by guards running over to accost you, or an obnoxious alarm signalling you being wanted by the guards. ***THE ALARM SYSTEM IS AWFUL*** I have been sleeping in a cell on the far end of a block, a necessity to recuperate from fights, and have become wanted. There were no guards, no prisoners, just me in the bed at the end of a cell block.

The camera is CONSTANTLY getting caught on walls, or facing in directions you don''t want it to. Fighting someone in a cell? You better get used to staring at the ceiling while you blindly listen your way through the fight.

There is NO depth. You do random missions for NPCs that interrupt you with what seems to be randomly timed dialogue screens. "Bring a desk to the hospital by 18:00" Who are you? Why do you want this? What do I get? Ultimately it doesn''t matter. Someone will likely jump-kick you in the head before you make it another thirty feet anyway.'),
