	 ('179895842','76561198030784015','513320','20251230',4,0,0,0,10,'ALICE VR is a VR exclusive puzzle game with a lot of problems.  Of course we''re making Lewis Carroll spin in his grave here, once more less than stellar developers are busy abusing the public domain.  Maybe Disney was right about abolishing it all along.  It might stop things like this happening, but probably not. 

On the upside, the game does feature customisable controls and resolution, so at least some of the basic, minimum requirements have been met.  Unfortunately there''s a number of other technical defects and shortcomings which contribute to the game being difficult to recommend to gamers.

From my experience with the game, it''s somewhat bug riddled and has design/implementation/stability problems that will render this unplayable for many gamers.  The game doesn''t work well with, well, most VR headsets and it''s an unpolished, bug riddled mess, with black screens, crashes, and stuff, well, just not working.  It''s not really in a fit state to be sold on Steam.

This seems to have been made a VR exclusive to prevent any comparison with non-VR 3D games, a comparison that this game would fail very badly at.  Developers must learn that while VR is great, if the only thing that makes the game great is the VR, then the game isn''t great at all.

These technical defects push this game below acceptable standards for any modern PC game.

ALICE VR didn''t appeal much to the people who own a copy of the game, either.  It has achievements, and they show us a very clear picture that the game didn''t really capture any interest from gamers.  The most commonly and easily attained achievement is "Down the rabbit hole", for starting the game, trivial to get, but less than 16 percent of players bothered to get that far before uninstalling the game.  Hardly a success story, even the people who own this game weren''t interested in it.

So, should you buy this game?  Is this one of the best of the 100,000+ games on Steam?

ALICE VR has the laughable price of around $10 USD, it''s not worth it given the defects and shortcomings with the product, especially considering the sheer number of completely free, much higher quality games on Steam.

For comparison, the $10 asking price for this game could get you games like "Mirror''s Edge", "Final Fantasy XIV Online" or "Assassin''s Creed: Odyssey".  Quality, professionally made games like those are frequently on sale cheaper than this.
'),
