	 ('40121783','76561198004196079','452410','20251230',2,0,0,0,10,'Each level of Damsel is like going through a playground, except that playground is filled to the brim with; vampires, deadly obstacles, hostages and collectables. The main replayability of Damsel comes from each level giving the player a plethora of options for how they want to play. There is something extremely satisfying about optimizing each movement in a level to try and achieve the highest score, which in my opinion is the greatest strength to Damsel as a whole. 

Damsel controls may seem clunky at first, but after a couple of levels controlling Damsel is like second nature. Each move in Damsel''s arsenal serves a purpose that allows the player to play how they want to play, without limiting them to one dominant strategy.  

Along with strong gameplay, Damsel offers an excellent synth-wave inspired soundtrack that gives the player a perfect background track while they slip, slide and shoot through the levels. The awesome comic book inspired look of the game also helps create a greate atmosphere, that gives some hints into what sort of world Damsel lives. Along with amazing background art, each character in Damsel has unique design and really breathes life into each enemy that inhabits the levels.

If you''re looking for a TL,DR here are my pro''s and cons.
Pros:
- Strong game-play
- Smooth controls 
- Strong replayability (especially with Arcade mode)
- Awesome Art
- Bangin'' soundtrack
- Motivated developers that are pushing very frequent updates out using community feedback

Cons:
- Early access, so still some bugs to iron out
- Not much in the way of a story'),
