	 ('8533708','76561197970844648','234710','20251230',6,0,0,0,10,'Poker Night 2 is a game you want to play if you feel like playing some cards and relaxing a bit. The comments of the NPC''s become a bit repetative at times but they are funny and that goes a long way. The action itself is a bit slow paced, mainly because the game takes some time to present you with the NPC''s dialogues in between hands. You can however skip to the next hand if it is your turn. The NPC''s poker AI isn''t all that bad, they can surprise you with some bold and unexpected moves but after a few hours of play you will start to see a pattern. They will occasionally break the pattern though, which makes it exciting. You can collect throphy''s and themes for the poker room which is pretty straight forward but fun nonetheless.

If you judge this game for what it is (a cool way to play cards and have a laugh) and not for what it isn''t (a poker tournament simulator) then you will have a lot of fun playing it.

I would give it 7.5 out of 10.'),
	 ('175357379','76561198219824337','3009850','20251230',4,0,0,0,0,'Honestly wanted to like this product but this Matdickie game didnt hit for me. For starters when you first play the game you cant even go into the editors portion or the fight mode(something that''s in every Matdickie game once you purchase the product) until you beat the game. Now you could argue that this is a pointless statement & I''d agree if this wasnt something that was implemented in previous games. Another thing is the controller config doesnt save so you have to do everything all over again once you boot the game up which kind of sucks if you''re a controller person & the keyboard configs being the arrow keys instead of WASD. As for the story narrative it''s okay, the missions are kind of bland compared to the 2d one which feels more impactful considering most of the missions consist of "deliver this product to ____ by ____" or "stay away from _____ for _____"  not to mention the alarm sounding for the stupidest stuff a random cop came in & bodyslammed me and broke the bed which led me in court(won the case btw) but it wasnt necessary compared to you trying to escape or somebody died by your hand. I may get the game again in the near future if it goes on sale but for right now this game wasnt  it. Overall this product was a big stepdown from the original and just feels rushed & not passsionated compared to the 2d version 5.3/10'),
