	 ('103570285','76561198190029750','584640','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'A charming short game that has fun, fast paced gameplay, well-made pixel art and OST, a cute story and exciting challenges, but a terrible endless mode.
The gameplay is pretty simple. you avoid/destroy objects in your way to reach the end of the level, you''ll find more weapons and accessories to help you avoid the obstacles as you progress. The game is pretty RNG dependant in nature, so sometimes you''ll find yourself in situations that are barely manageable, but that doesn''t matter that much, if you die you''ll not lose significant progress and you''ll respawn pretty quickly, that keeps the gameplay fast paced and dynamic. There''s also the eventual boss, while some of them suffer some problems regarding attack patterns and janky hitboxes, they''re fun overall.
The story is enjoyable and fits the game very well, it being more on the wacky side of things. All the characters are likeable and have little personality traits that differ from one another, there''s also a lot of comedy in this game and, while this is completely subjective, I had a blast with it, the game was surprisingly fun story-wise.
The worst aspect of this game is definitely the endless mode, as I said before, this game is heavily dependant of RNG, and this really doesn''t translate well from the fast-paced story mode to the long, boring ordeal that is the endless mode. Story levels are around 15-20 seconds long if I remember correctly, so you''ll die a lot but you won''t lose that much progress, differently from the endless mode, your objective is to survive 120 seconds to get the respective achievements in each world. The amount of praying you have to do to the RNG Gods is insane, this isn''t even a ''git gud'' moment, you''ll really find yourself unable to avoid your death in multiple points in your runs due to enemy placement, those might cost you some seconds or some minutes of a run, and as those pile up, the more frustrated you''ll get. You don''t even have any significant power-ups to help you, all of them are made with the story mode in mind, lasting around 5 seconds each, and while this is a lot to a 20 second level, it''s nothing in an endless mode.
That aside, I think this is a really fun game that is worth getting, just ignore the existence of endless mode or prepare yourself mentally to it.'),
	 ('16516720','76561198003269414','234710','20251230',10,0,0,0,1,'Disappointing sequel to the first game.  The first Poker NIght in the inventory had far more options like adjusting the AI''s chat and skipping chat altogether.  The first game also had far far better playing partners in terms of characters and humor.  I didn''t know who Tycho or Max was but  learned to like them.  In this one, even the characters I knew were annoying, with bad writing and bad interations with both the player and other AI.  Characters insulting you when you play a card is not funny, it is annoying because we know the play better than the AI and you cannot skip it.  The only reason to get this game is to unlock the extras in TF2 and other games.  Other than that stick wtih the first installment of the game, they put sooooo much more into that game and took so much away from this one, it seems like they didn''t even care about this game at all, it has 1/10th the effort and LESS customization options for chat, inexcusable.  I expect more from Telltale.'),
