	 ('124701697','76561198025100417','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'OVERALL RATING: MIXED

The production values are great and the poker gameplay is simple yet satisfying. But the loss of basic Quality of Life features from the first game, like the ability to change dialogue frequency, and most importantly adjust game difficulty, are major steps backwards. And Claptrap''s strong presence in the game definitely drags it down. He''s an obnoxious character but not in a funny way. Funny moments involving him are always carried by the other characters. If you can tolerate him, you''ll have fun.

I would recommend getting the first game if you can and play that until you unlock everything, and then only giving this one a try if you enjoyed it enough to want more. Even then, your mileage may vary.

3/5'),
