	 ('135189992','76561199440539761','3330','20251230',1,0,0,0,8,'Yeah this game is classic with playthrough better than most mobile marble games , I still prefer Luxor than it cause :
1. The power system is more manageable ; Luxor have system third color shoot gives the power up but Zuma you have to find power up and destroy it to get and with time . So you have good way to get power up just by hitting 3 combo and you choose the power by hitting specific color part3 but Zuma power is randomized maybe in place you cant get or maybe its above you but you dont have right color to destroy the power and its type is randomized for example you want to save yourself with power knock Marbles back because its very close to the gap but you see worst power possible in this occation SLOW and lose the round .
2. Luxor have more freedom to shoot because you have full line to move but Zuma you stick with one place and circle around , with half levels you go you see they are blocked a lot and sometimes completely blocked like last level .
3. Zuma have a random chosen color to shoot even when its close to the gap which is very frustrating and here Luxor saves the day with special role : when a marble get close to the gap the shooter colors turns from random to closest two colors to the gap so you could fight a little bit the line , and here when I play Zuma in this situation I say that its over but in Luxor my popular playtime in hard levels is fighting the marble until I win because these things and one above .
4. I noticed that when Marble is close to the gap : Zuma has only slightly change of speed , Luxor speed get slower but a lot and very noticeable between it and Zuma .
5. In Luxor you have specific bugs to counter which make your win just surviving the waves and give breath everytime you finish a level , Zuma is a noticeable pressure pattern with looots of stress with time ; the level has limitless quantity until you fill the green line by getting specific score , its kinda ok in beginning but believe me that it will turn into ball of stress after the third temple in adventure mode so you have to cambo or hit as much coins as you can to finish the line before it is over , and here what do I hate this game cause the negative thing I told up there will turn this race into lucky eagle eye and quick reaction master level .
6. Last is that you gain lives in Zuma by hitting specific point , Luxor have more advance way : when you hit five marbles or more you get life coin or when you finish the game and there is a big space between marbles and the gap (later they will calculate the space and drop life coins) , and collecting 30 of them get a life , its for me more sufficient to get life .
But even this negative parts (you know its the first Marble Shooter) but it makes its own play style and difficulty because you have to concentrate with points you get because its your own key to victory and use your power efficiently because you wont get then frequently and pause from time to time and have some breathing moments cause you wont get a lot in this game and of course use your lives in your darkest times.
If you like Zuma I recommend you to check Luxor (Ive played 1 and play 3 right now) its cool Marble shooter game and have fun with this one because it doesnt get its fame from nothing .'),
	 ('16684865','76561198085791733','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,7,'Well, that is a poker game. Where you play poker with characters you know(Claptrap, Glados) and this other guys that you don''t know(Sam, Ash and this other guy). But if you need a poker game, I think this is more then enough.'),
	 ('25862209','76561198112866114','279480','20251230',8,2,0,0,8,'Abalone is a board game app done by a company called Bulky pix which doesn''t seem to exist anymore as I could find no web page and the developers never respond to any customer’s complaints about Steam achievements not working. The game is really awful. It has a terrible tutorial which tries to teach you how to play the game while quoting some random quotes from Sun Tzu as if it''s some sort of profound sensei.

4-5 million people have played the game Abalone throughout their lifetime and for those people this version is hardly to be considered fun as it has no proper match making ability. Hence a novice will probably be pitted up against a world champion in no time. The ai in the single player is perfect and never makes a mistake. Some people have made a statement that violent video games make people violent. I don''t believe that. I personally believe that BADLY MADE/UNFAIR GAMES make people violent and there are a few of those that I have banned myself from playing. This is soon to be one of them. The game is so unfair that I often start shouting ''FRUIT'' at the top of my lungs and yodelling threats that I’m about to get a sledgehammer so I can turn their marbles to gelatine.

The board game has often been criticised that it’s possible to make a game go on forever by simply taking a defensive position and maintaining that. This version prevents that from happening as you’re often dictated that you need to win the game in so many moves etc.

Because of non-working Steam achievements, deaf eared developers, bad match making and completely unfair ai, this game gets a solid thumbs down as I often found myself losing more than my marbles every time I played it...

Below is an example of me playing one of the advanced levels called ‘war stage 3’, originally I was going to give someone 5 steam games for simply showing me the solution to it, but somehow I magically found a bug and was able to win by setting out only one of my opponents marbles though in reality I was supposed to set out two. After that I begin to look at ‘War stage 4’ and after getting frustrated with it after a couple of seconds I now hold out the 5 Steam game reward to the person who can show me the solution to this puzzle. It should be enough of a sample for you to work out if this is the game for you. Thanks for reading…

https://youtu.be/LC_5mC8TKDo'),
