	 ('8296684','76561198059794489','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'I loved the first Poker Night, the characters were intersting and very funny, the items were easy to get, and even after you get the items, it was still fairly fun to play. This one on the other hand, is [u]almost[/u] the complete opposite of Poker Night 1. In Poker Night 2 (or ALT+F4 Night 2), the characters are boring, the A.I. is borderline retarded (Example, In the first round, Ash and Brock went all in and they both busted out), the dialouge gets VERY repetitive, there''s no more difficulty or dialouge sliders, the items are a damn chore to unlock with the new "Bounty" system, which forces you to do damn near impossible tasks just get an item, and even the unlockable items aren''t that great. The characters in this game are so unfunny it gives me a headache just thinking about it, Ash is an unlikable dick, Claptrap is annoying (as always), Brock is very rarely funny, Sam is alright, and they butchered GlaDoS''s likable personality. Although I will say this, they did improve the gameplay in some aspects that are helpful if players aren''t too familiar with it, oh, and they added the new Omaha gamemode. The only likable qualities about this game are the Sam & Max and the improved gameplay. In my opinion, You''re way better off playing the first Poker Night.'),
	 ('1484854','76561197993678527','234710','20251230',0,1,0,0,9,'★★☆☆☆ Okay!

[h1]Card Video Game[/h1]

A great sequel. If you didn''t play the first, but can get into video poker and video game cultural references, it''s a decent buy. I''d buy this over the first one if you only get one. It''s a great line-up of characters and is just frustrating enough to keep you wanting revenge rather than quitting.

