	 ('35746133','76561198117518884','234710','20251230',9,0,0,0,0,'The only reasons to buy this game as opposed to "Pokernight at the inventory" are A. You might want the tf2 items from it more. or B. You like the characters more. These are both valid reasons. But I reccommend skipping this one. I may just personally have bad luck, But I can''t hardly win a hand. And also the bots seem more annoyingly smart.

On top of that, GLaDOS is annoying, Popping in for nothing, insulting in less comedic ways then ANYONE in the first game. She just comes across as being mean for the sake of it, which is partially her character I guess but it''s worse then losing a hand. 

The pause menu interface is annoying. You have to click and wait for a long transition to basically just happen, It takes to long, the noise gets an ear bleeding sort of grating, and Then it takes a second for the rest of the menu to load. 

Getting back to the items: You have to win three random (The game says this, don''t get twisted becaouse THEY used the word.) challenges, as opposed to the first game where a character just brought the prize appripoe of nothing. This forces the player to do stupid BS to try and get one item for another game, where as in the first it was a waiting game.

The 20,000.00 Deal ins of the games can make the games last way longer then they should, thus things are less enjoyable because it goes from a quick game to slogging to the end. 

So, The bots seem a bit tougher, which can be either good or bad depending who you are, It seems, in my case, to be balanced against me, most of the characters in this are actually ruder then the first, the items are stupid harder to get, AND The games get genuinely tedious the more you have to play. This game sucks even compared to it''s predesessor.'),
