	 ('108539864','76561198109578510','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'Childhood game, very nostalgic to play it again in 2022, also it''s fun and worth buying, 0.99€ on sale it''s more than worth'),
	 ('117991102','76561198115451561','584640','20251230',19,2,0,0,2,'The gameplay is intense and enjoyable at times. Some bosses were excellent and the story is funny.
But there are some things that I hated with passion.

The UI feels like it was purposefully made as unintuitive as possible. It displays controller prompts even when no controller is connected. You can''t navigate ui with a keyboard (Yes, even something as simple as pressing Esc to go back). The big "right" arrow without any text actually skips the cutscene instead of advancing it. And for no reason... everything is wobbly...

The gameplay felt unfairly hard almost all the time. I feel like hitboxes should be 50% smaller. You can barely touch something and you die. Sometimes things that shouldn''t kill you when you touch them still kill you. Like why can''t you walk on tree stumps? They are flat and they are just... stumps. Or you can cut a stump with a knife and you see that it''s destroyed but it still kills you at the same time... How come?

Overall an incredibly frustraing experience and I don''t recommend this game.'),
