	 ('46761423','76561198011544317','500670','20251230',0,0,0,0,3,'It''s Doom if it was made by the same guys who made Hotline Miami.

But it''s way much more than that. To anyone that''s familiar with twin stick style Shmups way back in the ''90s like Total Carnage or Smash TV, this game puts you into the role of a PO''d space marine chick who''s heading to the planet Eff You - it''s a real planet no joke - for the sole purpose of slaughtering everything in sight.

Let''s get things straight right from the word go. Everything dies in one shot. And by that, I mean ABSOLUTELY EVERYTHING from common mooks you see surging towards you to the  bosses.

BUT. And this is the big BUT. Remember when I said everything dies in one hit?

Well.

So do you. But that doesn''t mean you should take that on the chin, not while you''re still able to crack off shots all while beatin'' feet all over the place and I do hope you remember the one lesson from Hotline Miami, because while recklessness is rewarded, but remember one thing. The risk of you getting nailed by a stray shot from your enemies or environmental hazard climbs higher and higher still, so you need to be aware of your surroundings at all times. So despite this, you have to temper your recklessness and raw fury (see what I did there?) with a battle plan and exit strategy, because this gets intense right from the word go. Your keys to victory depends on your reflexes which has to be razor sharp and you need to have more precision than an electron microscope and more importantly, get ready to start racking up a body count that''s gonna slather the arena in blood, guts and bullet shell casings.

Speaking of your weapons, you have 10 shots for your machine gun and the method of reloading said weapon is to fire your shotgun. Yeah. Trust me, it makes loads of sense if you don''t think about it.

So. You in the mood for an intense arena shooter that has full on aggressive shoot-em-up action, complete with a soundtrack that''s just as angry as you are? Well whaddaya doing standing around like a big dope? You need an invitation? Grab this up and get to playing already!'),
