	 ('21201969','76561198161027732','375460','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'To be fair, I enjoyed this game when I first started playing it. It looked pretty cute, nothing groundbreaking, but better than average mobile game style graphics that suggested some care and consideration had gone into it. The translation isn''t as bad as others have said - yes the English is a bit wrong in places but hardly enough to trip you up. The only problem I had with the game at first was that the economic mechanics weren''t great. When the price of one commodity went up, they all went up, and usually by similar amounts, so the trading side of the game lacked a bit of depth and nuance. And since that''s the sole focus of the game, it does make it feel a bit basic.

However, what really broke this game for me was the save function not working or being unreliable. After playing for an hour, saving fairly regularly in the first save slot and then saving and quitting, I found that the game had only saved my progress sporadically. So when I went back to it, I had essentially lost about 20 minutes of progress. I played for a while longer, saving and quitting and reloading to see if there was any fix or if it was a one time glitch, but no. This game will not let you save. That''s the bottom line. And for a relatively shallow game to have so major a glitch, is a deal breaker for me. I only paid 33p for it, so I''ll let it run to get the cards, but otherwise, it''s not worth your time.'),
