	 ('195689336','76561198120631091','2427430','20251230',4,0,0,0,10,'Note: CoP is a great game. Apparently this version includes a copy of the original game, in case you cannot buy the original.
Owners of the original got this for free.
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/id/Kryllical/recommended/41700?snr=1_5_9__402]My original Call of Prypiat review.[/url]
I decided to play the entire enhanced trilogy because these reviews suck, and I wanted to see what has been done to some of my favorite games.

SoC had bugs, but ran fine and wasn''t a bad way to play. I 100%''d it, but I''d still just mod it. CS was a failure of a remaster. I don''t recommend either of them over the originals.
So what about CoP?
Well first off, CoP never had any real issues to begin with. It''s always been the most stable and least buggy of the trilogy.
So when I played through this enhanced edition, it just felt like I had a visual mod on, and a reshade that was kinda blurry.

What''s so enhanced about this? Well not much.
-There is a light graphical upgrade. New shaders, lighting effects, etc. Yes some mods look better than this, but overall it does look better than the original. However there''s this god awful blur that''s been added to the game. It''s not TAA, and I have no idea how to turn it off. Various methods have been discussed by the community, but everyone seems very mixed on their effectiveness. I went ahead and just updated the FSR dll and dealt with it. That''s modern gaming for you.
-Cutscenes are now in HD and clearer than ever. Unfortunately this is via the power of AI upscaling, which means artifacting and interpolation. I suppose it could be worse.
-Combat music toggled on for some reason, even though in the original game it''s off by default.
-Yes there''s censorship, and you already know why. The only thing I noticed was the lion art being removed. Rest in peace you little shit, I''ll miss getting jump scared by you at the school staircase. (Edit: Apparently it''s in Stalker 2 though. What is this nonsense?) 
-Locations have been renamed to their Ukrainian spellings, and the currency was changed. It was kinda jarring.
-No more grenade throw charge. M1 immediately throws at full power, and M2 at low power. Non-issue imo.
-Text now has a highlight because you can navigate conversations with W and S if you don''t feel like using the mouse.
-I might be crazy, but it feels like there''s either more wandering NPC/mutant spawns or a faster respawn rate in an effort to make the game feel more "alive". 
-fov slider

Overall, this one''s fine. It''s the best out of the trilogy, but I can''t tell if that''s because CoP is the most refined of the original trilogy in general. New players will have no issues playing this version of the game. It''s really not that far from just playing the original game with a few mods.

Wait they removed ''Live to forget'' by FireLake from the end credits. You couldn''t get the track from the band that''s in the original trilogy, AND STALKER 2? Oh is it because it was in Russian? What about the ENGLISH VERSION OF THE SONG? This might seem extreme, but that changed my opinion of this version a lot. The fact that you couldn''t make this simple change, and instead replay the epilogue track is just flat out lazy. So thumbs down it is. Get your shit together GSC.'),
	 ('14603949','76561198080016587','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,8,'Best cast of characters to appear in any game ever! 10/10'),
	 ('25735039','76561197996704924','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,1,'It''s nice to pass the time with a bit of Poker.

If you''re looking for reasons to buy: the characters and/or poker itself.

If you''re looking for reasons NOT to buy: dialogue gets VERY repetitive after the first few tournaments, and lack of variety. Only two modes you can play are Texas Hold ''Em and Omaha (you play 2 out of the 4 cards in your hand).

I recommend because I believe that everyone should [at least] have one non-hardcore, non-shooting, non-expensive game that only exists to pass the time. No online players to troll you, no open worlds to load and get lost in, no solid objective to meet or complete, and have the guilty pleasure of gambling, of course.

And if you can''t (or won''t) see yourself playing this particular game, then find games similar to this one. Cheap, time killing, light on storage, not covered in bullets and blood.'),
