	 ('86359454','76561198123161233','244070','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'Love this game.   It feels like a board game with fully animated WWI planes executing maneuvers over a battlefield complete with AA, trenches, airfields and depots.  You can fly as French, Americans, British or Germans.  You have a squad of four pilots, but missions may employ one, two, or four.  There are bombing missions, recon missions, strafing missions....but you are always controlling your squad of fighters.  Different planes become available at the appropriate period in time.  Missions are linked together in campaigns (Somme, Marne, Arras, etc.) progressing to the end of the war.  It took no time to become familiar with game mechanics, but I have much knowledge of WWI flying tactics and planes.  If you play the Wings of Glory miniatures game, this digital game feels like a solitaire, very fun version of WoG.  I have a new Legion laptop with Windows 10 and find this game trouble free.  (Caveat: in my first two hours of play, the game would "drop off" but when I restarted it, it picked up right where I left.  For some reason, there have been no problems since!)  I am enjoying the unique features of various planes and pilots, and like the visuals of historical plane markings.  What a thrill to deploy the Flying Circus DR1s, or Rickenbacker and Luke.  I bought this on sale for $1.24 and it is worth much more to me.  I can pick it up and play a few missions whenever I have a few minutes, but also can get drawn in to playing the whole war--which I can do in two hours .  Fun, beer and pretzels game.'),
