	 ('195268338','76561199099497174','2427430','20251230',4,0,0,0,6,'My Review
The game works well. The issue we have here is the blur it feels like it was meant to be played on an AMD card. I played with the settings trying to remove the blur, and sadly, it’s still there. The only option is FSR. You can disable it, but it makes the game look sh*t.

Other than that, I’ve played it for 40 minutes, but there is one problem: when you get close to NPCs, it’s like you can’t get too close to them. Plus, if they’re attacking someone and you’re inside a room with them right and he is standing right in front of the door, you can’t get out. Either you kill the guy, wait until he moves, or throw a grenade so he reacts to it.

Other than that, I’ve collected some artifacts, and yeah, it’s an alright game but I think they need to fix the blur issue and the NPCs.

Would I recommend it? Not really. It’s the same game, so I don’t see the difference. Just stick with the old one'),
	 ('200240238','76561198798893891','3009850','20251230',6,3,0,0,3,'Got a woman pregnant from kissing her. 10/10 on realism, MDickie always knows what his games need.
