    [/tr]
[/table]

[b]Lethal Tempting Girls[/b] is a first person shooter featuring attractive lady partners (and adversaries). This game is [b]clearly[/b] "Early Access".

[h1]Gameplay[/h1]
The main goal of the game is to collect currency, obtained by completing (randomized) missions. Missions can range from defeating bosses to saving hostages. Currency can be used to purchase, upgrade and regenerate (female) companions. As your companions level up, you unlock new poses (viewable from the "lobby area"). You can also unlock new lobby areas, but they are exorbitantly pricey. Each lobby has a variety of areas to pose characters, from beds to chains.

Yes, chains because [i]BDSM is cool[/i]

You can also remove your companions'' clothing, which also represents the number of hit points your lady friends have. You are able to bring any (one) lady you desire on a missions, which all play out the same. You shoot a bunch of baddies, and interact with "hostages" if they are in the area. There are only a handful of stages, and you don''t earn much for doing them. Expect to play the same missions again and again, and breaking even (to repair your lady troops).

[h1]Story[/h1]
You''re [i]some dude[/i] stuck in a virtual reality. In it, a series of deadly machines and "virtual idols" have gone rampant. Virtual idols are powerful foes, but (thankfully) you have your own idols ready to fight for you.

[h1]Visuals[/h1]
The interface is clean and minimalistic. If you don''t know what does what, you won''t break anything if you click on random icons. Beyond that, I don''t have much else to say. The in-game assets [i]feel like[/i] asset flips, but I can''t vouch for my feelings. In any case, the ladies look fine, and so do the stages. The enemies seem a bit out of place (stylistically speaking).

[b]- The Goods -[/b]
The sexiest thing you''ll see is lingerie and light BDSM. As ladies take damage, their clothing tears away, eventually leaving no more than their underwear. Expect. . . almost nudity.

[h1]Verdict[/h1]
This game is [i]bad[/i], but in an early stage of development. I enjoyed the game, and I want to see it become something bigger. With that in mind, I suggest adding this game to your "Wishlist", and giving it a try after a few solid updates. If you want to support development, buy and discuss it. That''s what I did.

[b]- Words for the Dev''s -[/b]
I like the idea behind the game, but it lacks in many departments. There''s no character development, no story, little variety, and too much grinding. I would have liked to have seen [i]at least[/i] (uncensored) nudity, and one or more "adult" animations. For how much grind we (as players) are expected to do, there isn''t much encouraging us to do. If you are interested in chatting, feel free to [i]hit me up.[/i]

[h1]Support the Wombat[/h1]
If you enjoy my reviews, please follow my Curator page. I live and die on your thumbs (up) and follows.

https://store.steampowered.com/curator/36272124-Wombat-Trap/'),
