	 ('174687890','76561197993295672','3009850','20251230',21,0,0,0,10,'Just too good of an opportunity to miss...

I''ve been a fan of MDickie''s games for a while now, and this one really delivers. This chaos and nonsense you get here simply does not exist in other games. I just completed my first run, and had an awesome time.

My character got sentenced to 20 days for contributing to climate change. Even though I tried my best to stay out of trouble, trouble often came looking for me. The first humdinger of nonsense happened when someone fired of a bazooka in the cafeteria when I just wanted a burger. Big Mess. Soon afterwards, I got picked on for crapping my pants. I got arrested for that, and got detention in the bathroom. While in there, someone told me to deliver toilet paper to someone in another cell block. I brought them the TP, and got told they were going to beat me to hell with it. So I ran into the library when a big fire started, and the guards asked me to put it out. I picked up a squirt gun in the next room, and then got told by the guard to put it back where I found it. So I ignored him, and tried to squirt the fire. I hit the guard instead. Got arrested again and got 3 days added to my sentence for assault. When I went back to my cell for the night, somehow someone rode a horse into the cell block, and the horse did nothing but panic.

And that was my first day...

Sure the game is a bit janky and clumsy at times, but it sort of adds to the hilarity. You''ll never get totally used to it, but it can create moments on it''s own.

A few words of advice. push "c" to activate your controller on the main screen if you are using one. You have to do this every time you load the game up. Second piece of advice is to play the game for a while to meet all the NPCs. This will unlock them for editing. To unlock editing and the custom fight thing, complete your first sentence. After that, that''s were the fun really begins.

You can now use the powerful editor to create the craziest inmates, cops, and civilians you can come up with. This is great fun. Learn to use the backup and save functions. It also helps to make your own manual back ups. Use the powerful clone function to create fighting styles and moves sets you enjoy the most. You don''t need to create a move set for each character. Just copy them.

Take your time, and you''ll have the prison and town of your dreams. A very twisted dream, but still.

Tell your friends to get this, or buy it for them. You will get your money''s worth. No other game creates stories on the fly quite like this one. There''s a learning curve since there is not tutorial, but you can read books to discover strategies. Overall, though, this is the summer of love video game style. Don''t miss out.'),
