	 ('12531942','76561198024120630','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'To me, poker is a social activity. The fun of exploring your competitors behaviour for tells, call their bluffs and reach over the table to gleefully gather your winnings, is a thrill that can''t be fully replicated in a game against AIs.

But damn it if Telltale haven''t made the most of it.

As a pure Texas Hold-Em simulator, Poker Night 2 does its job about as well as you''d expect. The rules haven''t really changed since that last time you went to Las Vegas and lost all your money. The novelty is that this particular iteration takes place at a "behind the scenes" club where fictional characters meet up after hours. Your competitors are Brock Samson, Sam and Max, Ash Williams and the CL4P-TP General Purpose Robot (a.k.a. Claptrap) - with GLaDOS from Portal acting as the referee.

To fully enjoy the game, it''s best if you know who these characters are - but their banter is still entertaining if you don''t. I myself had no previous experience with The Venture Bros. but still found Brock to be an entertaining competitor. It''s a fun little gimmic, and my personal relationship with these characters kept the repeating conversations from going stale too quickly (but fair warning, they WILL do so eventually). The abillity to buy the players a round of drinks, and their intoxication making them easier to read, makes for a fun dynamic - which is good, because at the end of the day.... C''mon.... It''s Texas Hold-Em: Unless you have real passion for cardgames, you''ll get bored after a tournament or two.

And that''s where the games'' main selling-point is revealed; By winning prizes in Poker Night 2, you unlock exclusive items in Team Fortress 2 and Borderlands 2. I personally have never played TF2, but bought this game solely due to the Borderlands 2 items (particularely the Mechromancer Sam-head and Zer0 GLaDOS outfit). And you may ask, was it worth it? Well... Yes. Unlocking the items don''t take THAT long, but it might SEEM longer if you get no joy from Poker or the characters. The game looks nice, the voiceactors do a great job and the gameplay is solid. Just know what you''re going into.

It should be said, though, that when I DID unlock the items for Borderlands 2, the game had trouble activating them. It looks like an error on Gearboxs'' end, since the files you download from Poker Night ARE placed in your Borderlands directory. Just be aware that there is a CHANCE that one of the games'' big selling-points might not work at the end of the day.

And ultimately, isn''t that fitting? After all, Poker is all about chance and the luck of the hand you''re dealt.'),
