	 ('43370456','76561197996638023','234710','20251230',21,1,0,0,9,'Most people purchased this game for the items, I purchased it for the Poker and the banter.

I have also played this game a ridiculous amount of time offline, which Steam doesn''t record. If it did, it would be in my top 5 most playtime games in my 250+ game-strong library, with at least 4 times the amount that Steam has actually recorded.

The dialogue can get repeatative, and there is a weird bug near the end of a round, that if you skip too late, Glados will say her lines twice.

The one and only thing that I can''t stand in this game is Claptrap. I make it my personal mission to knock him out as early as possible, which is not always easy.

The only achievement I have left, is obtaining $1 million total bank balance ingame. Considering you can gain $80,000 from winning a tournament, it sounds easily achieveable. But this is the ultimate facade of gambling. I have now been playing this since release, on and off for years and years, with the same save file, only restarting once in late 2013, and I have still yet to even make it halfway to 1 million. I think I have around 400k balance or thereabouts, which in itself is a recovery from a negative balance of almost minus 2 million. The achievement isn''t based around your total earnings, it is based around the balance itself, which makes it infinitely more complicated.

I recommend this for any fans of Poker, as it adds a level of personality to an otherwise cold and calculated game.'),
