	 ('38830724','76561198057766071','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'For those that already know how to play No Limit Holdem and No Limit Omaha,  this game is boring from an actual poker point of view.  Your computer oppenents are terrible and easy to exploit.  Also, there are multiple factual errors in the dialog.  For example, the action is always described as "[player] steals the pot" if the flop is not seen, even if there was a three or four bet followed by all fold in the pre-flop.

If you are a novice and you want to learn how to play poker for real, get a good poker strategy book and you will learn to wipe the floor with these opponents.  Unfortunately, there is no skill progression from the game''s point of view.  If you get to the point where you win every single tournament, you are done here.  That should not take more than a few hours.

On the other hand, if you just want pure entertainment and don''t really care about the fine points of poker, this game is good for maybe two hours or so of entertainment.

For $0.99, I totally recommend it.  If it is $4.99, only get it if you would be happy with that amount of play time.

YMMV

'),
