	 ('138457507','76561198073839130','234710','20251230',3,0,0,0,9,'This is a decent poker game that is made better by the interactions of the characters that are in it. Also you can earn some cool TF2 items by playing which is a bonus.'),
	 ('1422215','76561197993109243','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Much better than the first one. To be honest, I really didn''t care for the characters the first time around, but in Poker Night 2, I know everyone except Sam & Max, so it''s a lot more fun.

The characters seem to behave more like people, with tells and behaviors unique to each of them. I don''t want to spoil it, but one of them has a pretty clear behavior when he bluffs (for example).

The addition of Omaha rules to the game also is cool. For some reason I do much better at Hold ''em, but I think that''s pretty much a head game I play with myself.

At any rate, I give this game a solid B. It''s just about the best Poker I''ve ever played against computer opponents, and the banter between them is fun. I wish there was a difficulty option, because I won my first three tournaments in under an hour, and I''m really not a very good poker player. Though I guess there''s an inherent advantage in being able to read opponents that can''t see you.'),
	 ('200270875','76561199058985453','3009850','20251230',10,1,0,0,3,'During my first hour or so of playing this game obama came out of the ground and a cop pissed on him causing obama to tear off the officers arm with a m1911'),
	 ('100716207','76561197970524444','234710','20251230',3,1,0,0,8,'"It''s a mathematical certainty that 80% of you are going to lose tonight. And 100% of you will eventually die. Math is fun, don''t you think?" -GlaDOS

Awesome characters, awesome commentary - quite funny to boot.  The poker mechanics are OK, but just playing the game to earn the achievements is fun and casual.  I usually jump in randomly after a long period of time not playing the game.  If you get tired of the commentary from the NPCs, you can fast forward through hands after you fold.

Too bad TellTale Games went bankrupt.  Hopefully, someone buys them again so they can make Poker Night 2 and add in some TT TWD and GOT characters.'),
