	 ('202226794','76561198065528050','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'The actual dark souls of puzzle games. I have such a love/hate relationship with Zuma Deluxe and I have since I was a young child. I actually remember my first time playing it at my grandmothers house because it was the middle of summer and I had literally nothing better to do. Nothing could have prepared my young mind for how unreasonably difficult this game becomes or how quickly. I promised myself I''d beat this god-forsaken puzzle game someday and I thought it would be a lot sooner in my life. Granted I didn''t consistently sit here playing Zuma Deluxe every day of my life but Here I sit, nearly 28 years old, still yet to beat the final level.

The vauge Aztec theming drives me to bring up a bit of mythology. It was said by the Aztecs that there were multiple suns in the sky, one of which only moved in response to sacrifice, so they sacrificed all the gods to it- all of course but the god of death Xolotl, a dog-headed man who could shapeshift. Nowhere in the game does it imply I am anything but a random marble spitting frog statue, but I too feel like a death god turned into an aquatic salamander attempting to escape the jaws of my brother Quetzalcoatl trying not to die. This Game. Is That Hard.

I nod to you, Zuma Deluxe, for keeping me coming back year after year of my life to finally complete my quest in defying the gods. And I promise you. I''m finally close. May beating this puzzle game from the early 2000s bring my childhood self some semblance of peace. Game On, Old Friend.'),
	 ('19656409','76561198025407577','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'To be honest, I like many others also got this game solely for the TF2 and Borderlands items. I really wasn''t expecting too much when I first started playing, but eventually Poker Night 2 won me over with it''s charm and atmosphere. The gameplay itself is nothing new or special, since games like these are more dependent on luck. But what kept me going, besides the grind for unlockables, were the interactions between the characters.  I even found the different ways the characters busted out to be quite entertaining. For a while.

That''s when things started to dip for me, cause once you clock in enough games, the dialogue variations wear out quickly. And I guess unless you''re a Texas Holdem addict, things overall just get a bit too repetitive. But for it''s price (especially during sale) and the cast of Claptrap, Brock, Ash and Sam, I would recommend Poker Night 2 for a quick time sink during days when you just wanna play some cards.'),
