	 ('1275728','76561197990513926','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'With a new all star cast taking seat Poker Night 2 was quite the fun game of cards whilst listening to some of your favorite character banter at each other. The main appeal of these games is finally seeing characters who wouldn''t normally been seen together finally unleash their personalities upon each other. Although this game has many improvements over the first game with a new challenge system to earn unlocks, table customization and the ability to buy drinks so your opponent will be more obvious with their tells it suffered most from the bugs. Since the launch everyone who''s played complained about the game crashing or even being unplayable requiring people to research themselves to find a fix for their situation. I even experiences some crashes that cause the game to not launch until I set the game to run in Windows 98 compatibility mode. If you''re able to push past the potential bugs the game can be quite enjoyable and be a fun way to blow off a hour playing cards.'),
