	 ('17429040','76561198061712686','386990','20251230',6,1,0,0,9,'A great, well-written story set to some beautifully scenic artwork. The characters and dialogue are engaging and relatable, despite being based on long-dead poets. You''ll even learn a lot about their real-life counterparts (if you so choose)! All in all, would definitely reccomend to anyone who seems interested.

The only things to keep in mind is that the game deals with some very grim and confronting themes (if you couldn''t tell from the title), with the bulk of the story covering Samantha''s depression and her collpasing, choatic state of mind, and that is has a uniquely formal (and third-person) narrative stlyle. I''d also reccomend playing the author''s previous freeware game, [b] [url=ebihime.itch.io/dejection] "Dejection: An Ode" [/url] [/b] before this - it''s not essential to the plot, but it''s a great game in it''s own right.'),
