	 ('74218797','76561199074265686','1302780','20251230',13,0,0,0,10,'Pros:
1) An original tower defense game where you have to elevate your units on different floors to deal with certain situations.
2) Collect up to 16 units as you progress 50 levels and 8 worlds or by earn achievements base on your performance in each level.
3) 45 Zombies with unique and troublesome abilities to bypass your defenses
4) 9 Gadgets you can use to support your units.
5) Upgrades and Badges that can empower your units (So far I have managed to beat the game with little grinding involved)
6) Environmental Hazards that can help zombies to gain advantage like Escalators to prevent repetitive gameplay
7) (Art) Colourful and detailed art designs that you can easily identify both the zombies and units

Cons: (Note the names of the characters were changed to prevent spoilers)
1) Some of the zombies uses cheap abilities to lose your life or mines for example Ghost''s temporary invulnerability and Scientist''s invisibility when they are close to the door can prevent the player for having a chance to kill them to either secure a General Rank or save the mine for later.
2) Low Replayability and Post-Game content such as Endless Mode after beating the story.
3) Achievements can be grindy and may depend on luck whether if the Units feels like using their ability.

Overview: I almost forgot about FireBeast until I browse through my steam recommendations and discover this last week. Gameplay wise, this game with worth the price as the game contains 20 units, 45 zombies, 9 gadgets, 50 levels and more. I had finished the whole game after 7 hours of playing with little grinding involved.'),
