	 ('62420421','76561198055681724','244070','20251230',2,0,0,0,10,'There really is a lot of potential with Sid Meier''s Ace Patrol. It has a lot working for it, but it also has a lot working against it, which unfortunately out way the pros.

For the Pros: 
- The game mechanics and core gameplay are pretty solid, no real complaints there. 
- Aircraft movement is all straight-forward and each manoeuvre is fun to use as they all have their special use. 
- Each Aircraft have their own special characteristics (which they did have historically) which makes them unique to use. - -- How your pilots get promoted through kills and are able to learn new skills and manoeuvres is also pretty neat.

Now for the Cons:
- The game crashes after almost every mission I do. If you click through the end result menus too fast, it will freeze and crash, causing you to have to restart the mission you did. Needless to say it''s really annoying and frankly unforgivable for a game that really shouldn''t be that taxing on your computer, and should be much better optimised than that. Which is weird because it runs smoothly every other time.
- You can tell it''s a rushed mobile port. The graphics are sub par, even for mobile, and the menus are over-sized and boringly simple to cater to touchscreens.
- The aircraft choices are very small for each nation, meaning not a lot of variety.
- You can only have four pilots in your squadron, and a max of four in a mission. Again, most-likely to cater to iOS/Android processing power.
- The animations for aircraft movement are weird and unnatural, which doesn''t make the game very cinematic.
- The sound and the music is very meh, bleh and bland.

Overall. It''s a poorly made and barely-playable mobile port. Which is a shame because it has the potential to be a fantastic game with better animations, UI, graphics, aircraft variety and customisation, and optimisation.'),
