	 ('195318334','76561198911150922','2427430','20251230',14,1,0,0,0,'GSC game world I am beyond disappointed with this product.  This is both the fault of the company this enhanced version was outsourced to, and also you for looking at it (did you even bother opening the game up?) and deciding that it was in an acceptable state to release.  

However my biggest gripe is your community managers saying that the reason why this has negative reviews is because of "Russian review bombing".  Sure, there are those who have done it for political reasons.  But GSC open your damn product and see that people''s complaints are validated!  Saying its just "Russians who are mad" is insulting to me personally as someone who believes in Ukrainian independence and identity.  I just don''t choose to blindly shill a product that disappoints me like I find many of the people who support these new releases do.  I love Stalker, I love these experiences.  But when everyone is having issues with your product and you chop them all up to "theyre just mad Russians" is idiotic and just outright sucks.'),
	 ('202134132','76561198158993897','3563710','20251230',0,0,0,0,3,'Recommended (with reservations)

The game is cool for $3 and offers a decent amount of content for the price, but it’s also full of small annoyances that add up over time.

Main issues I found while playing:

- Buying ingots: Having to pick them up from the ground every time is exhausting. They should go straight into your inventory, and constantly spamming “+3” for dozens of orders a day is rough on the hands.

- Storage: Completely ignored it—it’s too much effort to move items there, and unlocking it with XP instead of money makes no sense.

- Sales area: Never used it. Hard to keep up with requests anyway, no easy way to see what’s inside without guessing, and again, unlocking with XP feels wrong.

- Forging: Once an item finishes, the selection menu should reopen automatically instead of forcing you to wait and re-interact. Also, higher-tier recipes take too many hits—an upgrade to reduce them (but keep at least one) would help.

- Running: Movement feels like the character is tipsy—not a big deal, but odd.

- Ending the day: Don’t instantly end it at 6 p.m.—just stop new customers and let us prepare for the next day.

- Rejection system: Feels pointless and overpriced to use.

Conclusion: It’s fun, but also clunky. Worth a try if you don’t expect a ton of content and can tolerate the rough edges.'),
