	 ('98696872','76561198198655669','874200','20251230',3,0,0,0,4,'The game is a straight forward puzzle platformer that has a few different objectives to make the game less repetitve. There''s definitely a lot of content, 100 levels, however most, if not all levels can be completed within sixty seconds, the only issue is that this game is entirely random, it doesn''t matter what the objective is, if you''re lucky you''ll be able to complete it on your first try, or even fail on the tenth if you''re unfortunate.
 The game isn''t challenging but it wasn''t meant to be. The only problem is the price, if it''s on at least 50% sale, then buy it if you like these sort of games, it takes a few hours to complete. Also, when you complete a level you get a coin, but there''s nothing to spend it on.'),
	 ('195679368','76561198002974207','2427430','20251230',1,1,0,0,1,'There are comparison videos on youtube, which are fine and informative.  Watch the simplest one if you really want to compare remastered and OG.

Also, maybe don''t even look at steam reviews to get an idea of how good a remaster is when it involves an area of the world that is getting more disinformation than any nation in history.  Half the reviews say ''keep politics out of gaming'' and the other half say ''Ukraine totally started this''.  It''s a circle jerk for attention... so I''m joining in!  Who doesn''t like a good....

There are comparison videos on youtube, which are fine and informative.  Watch the simplest one if you really want to compare remastered and OG.

I''ve played Stalker GAMMA for about 1000 hours, and the OG games once through each.  This remaster wasn''t even mentioned in an announcement on the GAMMA discord, so I think you can assume that mods have already done it all.  Yes, could have been better.  It was free for people who already own the game.  Stalker games could use a reMAKE (which again, mods have already mostly done) but a remaster is a bare minimum, so you know, it still exists and doesn''t look as bad, and that has very little to do with the annexation of Crimea.  I hear they got rid of some Russian symbols.  Since I don''t know what those symbols mean, I can''t say if they were seriously offensive or not, or whether perhaps a people who are being shelled just had a knee-jerk reaction to a bunch of Soviet stuff reminding them of the fact that they''ve been conscripted because there''s a war going on that was started by an ex-KGB operative turned President who literally called anyone who didn''t lament the breakup of the Soviet Union as stupid and heartless (which at the very least is, ironically, both a stupid and heartless comment.  Again with the circle... never mind.)

There are comparison videos on youtube, which are fine and informative.  Watch the simplest one if you really want to compare remastered and OG.

This isn''t a game that got more expensive because of its remaster, because the quality of the game has never been in dispute, just its functionality and dated graphics, which seem to be better overall.

There are comparison videos on youtube, which are fine and informative.  Watch the simplest one if you really want to compare remastered and OG.

I wrote this without even playing the game, and nothing changed when I did, because... there are comparison videos on youtube, which are fine and informative.  I watched the simplest one because I really wanted to compare remastered and OG.'),
