	 ('131781478','76561198012216661','1197770','20251230',4,0,0,0,10,'Lilly Knight is something refreshing. Yes, it is a sex game. But the different thing here is that it is clearly made with passion for the project. It is a very linear story about a sex crazed young girl on a quest to close the gates to a demon world. And of course, the only way to close them is by having a lot of sex.

It is a really bad story that even make 70s porn movies look like literary masterpieces. But the studio absolutely owns it, and knew that this game was an attempt to actually create a real game. With real game-play, and a story-line and half-decent graphics. 

Where this game absolutely shines is by hiring Mia Sloane to voice the protagonist. She absolutely is a hidden gem and really put a lot of emotion and fun in her acting of Lilly. 

The game hardly throws a challenge. The sex is fun, but even that is not taken too seriously while avoiding to make it too weird. This is a game, a naughty one at that - but that will make you smile and actually will try to make you play the entire thing through.'),
	 ('34979463','76561198043972532','234710','20251230',5,1,0,0,9,'One of the best games that Telltale made. Has some funny dialogue, well written characters, and most importantly offers you as much choice as every game they made since combined. Also, compared to majority of their "games" - is not a cash grab on overrated franchises, but a cashgrab on franchises that deserved it.

I hope one day they will hire someone to design some gameplay.'),
	 ('48205321','76561198078955765','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'This one is very similar to the first one, and right now this game is not available on steam anymore, so I''m srry if you don''t have this one. The place is the same and the rules are also the same, although instead of betting 10 000 dollars like in the first poker night in this one everyone pays 20 000 dollars. The characters you play with are different. All of them. You play with Brock, Claptrap (from Borderlands), Ashe and Sam (From Sam and Max). Although you still have a chance to see Max and sometimes he talks to you and to everyone in the table. It''s not the same though because Max''s voice actor is different in this poker night. I think Max was funnier in the first poker night, but it''s still cool. Of course you have different rewards for a couple of games. This is very good because as the game is not available the rewars are now a little bit rare. Also in this poker night game you can buy drinks to everyone in the table (except yourself) and the more they drink the more they become stupid and do pretty random plays, giving you some advantage. Also in this poker night your narrator is GladOS from Portal. And let''s say she makes fun of everyone really bad, but as always she preffers to hit on you. You can buy new cards, chips and even new scenarios with game tokens. 
Good luck, because this poker night is twice as harder as the first one.'),
