	 ('199897183','76561197997934524','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,2,'It''s over... it''s finally over, I''m done. This is one of those games that you''ve probably played before if you haven''t played [i]this particular version[/i], the Gameboy Advance version of [i]Lego Island Extreme Stunts[/i] of all things actually had a pretty decent rendition that I used to love and even before [i]Zuma[/i] there was [i]Puzzloop[/i] so [i]Zuma[/i] isn''t particularly [i]unique[/i] but it [i]is[/i] a satisfying, polished, deeply addictive take on this formula.

The gameplay is so simple you can understand it from a single screenshot, balls roll down a track and you have to shoot the same color of sphere to get rid of them. Sounds easy right? [i]Wrong[/i]. I started this a few months ago thinking it''d just be something casual I could do a few rounds of over lunch or to kill a few minutes, but golden age Popcap was working with some of the most powerful crack in the universe because it''s become an obsession. The first seven or so worlds were the breezy, caasual experience I expected, a fun way to watch little sphere''s explode with a satisfying pop, but around World 8 this game becomes the 10th circle of hell. I don''t know if spoilers really count for a game like this but level 9 is [i]not[/i] the final level, there are 12 worlds and once you hit world 8 it goes from a casual little reflex-based puzzle to "You have to understand every mechanic to surivive". You will be strategizing [i]all[/i] the ways to get gap-shots, hit the coin, roll the track back as much as possible because you [i]need[/i] every inch of breathing room you can claw back for yourself. I am [i]convinced[/i] the game deliberately gives you the worst color possible at certain times just so it can push you closer to losing. Getting over the World 8 hump took weeks, 9 through eleven were deceptively breezy, but 12? [i]Brutal[/i]. If you''re going to survive world 12 you [i]will[/i] become a [i]Zuma[/i] expert. When I [i]finally[/i] made it to the final level, which is [i]technically[/i] World 13, I was so relieved because I thought "okay, if I die now at least I''m on the last level" but guess what? If you die on World 13 you have to replay [i]all[/i] of World 12 and that crushed my soul. It would be weeks before I''d see the final stage again and weeks more until I beat it, but it''s finally over... I''m free now. I never have to play [i]Zuma[/i] again... (at least until I inevitably buy the sequel). My nightmare is over.'),
