	 ('41072383','76561198065636613','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'Cutting to the chase, then will get into more detail.
I make notes about stuff and the first note about this game was "this game is actually fun WTF :DDd the dialogues are brilliant". Now.
[b]This is not a poker game.[/b] It is bad as such. Don''t treat it as one, don''t expect it to be one.
You have 4 player characters (+GLADOS, Max and a talking trophy) with really interesting dialogue that I thouroughly enjoyed. Trouble is it gets repetitve fast.
But you should still buy it. [b]It''s a lot of fun[/b] while it lasts. If you like to go for 100% achievements - don''t do it.
You will ruin your great first hour or two that you had.

The trouble with the dialogue composition is you will get new phrases you have never heard like 8 hours into the game, but for those 8 hours you will get killed with the same jokes all over. Some take a little bit of time and it gets a bit annoying as you can''t skip and they hold the hand up and you can''t fold and go next. You will go bonkers if you''re grinding the achievements. It would''ve been a smarter design to have all the material play once with no repetition and then start replaying at random so the user doesn''t miss on anything.

Now, the achievements. The game is rigged. Too many bad beats. Even cheating by archiving save game files is still annoying, don''t do it to yourself unless you''re an autist like me.

By playing more you earn liveries for the table and chips and cards that are themed after the characters. When you unlock all 3 in a theme, you get an overhaul of the poker room, the music and some unique animations and dialogue show up. It''s kinda cool. Except the Portal theme. Its sounds were very annoying to me. Once again, this is put there to keep you playing and it''s a bad design with the repetitive dialogue. So if you don''t feel like unlocking it - you''re not missing too much. The default theme is best with its very soothing jazz music.

I tell you, it''s an enjoyable hour or two to be had, or maybe even more. I almost gave a negative review at one point, while trying to grind the achievements. Don''t be like me, just enjoy the game.

A TIE? What is this, soccer?

'),
