	 ('103149554','76561198969743313','386990','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Hello, yes, are you depressed? Or just stressed?

Relationships drain the life out of us, one minute hot on the go into the cool blue, you land that raise, yay your difficulties are over or you jump off the edge.

I''d love time alone to just spend with myself however I must feel life, that daily hussle and bussle miscreud as breakfast hour.

I''d love to devote my time to my heartfelt thoughts and feelings however only in private, I don''t mean secret, just in comfort, I don''t know where home is however I''d like to be at home with myself.

Life just gets so busy and then no one is around.

I can take ages, stay quiet, I just like the presence of people who have a life before I feel I have both privacy and feel at home with them.

Depression is just the collapse of stress, heartbreak isn''t depressing.

Heartbreak is being unable to trust love.

Which is true, you can''t trust love, you may have love and be unable to have the emotion. It is all a matter of perception.

However your perception isn''t necessary for you to know what love is and hence its availability were circumstances different.

People who would love you are all around just you have an obligation to love yourself and it takes work.

As to whether I approve or disapprove of the relationship, based on personalities is out of the question.

The characterisation, the virtues and vices is less is this a good or bad relationship on the rocks and a matter of development.

Choices in interactive games are to me about finding the morals of the author.

I may be drawn to particular likes in my choice of options however the overall theme will remain the same.

It ain''t the desire of the author to either have the relationship break up or not.

I like to see how the author characterises away from what''s bothering them.'),
