	 ('41414901','76561198331814694','386990','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I''m a big fan of Ebi-Hime, and currently own all of the VNs available and released on Steam, but Asphyxia was the first one I played / completed and has a special place in my heart. The characters and plot tie into various historical poets and their individual pieces, which is such a unique way to have wrote a story that I couldn''t pass up on the opportunity to read and learn more. The artwork is beautiful, the dialogue is smooth, the music is well looped and atmospheric, and the choices flow evenly from one to the next. The plot itself is bittersweet and leaves a sense of dissatisfaction (in my case it did, at least) with it''s broodiness and almost tragic multiple endings, but that is one of my favorite parts of Asphyxia. It remains true to it''s poetic origins, and doesn''t try to grow through prose into the happy ending many expect from VN. Sometimes a little bit of sorrow and finality is good for the soul, since it becomes a learning experience, and the way it''s framed for the characters once more harkens back to their poetic origins.

Definitely a great game for a great price, though I don''t think people who aren''t interested in gentle girl love (rather than fanservice-y type yuri) or poetry will be as captivated as I was!'),
