	 ('98930861','76561198002311591','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Underrated at release and an example of why it''s a shame Telltale went under. 

Why would anyone play a single-player poker game in 2021? Not sure, but I can say without a doubt that this is the best one you can get. The table-banter is fun. The characters feel like they have their own styles of play, and actual basic poker strategy does work at about the same rate it would playing mid-level players irl. The characters that were chosen are all strong and work together pretty well for interesting table-banter. Even Claptrap. 

This game is one I usually come back to late at night when I feel like playing something but want it to be chill. I find the pace of the table is near perfect and I don''t skip to next hand because I just like to listen to the characters and see how the hands play out. 

The reason I am still reviewing this game even though it is not available to buy is that hopefully it will somehow get released again, like Tales of the Borderlands was. 

When that day comes, I highly recommend this game, especially people who want a fun way to learn Texas Hold''em. It is also a fun game to 100%, seeing as the achievements are reasonably attainable.'),
