	 ('14535959','76561198033916210','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'This is a fun game... for a  while.  For $5 or less, it is worth it.  The characters are entertaining until the dialog gets recycled, then it becomes annoying.  Especially when play completely halts until the story you''ve already heard is done being told.  And there''s no way to skip it.  It would be nice if you could choose to get just the critical dialog to play the game, but it''s all or none.  And the available subtitles are almost illegible.  The poker game itself is not that realistic.  If you played tight (only when you have good cards) you would win just about every game.  Sometimes a player will call a big bet when there''s no way they can win.  I think the game is designed in your favor to make it easier and get you involved in more hands.  It seems like you get more lucky than you would in a real random draw of cards.  If you learned poker from this and were to enter a real game, I guarantee you would lose.  But if you''re never going to do that and/or you realize how unrealistic the gameplay here is, then it can be fun.'),
