	 ('30615831','76561198318058463','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,7,'When I first brought this I did not know what to expect as I had not played the other or seen anything to do with the game, I originally only brought it because I saw you could unlock some cosmetic stuff in borderlands 2 from it but I am glad I did get it. 

You have 4 opponents in it from the company''s other series, you are against claptrap, brock, sam (with max in the background) and ash from evil dead, the bartender is moxxi and the dealer is Gladus from the portal series, what more can you want from a poker game? 

Unlike a lot of poker games that just seem generic and bland this one could not be more opposite, between the different themed chips, cards and felts you can unlock which also change the scene of the room, Gladus making fun of you like she is known to do, the conversations during the games that the characters have with each other, the different personalities and playstyles each character has, it is a very fun game and by far the best poker game I have played. 

The only negative I could throw in is that the game has no multiplayer of any type if you are looking for that, the game was designed for single player and a fun way to unlock stuff for borderlands 2 and another game but the name slips me as I have no tplayed the other game, it says on the store page. 

'),
	 ('190708005','76561199249746951','3009850','20251230',2,1,0,0,3,'[h1] Hard Time 3 [/h1]

[h2] Review Date: [/h2]
March 20, 2025

[h2] Reviewer Name: [/h2]
Schqrk Reviews

[h2] Overall Rating: [/h2]
6/10 ⭐

[h2] Completion: [/h2]
N/A

[hr][/hr]

[h2] Introduction [/h2]
Hard Time 3 brings the classic mobile prison simulator back to PC. I didn’t play much of it, but it’s a fun throwback to the old mobile game with the same chaotic and strange prison life mechanics.

[h2] Gameplay and Mechanics [/h2]
[✔️] 🏚️ Prison Life Simulation: You can still fight, work, and survive in a weird, unpredictable prison world. It keeps that classic mobile feel with simple but enjoyable gameplay.
[❌] 🧩 Not Much Progression: I didn’t play enough to get far, but from what I saw, progression can feel a bit slow and repetitive.

[h2] Final Thoughts [/h2]
Firstly, shorter than my usual reviews but this is just due to the fact that I did not play as much. Moreover, It’s a fun, quirky throwback to the mobile version, but there’s not much new here. If you’re a fan of the series, it’s worth checking out, but it might not keep you hooked for long.

[hr][/hr]

[h2] Helpful Links [/h2]
🔗 [url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1072130/Hard_Time_3/] Hard Time 3 on Steam [/url]

