	 ('175278595','76561198173451687','3009850','20251230',57,4,0,0,0,'I really want to give this game a good review and this game has the opportunity to be perfect, but MDickie has made so many dumb changes that completely strip what made the previous games fun. The main issue I have is how the wanted system works. If you commit even the most minor crimes, the alarm will immediately go off and a million officers will swarm you instantly. Since NPCs can enter and exit rooms in real time now, officers will keep on spawning even if they aren''t any in the room. It''s nearly impossible to actually do the crazy fun stuff that made the previous games fun since you have no chance at getting away with it now. Which brings me to the next point. Instead of extending your sentence or fining you if they find you guilty, they do punishments like cutting a limb off, or the worst of all, the death penalty. No matter how minor the crime is if you rack up enough court visits it''s possible to get the death penalty causing a game over. This punishes the player even more from doing anything remotely fun which makes the game even more boring.

The main problem overall is that the game is just very boring. There''s no schedule like in the other games like dinner time, random terrorist attacks, etc. You just roam the very small prison and maybe get attacked for no reason. There''s not even any funny dialogue or random events like prisoners making fun of you, offering you to join a gang, betting money to fight you, etc. the NPCs only talk to you at the worst possible times to give either completely useless information or the most basic information about the game. The only missions I''ve encountered from other NPCs are stuff like giving them an item, delivering an item to a location, etc. Apparently there are gangs in this game but you wouldn''t even be able to tell because there''s no dialogue talking about them and NPCs don''t have tattoos or accessories to show their membership. Another feature that''s gone, which is probably the feature that made the previous games so repayable is the randomly generated NPCs. The 2D version had the default characters but you could also generate new ones. This game lacks that feature and there''s no excuse for it because the previous games from over a decade ago had the ability to randomly generate characters. Playing with the same MDickie characters we are all used to gets extremely boring.

I had this similar feeling with Old School when I realized quickly how boring it is, and even more disappointing is that this game has many of the same problems Old School has. At least though with Old School you had a schedule to follow and you could actually had more of a chance to escape from teachers trying to arrest you. There''s lots of new weapons added but you won''t ever get a chance to use them because you''ll get arrested or even killed instantly if you try to attack someone. There''s so much more details and features that are missing I can go on about like not being able to pick your crime, random terrorist attacks, random intruders, way clunkier combat etc. Calling this game a combination of "classic moments from the OG with the best aspects of 2D" is blatant false advertising because all this seems to be is the 2D version in 3D, but missing the previous features from the 2007 game while removing features from the 2D game. I''ve been playing MDickie games for almost 10 years and they were a huge part of my childhood. It pains me to see how in the past he seemed to genuinely want to improve each game by adding new mechanics, ideas, and features, but ever since the released of Old School, the games just feel very lazily made with only a couple new items, weapons, and features combined with all the annoying changes that make the game unplayable. Even Wrestling Empire suffered this problem by removing staple features like limb dismemberment. 

Tl;dr: This game is just a stripped down, lazily made remake of the 2D version missing features from both 2D and OG Hard Time and punishes you when you actually try to have fun. Just go play the older games instead.'),
	 ('200591799','76561198854457613','2427430','20251230',3,1,0,0,1,'shitty piece of shit'),
	 ('175187266','76561198441159372','3009850','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'A lot of the criticisms of this new version are very valid but for the $11 I spent on  (I would spend a full 20) this game, I have had a blast. I have been playing Mdickie games before they ever became a youtube content trend and while I expected a lot more from this version of Hard Time I was not dissappointed at all by any means. Tons of new content, you can actually arrest people now as an officer which actually gives you a motive to play as a warden as you can either be a noble peacekeeper or abuse your power,

Wardens are far more powerful (which I personally like despite people whining about it) in the previous versions of Hard Time it was way too easy to escape with a shovel and now its so much harder with the higher volume of officers, Also justs adds a layer of immersion too, you are far less invincible in comparison to former versions. you have to time your crime-doing, 

The prison is also smaller than both the 3D version and 2D version. I mean cmon man its 2024. Thats probably my biggest dissapointment about the game. Its still laid out basically the same with noticeable changes. 

Overall though even with the higher volume of wardens the chaos is still out of control. classic mdickie style, there is never a dull moment in this game. absolutely love it,'),
