	 ('72921067','76561198041916371','386990','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'I have mixed feelings about this game. The art is lovely, but the teacher looks younger than her students. The music is very pretty, too. The prose is also very interesting and undoubtedly helps create the continuously gloomy, desperate mood. I thought the weaving in of all the Romantic poets was clever and found the supplemental material fascinating. Romantic poetry isn''t my area of expertise, but I know enough about literature to appreciate what disasters most canonical authors were in their lives.

However, I''d like some variation in options for Samantha''s life. From a contemporary perspective, it''s odd that she hasn''t been advised to see a therapist before now. It hurtful that even her friends are brutally mean to her, and that before they are even acknowledged to be so cruel. Though, it''s all too common that others assume she can just "get better" if she decides to.

Maybe I was just hoping that I could romance Georgia and have Samantha benefit from her unshakable confidence because she is an absolutely spectacular character. I stan a shameless demon.'),
