	 ('88635683','76561198009754039','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'Is Necro-Reviewing a thing? Let me ask Ash.

The Pokernight series is simultaneously one of the most ballsy and mundane games out there you can purchase. The premise is a simple high stakes game of digital poker. No real money, no real losers, win some cool card backs and table skins. But wait. The dealer is GLaDOS and your poker buddies are Ash Williams, Sam (of &Max), Brock Sampson, and CL4PTRAP.  This game thrives on its dialogue and interactions. Telltale might be known for weird gameplay, but their writing is on the tee as always. Every character is written extremely well to form, and having characters like Brock Samson ask Ash Williams about deadites, or watching CL4PTRAP hopelessly hit on GLaDOS supplies a sense of euphoria you rarely get these days. There''s thousands of voice-lines and interactions for just about every situation that you''ll be running into new gags years later. Even if you don''t know Poker, the stakes are so low and the interaction is so fun that you''ll learn before you know it. If this band of characters doesn''t strike you, Poker Night 1 is essentially the same, with Heavy Weapons Guy, Strong Bad, Max (of Sam&) and Tycho Brahe (the webcomic one, not the real one). I suggest checking out one, if not both.'),
