Poker is hard, but it shouldn''t be, right?'),
	 ('9629141','76561198051315318','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'POKER NIGHT 2

From Telltale Games, the genius'' behind Poker Night at the Inventory, The Walking Dead series, (no, the good one) and such classics as that other game they made, comes the sequel of the previously mentioned game.

Poker Night 2 is a complex open-world Space-themed RPG, with an amazing three part story line, complex moral decisions, and in depth NPC relationships. Well, it would be, if it was Mass Effect, which it isn''t.

What Poker Night 2 ACTUALLY is, is a fun, short video game based on a boring, long card game. With such features as-
Playing Poker
Winning at Poker
Losing at Poker
Playing Ohama (''Whats that?'' Exactly.)

Ok, Im tired, so Im gonna sum this up. Poker Night to is an attempt to bring a beloved Card game to PC gamers. An attempt, which I can safely say without snipers taking me out, that has succeeded. Bring back the formula of its predecessor, you, a nameless, mute player, play a high stakes, (not really) game of Poker with your favourite characters from Pop culture, such as Brock Samson, the one guy from that Adult Swim thing, Ash Williams, the titular character from Army of Darkness (Ask your Mum) Sam, from Sam and Max (You know the Rabbit thing? His partner.) And Claptrap! Yeah! You know Claptrap! With luck, skill and patience you must beat these four, game after game, to win their secret special buyins.
Its pretty much the same.

Some new features they added are the random challenges, being a way to keep you playing, insead of spamming restart to get Max''s Pistol. These range from, ''win a hand'' to ''do a backflip,'' so they test your patience. The banter between the guys is funny, and there is heaps of it. GladOs mocking you get dull, but every now and then, a new skit will pop, and a smile will stretch across your face.

What I am trying to say is, I came for the items, I stayed for the Poker
Im stilling trying to *get* the items.

Bullshit....'),
