	 ('15164635','76561198001519540','234710','20251230',11,0,0,0,9,'A fun game with bad poker mechanics, mostly amusing characters (I can barely stand Claptrap in the Borderlands series, he isn''t much better here), and a bounty/unlockable reward system that half works. The challenge system for gaining the opportunity to unlock bounties is a step-up from the RNG of the last game (which lead to me restarting until I got bounty games after the dialogue became stale). GLaDOS is excellent as always, and having her as the dealer was a wise move.

When it comes down to it though, actual poker players say it''s nothing like playing poker, and the unlockable bounties for Borderlands 2 straight up don''t work; it''s possible to get them if you contact Gearbox support, but I think when you have to open a ticket to recieve what is debateably the biggest selling point of the game, the product is fundamentally flawed.

This isn''t a game for poker players or collectors.'),
