	 ('986920','76561197983733611','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Like the first Poker Night, this one suffers from serious dialog problems; over repatition, some badly written things, etc. They''re all present, and just as with the first game, if you want to score the BL2 and TF2 items, you''ll have to grin and bare it.

That''s not to say that the dialog and some of the interactions between the other "players" isn''t funny. Far from it, and at times it can have you laughing so hard you''ll cry. But hearing the same jokes/insults/etc over and over and over and over and over again can sometimes make you want to reach through the screen and slap them.

That all having been said, Poker Night 2 changes a few things from the original and adds in some twists. Some you can see listed on the Steam Store page, others you''ll have to discover on your own. 

All in all the game can be enjoyable, but the main reason that most I know that own the game play it is for the BL2 and/or TF2 items. And at only $5, even if you just play it to get all the items for other games and thats it, it''s still worth it.'),
