	 ('43156955','76561198023649205','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'[h1][b]Poker Night 2: Short but Sweet[/b][/h1]

[b]Poker Night 2[/b] is as the title suggests the second installment of Poker games at Night.

That''s it, review over! You want more? Fine!

Essentially at it''s heart it''s a poker game, but [b]Poker Night 2[/b] does something that adds a whole other level to this game and that''s its superb atmosphere. Sure you could just go online and play for real money or just grab a real deck of cards and gamble with friends but what you get here is something else.

In [b]Poker Night 2[/b] you''ll find yourself playing in [b]The Inventory[/b] an exclusive club for the richest players and so it seems some of the goofiest video game and pop culture characters! Oh did I not mention that? You get to play with some well know video game and pop culture characters such as:

[b]Claptrap (Borderlands 2)[/b]
[b]Brock Samson (The Venture Bros.)[/b]
[b]Ash (Army of Darkness)[/b]
[b]Sam (Sam and Max series)[/b]

And best or worst of all depending on where you stand with psychotic self aware A.I, your dealer is the one and only [b]GLaDOS (Portal)[/b]

The writing for all these characters is fantastic, non stop witty jokes and references to their source material as well as the odd gag here and there.

Other then that [b]Poker Night 2[/b] doesn''t offer too much, there are some items you can win from the characters in the game which can be used in other games such as [b]Team Fortress 2[/b]. these can be found [url=https://wiki.teamfortress.com/wiki/Poker_Night_2][b]here[/b][/url]

If you''re looking for replayability this game can lose it''s charm after a few hours so if you don''t mind a time killer with a few extra items grab it on sale but you won''t be dissapointed grabbing it at full price!

Have fun and remember gamble responsibly, pffft who am I kidding it''s just a video game.

[b]GO ALL IN![/b]'),
