	 ('186049230','76561198017731235','3009850','20251230',11,4,0,0,0,'If you have Old School, you have this game. It''s nearly the same with nearly all the same assets and locations, except you''re in prison.

You create your character, customize them, and when you start in prison you nearly instantly get in trouble for "Impersonation". This happens over and over until you set all your clothing colors to the exact color percentages that match your cell block. You are not provided these numbers or a way to know how to even stop being arrested over and over. This is one of the many issues with this game that easily could have been fixed, patched, or provided to the player. Maybe even a default "Prisoner" outfit that you can''t change the color to.

You cannot change the controls and the provided controls are awful. I tried using a controller but I could not move up or down, only left or right. WASD? No, it''s the directional pad and random buttons across the keyboard.

All the assets from Old School are here, the NPC''s look a little different but do the same thing. They all randomly attack you, if you defend yourself you''re arrested. Think you can fight the officers and not get arrested? Nope. All they have to do is grapple you, which is extremely easy to do, then you''re in a court room again. You can also get taken to court for sleeping.

Want to go on a rampage and just have fun? Nope. The second you strike an officer or do ANYTHING other than stand in your cell, you''ll be grappled by a guard and teleported to court.

You can try to escape the prison, which was my goal, but with how easy it is to get grabbed by a guard, it was nearly impossible. The only time I enjoyed myself was the random moment where crime became legal for 1 day, then I got arrested for sleeping, again.

Even if you can get past the controls, the 100s of times you get attacked by guards/inmates for no reason, getting arrested for the 100th time, what do you have? A standing in jail simulator.'),
