	 ('171512635','76561198388102698','584640','20251230',5,4,0,0,0,'This is probably the worst gameplay loop I''ve seen in my entire life.

Videogames are usually made by people passionate about videogames. This feels like it was made by someone who not only hates them, but does not even understand what a videogame is supposed to be and feel.
If the levels are going to be random, at least make sure I don''t go through 30 impossible setups at a time. 
If you''re a barely competent programmer you know you can generate a random seed that will at least cover most cases that would avoid killing the player due to bad design and laziness (placing of the main obstacles, speed and spawn location of the fucking birds, placing the 3s twice with a SINGULAR gap between them, ffs...).

I only stuck for as long as I did because of the story, but it feels like that will end up going nowhere. Kudos to the artists and musicians though.

It had potential, I really like chickens. But to whoever ruined this experience with the gameplay implementation itself: fuck you, and go for everything else in life BUT game programming.


I don''t feel frustrated by the game loop itself, but with its implementation. It''s fine if you want to do a chrome dinosaur clone, but you can''t be as shitty as to fuck that up this badly.'),
