	 ('29115065','76561198289473722','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Poker Night 2 ended up reaching higher than my expectations. I''ve read a lot of negative reviews on this game due to the sometimes annoying dialogue and "insane difficulty", but I still stand by the fact that this game is great.

The difficulty was nowhere near as bad as I expected. Like Poker Night 1, you can actually knock someone out in as quick as 3 rounds if lucky. The Bounty Challenges can sometimes be tedious, but it''s all worth it in the end for that free TF2 and Borderlands 2 loot.

If I can give a tip: DO NOT LET SAM BE THE LAST COMPETITOR REMAINING. HE WILL DESTROY YOU BY THROWING HUGE BETS AND RAISING ALL THE TIME.

Speaking of the AI, they work great here, and are a lot better compared to Poker Night 1. 

Overall, Poker Night 2 is a great sequel game to Poker Night 1, with more loot for TF2 and new loot for Borderlands 2, as well as new characters to play against. If you like the first game, then you''re bound to love the second.

Rating - 8/10'),
