	 ('60954300','76561198046113874','1086030','20251230',21,0,0,0,9,'Okay, first off, the description''s wrong; both main characters are very obviously bisexual.

There are a couple of common problems. Text should be unlabeled if it''s the protagonist''s thoughts and labeled with their name if it''s spoken, and it''s not done consistently (meaning Miley says some things out loud she probably isn''t intended to). Miley has an "ahegao" face emote used in nonsexual contexts. There are some gynecological closeups on one route, probably intended for men buying yuri. There''s basically only one pose for each character with outfit changes -- no one gestures.

The writing is OK, though it describes what I''d consider a really bad date (and a worse one-night stand). [spoiler]Emily is a manipulative, narcissistic bitch who plays constant mind games and sets little "tests." Desperate or not, I''d have walked out on her after the practical joke with the spices; you can put someone in the hospital that way.[/spoiler] Miley''s an appealing character, but she''s a cliché anime-protagonist-doofus; with how many characters like that we''ve seen it only makes sense they''d have perfected the formula.

