	 ('14429004','76561198057842710','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Poker Night 2

I got this game since it was super cheap and on sale. I gotta tell you, it was worth the price I bought it at.

The game play consists of you just playing Texas Hold Em'' or Omaha with the same 4 characters all the time. There''s Brock from a show I forget the name of, Claptrap from Borderlands, Ash from Evil Dead and Army of Darkness, and Sam from the Sam and Max games. Of course Max is there too and will be involved in conversations sometimes...and yea all the characters have conversations with each other all the time. It''d be from Claptrap trying to figure out a catch phrase to use to Brock questioning Sam''s very existence. I gotta admit, you will find yourself chuckling at their random conversations they have.

There isn''t much of a story besides you coming to your favorite hang out to hang out with your favorite characters in high costing poker...yea there is a small currency system. You will start off with 20 grand and you will have to buy in, in order to play poker. I forget the amount you need to buy in. I believe you can also buy the other player''s drinks as well to throw them off their game. I never really got to doing this but I found it a neat feature once it got introduced to me.

For those of you who don''t know Texas Hold Em or Omaha, you are required to learn it in order to play this game and be successful at it. It will not teach you how to play, it will just throw you in and say good luck!

After playing and winning a game or two of poker, you will find that you can have a chance to play for the character''s prized posessions. Of course it seems like they don''t want to give it up but they do. I never got to win one of these and when I was about to...I experienced a game breaking glitch that made me have to quit the game all together...yea don''t do any actions too quickly or you will find yourself staring at the characters endlessly like that weird neighbor next door with a bad dress code.

7/10
If you can get this game for like a dollar or less. I urge you heavily to get it. Its not a graphics hog and you will have a couple hours of entertainment. If you need a cheap time killer, this is the game for you. This game doesn''t have a whole lot of replayability unless you return to it after like a couple months of playing it. But it definitely is worth a playthrough or two.'),
