	 ('173591806','76561198067737650','840930','20251230',4,0,0,0,4,'This is the worst game in the XL collection. It really doesn''t have much to do with skill because the only control is slowing the player icon in a vertical lane to avoid object impacts. Another lane to jump horizontally or lives would make this a much less frustrating experience. It''s basically just 60 sec runs over and over until you get lucky with the object pattern and good power ups. Sometimes the objects will be reasonably spaced and other times you''ll have blue and orange rectangles stacked in a pattern that''s impossible to get around. Impact detection for the rectangle objects are awful and the "near misses" are extremely inconsistent. The time stop and nuke power-ups are useful, but the +2 is just a waste; it should be +5. My best runs were due to not getting any +2''s and luck for good object spacing. My average run is about a minute. I absolutely hate the pacing. It needs to start out slower and build up. The escalation between objects around 50-80 points is nuts.'),
