	 ('174759433','76561198003903323','3009850','20251230',0,0,0,0,7,'This one is hard, no that''s not an attempt at a pun but... I really want to like this. I''ve been looking forward to and hoping for Hard Time 3 long before it was even announced. Let alone before it probably even began to be created by MDickie. 

Something about it feels off and I think I''ve figured out what it is, the geometry. Now I have to admit I''ve only played for a short time and have not explored the city but from what I can interpret it''s the same locations and found in Old School.

The prison feels strange, the central hall feels cramped and the cell blocks can be accessed from walking from one end to the other as in Hard Time 2D which is fair enough I suppose but it doesn''t match up with the layout of the prison. I know this game isn''t focused too much on immersion but cells on both sides of the block have outward facing windows pointing to a city landscape high above which according to the map of the prison doesn''t make sense. 

The library and workshop also seem to give off a less than secure vibe, I know these were assets also taken from Old School but hell even in the cafe there''s still posters on the wall for kids. I don''t know if all of this is meant to be changed over time but it''s small things like this that are messing with my head and preventing me from getting into the game and believing that I''m actually in prison? The prison itself is where players will spend a good 70 - 80% of their time whilst serving their sentence so it would make sense to make this space as engaging as possible.

Also, the jobs issued by guards and inmates don''t seem to make sense. I get told to find another inmate, I find them and then I open a dialogue and I only have the option to ask where they are, and the person says they don''t know... despite being the very inmate I''m looking for? 

Again, this is weird, I really want to like this game, I played the original non-stop and was hoping this would build upon it. I thought there''d be influence from old school, like a timetable system. Hell that would work perfectly for a prison environment right? Maybe jobs to apply and work for? Again this was featured  in the first one and MDickie''s skills have improved 100% since then which again is why I feel so conflicted about not liking this game. 

I mean I DO like it but... it''s missing something. Maybe I''m getting ahead of myself as of course, I know nothing of game design so I really am in no place to dictate what makes the cut and what doesn''t and for what reason.

Hard Time is in my opinion the most or second to most known MDickie title, possibly now stepping back in the wake of Wrestling Empire (Brilliant game) and I just hope there''s more to fill this out as an experience to come back to for years to come.

Ah- MDickie, I apologise if you actually do read these comments I hope you forgive this poorly constructed critique. (I seldom write comments on games). Maybe there''s more planned? Or maybe there''s limitations I''m unaware of, either way I just wanted to voice my thoughts. 

I recommend it of course all the same but certain features are missing and for me it shows.

