	 ('16693124','76561198053802723','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,3,'Overall review after completing Poker Night 2

PROS:
-You can play both Texas Hold ''em and Omaha style
-Nice amount of challenge, never too easy
-Interaction between characters is a nice distraction from the high stakes poker
-Unlockable chips, cards, and felts from different games that can be combined to decorate the Inventory
-Unlockables for Borderlands 2 and Team Fortress 2
-GLaDOS is present

CONS:
-The menus are painfully slow to navigate
-Animations can be off at times
-Some bounty challenges are very time consuming
-You can only skip dialogue in the beginning of the tournament, you cannot skip the rest
-Characters will soon repeat their lines, which becomes very annoying
-Experienced times where on a character''s turn, they wouldn''t do anything, requiring a restart to fix
-Luck(?)'),
