	 ('82705580','76561198022308080','513320','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Good walking sim with some issues. 

I only played it for 1h and the setiing is nice.
Bit of a strange Alice setting but nice.

There are some parts realy just waling.
Not that bad, but somtimes fells like stretching the game.
On the other side its all about the Story in visuals so it''s fine i guess.
Afaik you can adjust the charater speed if these "empty" sections are bothering you. I havend tried it.

What was bothering me the most, after five minutes my charakter was way off where it should be, taking me straight through walls. Since it''s not Room Scale i guess it was a tracking issue. Maybe on hardware side but could also be the game itself. idk. i was playing standing up and havent moved an inch. After clipping through a wall first time i even stopped turning irl and only used the controller for any movent but still ending inside of walls. even after resetting my possition.

And the controlls.... well...
i hope it''s compatibility with my index but i only could move forward.
rotation is always 90° via the A buttons or grip on the left and right controller.
Everything else semse fine. like interact is ponting and trigger.
Not be able to rotate via stick was very strange.
Also the walking direction is always the directin you are looking. Not where your controllers (body) is facing.
Strange but i can get used to it.

Interestingly this game is one of the few where i didn''t got motionsickness while moving normaly (no teleportation).
That''s defenetly a pro.
Some games e.g. vr dungeon knight makes me verry sick. after a short time with normal movement.
Skyrim vr isn''t that bad, but i need a brak after about 1 or 2 h.
Alice VR was totaly fine.

At the End
If you can get used to bad/strange Controlls (at least on Index Knuckles)
like walking sims and want to play a sci-fi version of Alice: 
Get it! It''s not that bad of a deal for 10 bucks.
Or just wait for a sale if 10 seems still to much.

Haven''t had any performance issues.
With the clipping through walls maybe an tracking issue on my side, i think i can still recommend this game.
At least for an Index-Player!'),
