	 ('200964990','76561198159649809','2427430','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I''ve been playing the Enhanced Edition since day one, and at first, it was clear that the use of some upscaling and lighting technologies caused noticeable graphical and performance issues. In fact, in many cases, the game looked and performed worse than the original, which was disappointing for an edition that aimed to improve the experience.

However, everything changed with the 1.2 update. The improvement was absurdly good — the graphics and overall performance were massively enhanced. The image is now crystal clear with excellent resolution, and the upgrades in lighting, textures, and overall quality of life are immediately noticeable.

This truly feels like the definitive way to play the vanilla version of Call of Pripyat. I love that GSC took the time to fix things so quickly after a rough launch. My sincere congratulations to the developers — they turned things around impressively.'),
