	 ('7931625','76561198048869325','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'"MY mother warned me against playing poker with robots, cripples, dogs and mutes."  -Brock sampson.  This game is fun and addictive, though it does require skill at poker or critical thinking.  Know the right time to bet small and bet big, because that will make the difference between a game ending too quickly or lasting longer than it should.  Know when to fold; if you stay in every hand hoping for blind luck you will be disapointed often.  

You might get a bit offened if you are thin skinned, because the other players - and the dealer - will intimidate and sometimes insult you.  Especially when you lose.  "How could that be fun?" you might ask.  Well, when the other players are Brock Sampson, Claptrap, Ash form the Evil Dead movies and Sam from Sam and Max, and the dealer is GLaDOS, I found it easy to take their ribbing in stride.  

Pros:  Fun and not too difficult if you pay attention to the rules and not be afriad to fold.  Brock Sampson and GLaDOS are just awesome.  In-game challenges and unlockables are good, and there''s a decent amount of achievements for those of us who are into that.  You can even win unique accessories for use in Borderlands 2 and Team Fortess 2.  All this for less than the price of a typical combo meal.

Ths cons are:  They need some mouse accelleration as it is a bit unresponsive in the menus.  If a tournament goes for on hour or so there''s the chance you will hear repeats in some of their conversations.  There''s no difficulty setting, which will put off people who would prefer an easy ride.  They didn''t or coulnd''t get Bruce Campbell for the voice of Ash, and the guy doing his voice does a pretty weak imitation.'),
