	 ('42893095','76561197978907605','234710','20251230',4,0,0,0,10,'It''s pretty much the same as Night at the Inventory, just with different characters and a slightly updated "unlock" system. The stuff you unlock is primarily aesthetic, but you''re given the option to serve your opponents drinks which will make them more likely to give their tell in a given tournament.

As I''ve said about the last one, this is a pretty fun game if you enjoy poker, and the banter between everyone (and now GladOS, who sorta acts as the hostess) is pretty enjoyable. I like this one more than the last on the sole basis that the gameplay is more fast-paced and the achievements are far less grind-y to get.

It''s a good game. If you like poker, you''ll probably enjoy it. If you don''t, you won''t. The game doesn''t feel rigged or unfair in any way compared to a real poker table, which is something I see a lot of people often complaining about. It''s as fair as anything else. If anything, the player has far more advantage in this over real poker because you have advantages that the AI doesn''t have access to, and the AI will behave in certain ways given a set of circumstances whereas a player would be more unreliable. So uh, stop whining and get better at poker.'),
