	 ('63217946','76561198043905366','234710','20251230',2,1,0,0,10,'It''s the sequel to the Poker Night at the Inventory, what did you expect? More of the same stuff, just replace the cast from the first Poker Night with a newer cast. Here, you''ve got a new group in Ash Williams from Evil Dead, Sam who is the other half of Sam/Max, Brock Samson from Venture Brothers, Claptrap from Borderlands and your dealer is GlaDOS from Portal. I didn''t feel like this group meshed as well as the previous cast did. In the first Poker Night, every character played off eachother with remarks and commentary that just built a blend of chemistry. It''s like hanging out with a bunch of obscure but cool friends.

I didn''t get a lot of that in Poker Night 2, which was a miss for me. I felt like everyone is just off on vacation from their respective universes to just decide to sit down and have a game of poker. Everything else still is the same, just different themed chips, cards and table. Still the same deal, earn a character''s buy-in by eliminating them when they go all in.

Just like the other game, you can''t buy this anymore since Telltale went defunct in 2018. If it did return, though, I don''t think I''d recommend this. This is honestly a choice of which group of characters you''d like to play with. I don''t care for Claptrap, I don''t know Brock Samson enough, I don''t care for Sam, GlaDOS is okay and Ash Williams is easily my favorite of the bunch. Regardless, I still had played and had more fun with the interactions of the first group in the first game.

The only way I think, that the Poker Night games could''ve been more flavorful, is if there was a bigger roster involved. Like, have 12 characters you could see come to the table, all in rotation. Something to add more spice to the game, than release what feels like DLC packs.'),
