	 ('176773831','76561198134989107','3009850','20251230',15,0,0,0,0,'As quite a fan of Mdickie''s games, I was really hopefuly for Hard Time 3 especially given how successful Wrestling Empire has been since it''d came to PC, however, for the three hours of playing this game I found myself simply bored. Here''s why:

No schedule?
There''s no set schedule - You sleep in your cell from 20:00 - 08:00; You wake up, you go around the prison and a guard or another prisoner will occasionally give you a task that''s really dull. The task will either end up with you being beaten, arrested and your sentence extended or will be do-able and your sentence is reduced for a day. 

Overcrowded, corrupt guards
Guards will randomly start fights with you, but if you fight back? Your sentence is extended. I had my prisoner lay in bed, a guard came over, didn''t speak to me and instead began to beat me up - I fought back, was arrested for ''insubordination'' and my character was sentenced to have a limb removed. You start a fight with a random inmate in a confined area, and you''ll be wanted for it regardless of if anybody saw it; In seconds, the room is swarmed and you''re against guards with fully automatic weapons, if they grab you? You''re arrested and your sentence is increased. I''m all for the goofiness and unpredictability of Mdickie''s games, its what makes them fun for the most part, but this game''s unpredictability combined with its lack of objectives simply make it frustratingly boring. It''s not worth the current price tag and I wish I''d stopped prior to the two hour mark so I could get my money back.

Editor
