	 ('107288587','76561198035100973','584640','20251230',29,4,0,0,0,'Absolutely incredible presentation and sense of style. I loved the cutscenes and the bosses were decent.

But the general gameplay is horrendously bad. Almost every weapon you unlock during the story is useless, the pistol by far being the best weapon. Most of the equipment is equally useless though not quite as badly balanced as the weapons.

The real problem with the game however is that the random generation is completely fucked. Once you get past the 2nd or 3rd world, passing a level comes down almost completely to luck because getting impossible sequences is incredibly common. It''s hard to believe considering how simple the game mechanics are that the randomly generated stages could be so scuffed.

It''s impossible to really comment on the difficulty of the game because it is completely luck based. It goes anywhere from braindead easy to actually impossible, trending more towards impossible the further you get in the game. It''s beatable 100% don''t get me wrong, you just have to grind out attempts until you get a lucky level sequence, which is not at all satisfying. I ended up quitting on the final world because I just got tired of losing completely unwinnable scenarios.

One theory I have is that the game is actually designed for local Co-op with zero consideration for re-balancing for 1 player. Because at any point in time a 2nd person can drop in or out and it doesn''t seem to scale or change the game at all. The game would be significantly easier with double the fire power and effectively 2 lives per stage. This wouldn''t necessarily be a problem if the game advertised itself as a primarily a co-op experience, but nowhere on the store page does it even mention co-op even exists in the game so who knows.

Either way though its really besides the point. The randomly generated stages are completely unbalanced and the gameplay is extremely subpar overall. Would not recommend.'),
