	 ('65797784','76561198010723882','513320','20251230',3,0,0,0,10,'SUPPORTS OCULUS RIFT, BUT NOT TOUCH!  MUST USE CONTROLLER WITH RIFT!
It actually says that in the Requirements, but you have to look closely.  If you try to use Touch the game crashes, just like so many of the comments are saying.

Now with that issue out of the way...

Alice VR is a good VR adventure.  While it has a few short comings which prevent it from being exceptional (A rating) it is never the less professionally developed and quite playable (B rating).

Pros:
+ Pure adventure game of exploration, puzzles and story.  No combat or reaction time requirements.
+ Beautiful 3D graphics.
+ The surreal hallucination scenes are just wonderful.
+ Comfortable 90 degree click turns available in VR.
+ No unfair puzzles.  They can all be figured out.
+ Excellent voice acting.
+ Took me ten hours to finish.  That meets the old industry standard of $1 per hour of game play.
+ Sound track, art book, wallpaper and additional level come free with the game.

Cons:
- Story is a little weak.  It could have been fleshed out much more.
- The Lewis Carol characters could have been used to much greater effect. Some are barely mentioned.
- We are told that our choices affect the game''s outcome, but I found very few places where you had a choice.  It appeared like you had to collect everything in an area before you could move on.  I recall only two places where you might have been allowed to leave resources behind.  Any such capability should have been made more clear in the game play.
- There are dune buggies to take you across large areas faster, but they do not have click turn in VR.  You must constantly blink to avoid motion sickness.
- Save points.  I want to save a game every time I successfully accomplish something so that I don''t have to replay significant amounts of the game every time I start it back up.  Too bad for me.
- Only one save game slot.  I like to have multiple slots so I can experiment and then go back to a save point to continue the game.  Also, I would like to let my friends try the game out without losing my save game.

But the bottom line is that it is a very good professionally made adventure game.  I enjoyed playing it.'),
