	 ('39483727','76561198327367911','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Classic Texas hold ''em, and Omaha (not sure if anybody ever plays Omaha, but it is in here) with a very memorable cast from various games. The banter and humor is excellent, there are also a number of challenges you can play for to keep you interested, as well as different felts, themes and decks to unlock.

Pros - some very lovealbe characters showing their quirky personalities, various things to unlock as well as rewards, easy casual game play at its best.

Cons - after playing the game for more than 10 in game hours, you basically know every bit of conversation in here and although very funny in the beginning, there is no option to skip it once it get''s started later in game. Either we need even more dialogue, or it should be skippable. Another big sadness for me was the lack of multiplay so a friend could join in the fun, even if a friend could play as one of the main characters, it would have been great, but alas, no. This would definitly have tipped the game close to 10 for me. More characters would also be great, or the option to select which characters you want to play with.

Multiplay aside, it''s still one of the best single player poker games I''ve ever played. Looking forward to Poker Night 3... Any of the ''Tales from the Borderlands'', ''Walking dead'' or ''Wolf amongst us'' characters will be great Telltale... 8.5/10'),
