	 ('177602739','76561198193350841','3009850','20251230',24,10,0,0,0,'This game is one of the wildest things I have ever played. I killed someone, was arrested for vandalism, got a leg chopped off, gave a random woman a baseball bat then she gave birth to a child after we hugged. I then took the baseball bat back, got arrested for theft, and received the death penalty. 5/5'),
	 ('1006980','76561197984224864','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,6,'A fun poker game with lots of personality. Very inexpensive, rather entertaining.

My complaints are the same as the original: no DLC expansions, and too limited a focus of poker. While the inclusion of Omaha along with the default Texas Hold''em is rather nice, its still lacking many great poker variants. No 5- or 7- card draw, stud, no high/low, no dealer''s pick.

Moreover, no multiplayer, real-time or asynchronous, local or online. This is probably the most dissapointing aspect of the game, really. I really wish they had charged more to include these features.

While its hard to go wrong for $5, I really think Tell-Tale should go ahead and see how much of a game they could make for $10 or $20!

edit: 5/23/15 - the lack of Cloud Saves is a big problem as well. All my unlocks went out the window :(

edit: 1/7/16 - Poker Night 2 runs pretty well on a Microsoft Surface 3 on low settings. Mostly okay with touch.'),
