	 ('198509710','76561197980395376','2427430','20251230',11,3,0,0,10,'[h3]Same as it Ever Was[/h3]

There isn''t all that much to be said about Call of Pripyat: Enhanced Edition. The edition''s enhancements are minuscule at best and don''t really improve the game much. Aside from the spelling of certain locations being changed, the only real difference I noticed was that the saving and loading has been made much worse than in the original.

In the original, you had 5 quicksave slots that cycled as you saved over them. This kept the number of saves manageable, but allowed you to have several states, not including manual and auto saves, throughout the game. In EE, however, there are no quicksave slots which means that quicksaves will rapidly accumulate over your playthrough. This will cause the "Load Game" menu to open more and more slowly the more save files there are, making the game hand for multiple seconds even with an m.2 SSD, and will only get progressively worse. The only remedy is to find where the saves are and delete the old ones to restore the opening speed.

For future reference, the save files are found under "C:\Users\<username>\Saved Games".

Beyond that issue, is is largely the same exact Call of Pripyat that I have already played several times. I believe the original, with some mods, is the superior alternative to this.'),
