	 ('198115673','76561199208485664','2427430','20251230',1,0,0,0,2,'The Call of Pripyat is my favorite part of the main trilogy. It conveys in detail many real locations of the existing place, which is why the fans of the series are so fond of it.
The visual update in this part was realized the best. I didn''t find any bugs or visual defects during the entire playthrough, and the game didn''t crash even once.
Pripyat, as an exclusion zone, looks incredibly realistic. We don''t just visit a post-apocalyptic city, but really feel its character: abandoned apartments, abandoned roads, broken cars, and many small details that make the world come alive. All of this makes you feel nostalgic and at the same time realize that every step in this place could be your last. And the children''s voices in the X-8 laboratory and the playground evoke eerie feelings.
It was a good hunt, stalker.'),
