	 ('11712996','76561198039987043','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'Don''t bother getting this if you played Poker Night 1. The game is the same, and the AI is just as dumb. The only one winning here is whoever decided that rushing out the same game with a slightly different setting and lesser-known characters wasn''t a one-way ticket to Hell for excessive greed.

Who are these characters anyway? Last game, they got Max from Sam and Max who we should all remember from childhood cartoons, Strong Bad from the most awesome flash website ever created, The Heavy from a FPS, and one original character who was a spoof of what TTG thinks of gamers which was actually somewhat amusing at times.
This time, there''s a bland angry guy who has the voice of Joe from Family Guy, some annoying robot thing that claims to be from Pandora but definitely was not in Avatar and was probably only included so the graphics people could work less, some guy called Ash who can''t be the adult version of the Pokemon character unless he''s fighting undead Marowaks or something, and finally the only character who isn''t out of nowhere or just made up, Sam from Sam and Max.

Even having Sam is barely enough, he was only given about 4 good lines, all where he''s talking with Max rather than these other personality-deprived nobodies. Much more often, you''re stuck hearing annoying robot guy''s excessively long voice clips that can''t be skipped and which pause the action (there really should be an option to mute him or replace him with Max or something), or having to hear 10+ times a game everyone overact to every All-In, despite how commonly the AI does it themselves. But at least GLADOS is the dealer so we don''t have to hear bland short sailor guy talk much anymore.

If you want to play poker online, find some other free website to play it at, it''s not worth it to get this just for Sam, Max, and a couple of other much less interesting personalities, all backed by the same stupidly bluffing AI as the last game.'),
