	 ('159731942','76561198045061508','513320','20251230',0,1,0,0,4,'So far I find it to be decent game. When I first loaded the game I would constantly get Fatal Crash. I eventually learned that you cannot use touch controllers to play this game or it just crashes. I also learned the developers don''t care about this game anymore and will likely not update it any longer. I ended up having to play with the HMD and an XBOX controller.. That is until the xbox controller stopped working after loading a certain level. I found the the keyboard and mouse would work so I used those, and then I encountered gravity walkways which broke the mouse controls after getting off. Mouse would only work to rotate chatacter while upside down. Ok.. not an issue.. I can still move with WASD. I cannot turn  I can only look in one direction for the remainder of the game now. 

Another note, when you first load into the game it is very poor resolution. That''s because even though the VR scaling is set to 100, it incorrect. You have to set it to 200 to get a normal resolution. 

So all these problems yet I still recommended it? Why? The story is pretty neat, the visuals are nice and the shrinking and growing mechanic is fun to explore the map with. There is decent voice acting and I am interested in seeing how the game ends now. So while it is a hassle to get it working and to play it, as it does not truly support all the VR devices that the developer states on its store page. I bought this game on sale for 86 cents sooo I cannot complain about it. Its worth the cost at that point even with all its problems.'),
	 ('77399960','76561198063363009','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Truly a classic

A one-of-a-kind game that mixes action and puzzle perfectly in it''s own way.

The mechanics are very easy to understand, but as the speed gradually ramps up and more different colors enter the scene as you progress through the game, the more challenging it gets to the point that you almost have to give up thinking and rely on your first instinct to keep those balls away from that accursed skull...
I especially found the last two temples frustrating, but I found it very rewarding the moment I finally beat that last obstacle and cleared the game.

The only downside is the fact that you have to face the same levels again after you beat the 3rd and 6th temple (the only difference is the bigger speed and a new color), but i find that personally a minor detail in the end. 

Overall a must-have for those who like to play fast-paced action-puzzles and for those who love to casually play a game.'),
