	 ('165023456','76561198997312411','3330','20251230',1,1,0,0,0,'Zuma is a PopCap classic unfairly overshadowed by the likes of Peggle and Plants vs Zombies. This thing is constantly dirt cheap and it''s an insanely good value for the number of hours you''re liable to get out of it (my estimate''s about twenty hours higher than it should be because I left my PC on with Zuma running overnight once or twice, but still: crazy value).

My only criticism is that the low resolution doesn''t play nice with Steam notifications. In something like Peggle it''s not so big a deal, but Zuma is built on the premise of an aggressively approaching deadline, and a popup telling you that someone just launched No Man''s Sky for the thirtieth time in a row because they''re struggling to run it on Linux can easily kill a run because it covers a quarter of your screen and blots out the positions of half the balls in play. But that''s not so big a deal if you disable notifications or just unfriend people who insist on running Linux despite clearly not having a firm enough understanding of it to do so.'),
