	 ('47791284','76561197973530934','234710','20251230',4,2,0,0,5,'They should rename this to "Bad Beat Simulator".  If you are in the market for a poker game, this isn''t the one you''re looking for.  Sure there are some poker-like elements to this game but you will find that you will have to wade through a lot of "chuff" to get to the intended material.  Even then, when you do get to the poker aspect of the game, the game will mercilessly punish you with one inexplicable bad beat after another.  

I tested this - after a bad beat, I ALT+F4''ed out of the game and ''restarted'' from where I left off.  Sure enough, the game dutifully served yet another bad beat just to make sure I knew what game I was playing.  Did this maybe 10+ times before I realized the game had ultimately decided I was going to lose this match.

Other elements of the game are well done.  The characters are well represented and engaging.  The dialogue is fun and immersive as can be.  However, the banter quickly becomes repetitive and can be an annoying hinderance when all you want to do is play some cards without suffering through a series of conversations before you are dealt the next card.

Perhaps it''s a good thing you can''t purchase this anymore.'),
