	 ('198546592','76561198122307857','2427430','20251230',1,1,0,0,9,'Arguably the best standalone S.T.A.L.K.E.R game in the series. 

Certainly the best game mechanically with a ton of new features added from the first game - things like repairing gear, overhauled artifact hunting making it more immersive & fun, improved side quests, improved exploration of the world to some extent with lots of open ended buildings and places to find that actually have interesting things to find (one time I found an abandoned cave with a mutant in it who killed another S.T.A.L.K.E.R which led into a whole questline), improved gunplay and much more. 

I''d still put Shadow of Chernobyl as my favourite because of it''s story & atmosphere, but I don''t think anyone would fault you for having this as your favourite. Clear Sky is the worst game i''ve ever played so I won''t even talk about it. 

9/10'),
