	 ('115866881','76561197972136158','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'It''s not a great poker game. If you want to play *poker* there are tons of better poker games out there. The gameplay is slow and frequently slowed down even more by the sometimes long conversations the characters have with each other that you can''t skip. All of which are fun the FIRST time you hear them, but it gets repetitive after a while. Plus I have serious questions about the RNG and the fairness of the AI. It seems like the AI knows the strength of my hand and adjusts to it. It also seems like the AI pulls off a highly improbable lucky win way too often for it to be totally random.

The only reliable way to win is to play extremely conservatively, let them knock each other out and win going all in with an unbeatable hand against the last player. Don''t try to bluff the AI, they rarely go for it, don''t bet big unless you have a really great hand, and if you do have a really great hand, expect them to fold. As if they somehow know. They know when you''re bluffing and they know when your hand beats theirs. Especially Ash, it seems. Never re-raise Ash. If you have a full house, he has a better full house. If you have a pair of kings, he has a pair of aces. If you have a straight, he has a higher straight.

All that being said though, that''s not why you''re playing the game. You''re playing the game to "hang out" with the cast of characters. Heck yeah I want to play poker with a bunch of licensed game characters with GLaDOS as the dealer... And it is a lot of fun until it gets stale, and it does get stale, but it''s fun for a few hours. Just don''t expect the worlds greatest poker experience.'),
