	 ('70318226','76561198022298572','244070','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'This game is old--so it is cheap.  I stumbled upon it by accident and decided to give it a go.  I play tabletop Wings of Glory WW 1 and this seemed a close computer simulation.  I was not wrong.  This game is fun, engaging and would be extremely entertaining if not for the continual end of mission game crashes.  I saw others had reviewed this game poorly due to ongoing crashes, but decided to give it a go anyway. 

What I have discovered is the game plays through a scenario and then it kicks you out of the game.  You go back in and it lets you play through the same or a similar scenario and upon completion you can advance--if you survived the mission for a second time.  Save the game.  Play the next mission--the kicked out.  Load saved game, play through to completion, and then save.  Etc.  Frustrating but a fun beer and pretzels game.  My daughters found it fun that I was able to name female World War 1 pilots (because that totally happened) after them.  They periodically stopped in to check on "their" progress and were delighted as they received promotions and upgrades.

Make no mistake--this is an old, glitch filled game that leads to a lot of frustration.  It is also a fun filled experience that allows you to escape into a World War 1 fantasy world that is not dangerous and allows you to shoot zepplins for a mere few bucks.'),
