	 ('174862923','76561197999481997','3009850','20251230',4,1,0,0,0,'10 years since I touched one of these and MDickie is still making straight trash.

The controls are broken (pressing the right stick is not Use, it''s Pause), the camerawork is sloppy, you have full customization over your character''s looks and if you choose to use this you''ll be constantly accosted for breaking the rules of the prison (Impersonation) and get into a fight every time you try to go change, and gameplay is constantly interrupted by other characters walking up to you and threatening you, apologizing to you, selling you things, or asking you for favors. I spend more time getting accosted by NPCs than I do controlling my character and playing the game.

I know most reviews for this thing are positive because it''s "so bad it''s good," but in my experience it''s just bad enough to be bad.'),
	 ('175575496','76561198259928404','3009850','20251230',23,9,0,0,0,'MDickie fan here. Mat PLEASE TURN DOWN THE AMOUNT OF NPC INTERACTION. I CANNOT FUCKING BREATHE IN THIS PRISON WITHOUT SOME SINGLE CELLED INTELLIGENCE ASKING ME TO DO RANDOM SHIT OR COMMENTING ON ME EXISTING. 

Sometimes it also feels like this game despises you for being alive, and will sick every single NPC on you in existence if you so much as brush against someone else. It''s a fantastic game if you want to be inspired to perform a spree killing in real life in that regard.

Legitimately this is the most insane negative feedback loop I''ve ever witnessed in a piece of digital entertainment. It''s like the game hates you for wanting to play it. Whatever you''re doing stop it because an NPC needs to talk to you for 5 uninterrupted seconds. And the 5 seconds wouldn''t be that bad if it didn''t happen 10 times a minute depending on how many NPCs are in the room.

Oh god don''t even try to fight anyone. The NPCs have a tendency to crowd around you and get in your way, then stop you again for another unskippable dialogue box to ask why you''d attack them when they WALKED INTO MY SHOVEL.

Like legit just do not play the game. Play the first one it''s free. Hell, you could also play the 2D  one, which is also on steam. Either version has about half of the interruptions this game has.

Are you sick of me bringing up how often the NPCs randomly stop you to talk? Imagine how much I hate dealing with the NPCs making me STOP what I''m doing to jabber some nonsense directly to my face every 30 seconds. It''s asinine. Genuinely unplayable at times because I''ll get into a fight, someone will decide to make it their business, then the NPC I''m attacking will remind me that I need to deliver a pipe to the yard at 07:00 hours, then I''ll hit them again and the sirens will blare informing the station that I am wanted for assault now, then I''ll try to finish the job but someone will come up and tell me that choke masterson is a good friend of theirs and they''re gonna get involved, then an ally shows up and lets me know that they''re gonna help me deal with masterson, then my character loses his fucking mind in sync with my real actual mind breaking from how little I am allowed to do in this game, then I get grabbed and my character is given the death penalty or beaten with sticks or whatever.

That''s every single second of this entire game. It does not stop being like this. MDickie desperately needs to make an "Events" slider or something in the options that lets me turn down the god damn NPC dialogue frequency because this shit is intolerable.'),
