	 ('195355230','76561197970569079','2427430','20251230',4,0,0,0,10,'Yeah, yeah, there are some edits. But a lot of stuff still remains. I''m not so beholden to the little Soviet things here and there that were removed that I''ll make a stink about it. Big whoop. I love the atmosphere of the games and am overjoyed that all three run well on handheld PCs of which I''m playing on an OLED Deck and Claw 8. There are some technical issues, to which I would say, welcome to STALKER, but hopefully these things can be ironed out with a few patches.

If you''re one of those weird snowflakes who cry about "woke" changes being made in a VIDEO GAME, imagine if you made a celebrated game under the yoke of an oppressive regime that years later your country gains independence from, shortly after which, said oppressive regime attempts to wrest back control of your country, plunging your world into years of war, killing at least one of your coworkers in the process, and probably some friends and family. I can understand why they wanted to make some changes, and I fully accept it. No skin off my back. Can''t accept these changes? Well, the originals still exist. 

I love STALKER and love that the Enhanced Editions allow even more people to play one of the most atmospheric series ever made. I hope it does well for GSC and that GSC and STALKER may continue for many more years to come.

Good hunting!'),
