	 ('95092607','76561198090633441','1302780','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'Zombo Buster Advance is a Tower Defense game with a twist (that you can change the position of the units once they''ve been put down)... it''s fun, kinda short if you don''t go for all the achievements (but if you do the time played can be 3 to 4 times as long- 34 hrs for me first play through to completion... still kinda short....).

The units are self explanatory, if you choose to play this game you will have your favorites but be aware that to get all 93 achievements you need to play with just about every unit (thus the 34 hrs).  The obstacles are interesting and there are a number of interesting zombies.

Several problems with the game...
Game is short and ...
there is no extra endgame sequence, there is a short little "still video... thingy" at the end... and then nothing
The Zombies and the Units and the areas all have their best unit deployment but they don''t really have any clues as to which one that will be... you''ve pretty much have to go with trial by error to figure it out....
The upgrades for units was interesting but eventually feels really grindy and it was weird that I didnt have every character leveled up at the end...
replayabillity

Still, this is far from a complete failure and is a fun if a tad short and not really all that re-playable.... It could have an interesting sequel...  so I will give it a positive.
