	 ('145338567','76561198153145805','3330','20251230',23,2,0,0,0,'I am so mad that I have found this game on Steam.

As a guy in my teens/early 20''s, I used to play this game ALL THE TIME on my piece of crap laptop. I would furiously conquer level after level, trying always to get better combos, more gap-shots, and complete levels faster and faster. I don''t know how much time I sunk into doing this stupid game, so the fact that I''ve got pulled back in once again is insane.

This is an easy buy. You''re a little frog in the middle who spits marbles and trails of marbles going around you. You try to match 3, which clears those marbles. You try to do "bonus" things like shooting marbles in between gaps or clearing out large numbers of marbles at the same time. It''s really not that complicated... it''s just about as simple as it looks.

But I''m telling you, it''s addicting. It really is. Before you realize what''s going on, you''ll be sucked in and won''t want to stop.

This game is SUPER old, so you could probably run it on your microwave. No need to worry about laptop specs. 

You will find yourself furiously trying to survive as the levels get more and more difficult. Do you have what it takes!? 

ZUMA!!!!!!!!!!'),
	 ('11774709','76561197972631789','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,6,'It''s well done. But there''s too much talking during the game. It keeps trying to be funny all the time, turns out to be really annoying (believe me) because there''s no option to skip those long conversation sequences. 

I wish there was an option to make them shut up or something.'),
	 ('183497262','76561198877239297','3009850','20251230',2,1,0,0,8,'This game should''ve won goty'),
	 ('123156817','76561198051708512','584640','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'So I''ll say this game is good, but with the caveat that you have to be able to put up with some nonsense.
Core gameplay works well and it''s unique enough to stick out in other auto runners. I also like the boss fights quite a bit. 
The story is funny enough to keep going. Kinda generic anime tropes used for comedic effect. It works.
I also really like the challenges, I almost wish that was the whole game honestly.
So the negative,
Many of the upgrades/weapons feel extremely useless. Some are clear upgrades on others but then it feels like a downgrade afterwards? Some are good only really for bosses but that''s fine ultimately. I think a lot of the middle weapons kinda get stuck in they aren''t really better than the previous ones. There''s like 2 abilities and 3 weapons out of the 16 total upgrades I think are actually useful. Even then the best weapon has this weird ability where it''s a near screen clear but sometimes enemies just happen to sneak past it?
The random generation can be extremely annoying though. It has a habit of sometimes creating seemingly impossible combinations due to putting some enemies too close to one another or too many of the same ones in quick succession. In the story it''s annoying but ultimately not too bad, but Endless mode is where the cracks of the generation really begin to show. I think there''s very few viable loadouts for endless mode which is a shame.
Overall I had fun with it, I wouldn''t of put 12 hours in it if I didn''t. Though probably about 4 was fighting endless mode because of the previously mentioned things.
I recommend it if you don''t do the endless mode!'),
