	 ('12045384','76561198044395191','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Usually when a game seems too good to be true, it is. You aren''t going to pay much for this game and thats okay. Poker Night 2  has an awesome cast of characters: for those who actually know who the characters are. This game is both comedic and fun. I don''t know what its like to play this game without knowing any of the cast but even if that was the case a portion of the comedy stands on it''s own without having to understand a reference. The cel-shaded art style is done very well and allows for characters from a cartoon/ a live action film to fit in visually without seeming weird. The length of this game''s fun is based on how much you enjoy the characters and playing poker with them. Eventually the jokes will repeat but it still creates a nice atmosphere for your standard poker night.You will also recieve hats in tf2 and items for Borderlands 2 for doing certain things. Poker is fun to most and when actual money isn''t on the line the only gamble you''ll have to take is whether or not you buy this game: which would be a full house.'),
	 ('195317689','76561197972369460','2427430','20251230',92,2,0,0,0,'At its core, its just stalker:Call of Pripyat with a slightly different coat of paint. If you don''t own a copy of the game I would recommend the original, on GOG - Why? Well after a short return to the zone let me give you my thoughts, and the things I noticed that were different between the original and the enhanced edition.

Firstly its basically the same, some meager graphical enhancements and modern graphic options but barely noticable except for water effects. By default the game has motion blur and depth of field JACKED UP making everything pointlessly blurry, and the DoP is ass backwards for some reason when aiming down sights - making it pretty stupid, you literally ADS to  have a harder time aiming so turn those two off asap.

By default the ''camera shake'' is off, but this doesnt refer to your camera getting shaken when you get hit or blown up, this means head bob which if you played the originals is really annoying and stupid so this is a quality of life improvement I can approve of. On the flip side, they introduce absoltely horrendous ''combat music'' that should be immediately turned off, and the dynamic sound is broken makes your own foot steps sound like someone is ten feet behind you, turn that off too.

Now for the changes that were not about improving the game, and a part of me thinks its the real reason they squeezed out a enhanced edition with so little overall effort put into it: The original took place way before the current ukraine/russia war and the games had a lot of russian names, references and even the currency was russian. This version replaces all that when possible with a ukrainian equivilant and from what I understand, outright removed russian localization which is kinda bonkers to me, I have never gotten along with russian gamers but at the end of the day they are just that, gamers - they are not putin and punishing them is just petty.'),
