	 ('54495453','76561198060415320','1086030','20251230',41,0,0,0,10,'This review isn''t one I''ve been looking forward to, but I still feel obligated to write it.

Normally, I like what Dharker Studios puts out. Not love, like. Negligee was good enough, and Negligee: Love Stories was fantastic. The idea of a game exploring Emily''s personality more really caught my interest. Don''t get me wrong, the writing''s great, and my main purpose in buying it was satisfied. She''s a great character, and the one created to explore her, Miley, is given a nice amount of depth for the short time we''ve known her. The sprites and CGs, like practically anything Kopianget does, is stunningly beautiful and more than enough incentive for 100% completion.

That said, I sadly can''t say that, as it is now, I can recommend this game. One reason is that there''s an extra charge for the adult content. I can understand continuing the patch system for such things given Steam''s ambiguous enforcement of its content policy, but not making that patch a free option feels cheap and underhanded, even given the game''s lower-than-usual price. The other reason I can''t recommend this game is because it has a very unpolished feel. The icon is the standard Ren''Py project icon rather than a custom one, which for a studio like Dharker feels like a cut corner too many. In lots of the scenes, the music doesn''t match the feel of the scene, and triggers at odd moments.

There''s lots of room for improvement, and if I see these changes made, I''d be more than happy to change my vote. At the moment, though, I recommend against buying this game.'),
	 ('102510678','76561198110074010','73190','20251230',13,1,0,0,10,'[b]I strongly do not recommend this game[/b] - you''ll lose both your time and nerves, no matter how much you would like the concept of potential of the game. This game had huge potential. But it is botched in so many ways, that it is just not worth it. Maybe only if you plan to develop similar game, go check it out.

I have several pages of things that I dislike about Pride of Nations, here are few most important of them:
- wait time between turns - on my i5-6600K running at 4.7 GHz, this game capable running on just 1 core is taking 3-6 minutes to calculate 1 single turn in the early game (was about a minute in the very beginning, year 1850). In 50+ hours in this game I''ve been able to progress from year 1850 to 1856. Campaign ends in 1920. Okay, I was doing other stuff about half the time, as you are not able to do anything in the game during the wait time. But even if you can accept that you play a turn, then do other stuff in your real or virtual life, the game is still not worth it because the list only begins:
- crashes - game crashed to desktop many times without apparent reason
- clunky UI - mouse movement is delayed, map scrolling with mouse is a nightmare, drag & drop system is very inconsistent especially with moving and merging units and there are UI elements which were not implemented in the game - like message importance or loans + many other issues with the UI
- dis-balanced overcomplexity with incomplete manual or tooltips - I''ve read the whole manual of the game, all the guides and I still did not understood why some options are missing to me, or why I cannot do.  Or issues like militancy being described as a huge issue, when I have it at max level in all my national regions, without a real way to lower it and without any negative effects from that.. etc. etc.
- missing any ledgers or easy ways to view known/important information about the world, other countries etc.
- historical/geographical non-senses despite the game aiming to be very historically accurate - like region Slowakei without any Slovak population, or region with Troppau (Opava) without any Czech population.. and many other..
- messy messages - there are way too many messages each turn to read all, with no priority levels, and no filter on which are relevant to your nation.

So sorry to say that, but this game was my biggest dissapointment, also because of high hopes and some really enthusiastic reviews I''ve seen on the web. And because I love games on world maps, especially grand strategies. And because it has so many great mechanics and so much potential...  [strike]And it might not take too much to fix it in my eyes..  [/strike] no sorry, it is unfixable without great effort.. I was just typing out list of easy fixes, but many of them are not easy, and yes there are many of them and just the code optimization is not feasible to make it at least 10x faster to be playable. And even 10x shorter waiting times are still too long, so... 

I would love to see someone take concept of this game and maybe mix it with Victoria 2, let multiple historical start dates be available and ideally make it possible to play until modern era of 21st century. That would be a fantastic game to play.
'),
	 ('24112560','76561198185970946','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Ok, I will say this once cause it is totally true! Excellent game that brings the childhood back. This game is so f***ing awesome. I remember when I used to play it in school, my computing teacher let us to play it when we had finished, this and other games, but this was special because besides I played it with my friends I also competed with them to see who was the fastest. The game didn''t save up so we had to start from the beginning, but so easy the first levels. In my house I downloaded it and started to play, I was almost a whole Saturday, and reached the third temple in a very little time, obviusly I died but I never gave up. When I realized it was in Steam I put in mind to save and buy it in a near future. And now I am here playing it and remebering my childhood. This game was the inspiration that gave me to become a gamer, this was the exact game that made me to realize how much I like games and play them. Is this type of games that looks so easy to play but when you keep moving and moving forward and trough the game, the difficulty increases and so your experience and cognitive coordination of hand-eye and viceversa. I highly recommend this game to those new gamers, this turns into an addiction believe me. Until you don''t finish it ou won''t leave it and that happened to me, Unfortunately a virus ruined my computer and I couldn''t keep playing but I still remember perfectly well this game, all the stages and the final level (which I passed only once and at the first try) and the tricks to beat it. You will never get bored of it! I assure you. I thank my teacher to show me this game and to PopCap to bring it to life, excellent work. The mentioned before made me into what I am today, a dedicated gamer that loves videogames and to play them with my bros.'),
