	 ('67535828','76561198027474775','500670','20251230',2,1,0,0,0,'DooM for the poor, that is what I think when I play this game.

[h1]Story[/h1]

A nice and well behaved girl travels to a planet full of demons and creatures alike so she can have a nice chat with them and show them her weapons and how they fire.

[h1]Gameplay[/h1]

TxP is an Arena/twin stick shooter with the simplest of ideas: to kill demons, one weapon two modes, multiple demons to kill and lots of blood and bad language. Gameplay is frantic, fast paced giving you no time to rest, bosses are easy and at the same time hard to kill while you are chased by other enemies. There are not any other things to say to be honest, it is generic but very fun and it will keep you wanting for more just to see where you can get as difficulty increases over time.

[h1]Graphics[/h1]

Very 80''s/90''s arcade like graphics, pixel art style, appealing to the eye, especially for those who grew up with such style.

[h1]Sound and Music[/h1]

Musically TxP offers some interesting tracks that sync with the chaos of the game, it could have had some extreme riffs to 
match the bloody and gory destruction. 

As for sounds, the game is full of different effects that represent the slaughter of demons and punishment we deliver with every shot and combo, demons grunt and feel indescribable pain, blood splatters and guts explode, cool stuff.

[h1]The Bad[/h1]

TxP does little to explain how combos work, actually I had to check some steam guides to see if there were any combos or upgrades at all, in fact there are and these trigger on how we kill demons, the "how to play" is short and misses a chance to detail the gameplay further.

Also, it is a sad and missed opportunity that TxP doesn''t offer some more extreme music, some killer thrash/death riffs or death metal would have added the feeling of total destruction and carnage, even if they have a couple of tracks that loop would have been great, the game''s setting asks for something brutal.

For the most part the game is great, however the absolute chaos will usually make you lose sight of the main character, the bloody floor, guts and demonic remains will be your worst enemy, seeing among the corpses and gore will give you a hard time.

[h1]Conclusion[/h1]

In short periods TxP delivers a fun time, it will constantly make me come back for some quick slaughter, it is obscene, violent, gory, over the top and satisfying. It doesn''t have any other mode so that''s why I play only for a bit, play some death metal from your own playlist and you are all set to begin the butchering of demons. DooM for the poor if you don''t have the money.'),
