	 ('2459503','76561198007665656','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'TLDR: Aside from the very good dialogue, it''s just not fun. Play Poker Night (1) instead.  
  
I bought this game because it was supposed to be fun like the first game & feature new & improved dialogue with the iconic characters. And the dialogue is indeed improved, much less repitition, with some nice touches like their ability to call or check whilst speaking.  

Unfortunately, that''s about the only good thing I have to say about PN2. People can (and have) argued about the difficulty all day long, but since this is _my_ reco I''m gonna say that the odds are definitely rigged; this is nothing like actual poker based (at least in part) on the odds of drawing cards, &  instead becomes mini games of handing out drinks to debilitate the other players &  working the AI the way they want you to.  No matter what the hand you have, no matter what kind of bluff you pose, the AI will beat it, it isn''t true odds, frankly it''s bullshit. You can never truly replicate the excitement from bluffing real people, but at least in PN1 it was based on chance & it was fun. I can''t stress how shitty it feels to lose hand after hand to fake odds, or to have all-ins at every inopportune moment, and to have all the ai fold no matter what bluff / non bluff strategy you employ.  

As good as the dialogue is, it is now unskippable, it slows down the hands, & when someone leaves the table, expect to wait as much as 30+ seconds for the next hand to start. This makes the frustrating games/ hands even more regrettable.  

If Telltale games makes another Poker Night, I wouldn''t buy it.  I thought this would be fun, relaxing, & might improve my poker skills a bit. Aside from the dialogue here and there, I ain''t enjoying this one bit.'),
