	 ('41836992','76561198022567106','234710','20251230',3,0,0,0,9,'Digital poker is generally a fast game: once you''ve decided what to do with your hand, the round is essentially over. Unlike real life, there''s no value in watching the AI deliberate. 

This game, however, chooses to drag out the proceedings, with lots of little one-line quips from each character as they take their actions - one liners that soon become repetitive.

Just so we''re clear: this game lingers over the least interesting part of digital poker, which most other poker games simply skip, in order to give you repetitive, not-quite-witty one-liners over and over.

It''s not a game. It''s torture. GladOS wins!'),
