	 ('191353427','76561199100463542','3330','20251230',1,2,0,0,10,'Zuma Deluxe has a bland and mostly uninteresting artstyle, the levels rarely feel distinct from each other, and the difficulty is artificially inflated. Starting a level out with the spheres immediately halfway across the level isn''t challenging in any meaningful way, especially when you have levels like Zumaic Exodus where the level starts right by the frog and spirals out to the edge of the screen. Meanwhile, Zuma''s Revenge may have these problems to an extent, but they''re not as bad and that game still manages to be a consistently enjoyable experience with 60 unique levels as well as boss fights that are pretty fun, instead of a near-identical set of three worlds copy-pasted four times. What I''m trying to say is, there is pretty much no reason to play Zuma Deluxe over Zuma''s Revenge.'),
