	 ('115068134','76561198043472327','1197770','20251230',2,0,0,0,10,'I upvoted this at first, but after playing some more, I just can''t any more. I really wanted to, because the number of 3D non-visual-novel-style naughty games can be counted on one hand, but.. With that price point I couldn''t recommend it to anyone. Maybe at a third or fourth of the price.

It''s babies first game, but in adult
Missing collision maps even for stuff in focus (there''s a sword early on you''re meant to get, the stump it leans on can be walked through, for example), shoddy modelling (a guy early on was supposed to be tied to two posts.. but the model just held its arms out, no bindings or anything), wocky framerate, missing animations (character talks but the model just stands there emotionless and motionless)..
It''s like someone made a first draft/proof of concept of the game and then decided "well good enough" and released it without any quality control at all for a higher price than some of the best indie games.
This is a game in alpha stage. No, not even beta, in beta, at least collission maps for foreground objects would be fixed.

the voice acting is pretty good tho. At least at the places it does have it which seem kinda random.

I still kinda like it but that is absolutely not worth full price.
It might be if it was actually made with any sort of care, but it wasn''t. I''d love to call this a passion project with flaws, but when basic stuff is missing in even in the very first level, you can tell that the passion was quite limited and the moneys was probably the main driving focus.'),
