	 ('86339802','76561197989690212','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I played this so often as a Flash game 10+ years ago that when I saw it going on Steam for £0.84 I had to get it. I am glad to say that it is still as addictive now as it was back then. I don''t know if it has much lastability these days but if I only get a few hours of fun out of it, it will be worth the purchase. I can always come back to it after another break (and it probably will be less than 10 years this time!).

By the way, I play on Ubuntu Linux 18.04 with compatibility layer on an old laptop with graphics acceleration enabled without any problems. Graphics acceleration improved the graphics a lot without much slow down (a little slow down wouldn''t bother me anyway - it might even help ;-) ). The only thing that caused a problem with a lot of slow down is enabling graphics acceleration AND custom cursors in the options. Without custom cursors it works fine.'),
	 ('85802609','76561199119534414','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,8,'Its good, mindless fun.'),
	 ('43616722','76561198051511128','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I love this game. I used to be a pretty hardcore poker player and the game isn''t much of a challenge, if you don''t play too many levels above. But if you''re looking for a casual few games of poker, instead of just playing on a lifeless table or online room, you get this neat little environment where the characters you know and love feel really interesting. I haven''t played enough to know for sure but it seems like the play styles even match the characters. Claptrap is loose aggressive, Brock is a smart all rounder, Jack is tight aggressive and the max is just kinda tight. Having Glados as the dealer is pure genuis as well. I have genuinely laughed at quite a few moments in the game, for example heads up against Claptrap with 7/2 offsuit I called all in preflop and Glados says "I have scanned millions of hands from tournaments and cannot find another example of someone making this play."

If you like poker at all this is a really fun experience if you''re in the mood to casually throw around some cards. If you know the characters it''s even better. Very impressed with Poker Night 2 and recommend it whole heartedly.'),
