	 ('59317861','76561197998761337','500670','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'Priced well for what it is, Tormentor X Punisher is a solid twin-stick shooter. That said, there''s not a -ton- of content in the game. Each session is pretty short (as intended) and gets frantic quick. There are several interesting bosses, each of which appear at random with a brief intro before throwing you back into the chaos. The standard enemy roster is pretty reserved, but considering the rapid pace of the gameplay, I think that''s for the best. 

While you''ll only ever be dealing with two weapons--the titular Tormentor (a machine gun) and Punisher (a shotgun)--there are some -very- novel ways you can use both of them. For example, the last round in each mag of Tormentor leaves a fire trail and Punisher can be used to reflect projectiles. The game is good about rewarding you for figuring these out too; providing you with buffs if you can pull these maneuvers off multiple times in a run.

The music is decent, the sound effects are VERY punchy, and the voice acting is suitably over-the-top. Has a good sense of humor too.

The only real complaint I have is the camera shake. While you can tone it down, you can''t turn it off, so if you have any sort of motion sensitivity, I can see that being a big issue, especially in some of the larger/later fights.

All up, solid. Not amazing, but I''ve enjoyed my time with it.'),
