	 ('175410659','76561197998877524','3009850','20251230',15,3,0,0,0,'as a dutiful purchaser of mdickie goods, this one kind of sucks. this is by far the most barren and dull game mr. dickie has made in a while - the prison gameplay is hugely bland an uninteresting, with little to no interesting content provided for you to do, not even a schedule, etc. instead, you''re left to make your own fun, which is problematic because nearly everything makes you acquire a Wanted status, and that status does Not go away until you are either arrested or killed. if you''re arrested and manage to beat your case, a mechanic that''s been around since the first Hard Time, the cop will hate you and endlessly hound you. in my first playthrough i beat a bunch of cases (most of which were things like "arrived at cell late" or "not following orders," although the orders i was supposed to follow were extremely arcane) and ended up with a cell block full of cops who would just outright try and murder me as soon as i walked into the room, and although that''s kind of funny in concept, it renders the game totally unplayable really fast. 

if you go all-out and just try to do stuff like escape or kill those pesky guards, you''ll find that there is no fulfillment there, either - guards seemingly refuse to die or suffer any permanent consequences from your actions (in one occasion i killed a guard, then he showed up the next day, and then i cut his arm off, and his arm was back on his body after reloading the zone. why bother?), and escaping leads to an empty open world that mostly is populated by cops who will instantly arrest you. it really just isn''t fun, which is too bad because the original Hard Time feels so much more intricate and engaging than this despite being freeware! i had some similar gripes with old school, but Hard Time 3 just feels so unrealized and i hope it gets some updates because as it stands it really lacks a backbone'),
