	 ('71073568','76561198200089955','3330','20251230',7,5,0,0,8,'Zuma Deluxe is one of those games that''s considered classic, but aged like milk.
Its gameplay is monotonous, lacks development and gets boring pretty fast. That is when you play until the Stage 9.
At Stage 9, it gets even worse — your success becomes less dependent on skill and more dependent on the ball spawn RNG. As a result, you''ll have to repeat it over and over until you get lucky enough — all while suffering through the gameplay that you''re already sick of.
After coming to a conclusion I no longer wish to beat this game in a fair way, but still wish to see the ending, I cheated — edited the "levels.xml" file to decrease the ball amount and their movement speed for Stage 9. But when I proceeded further, I got even more disappointed. Turns out, Stages 10, 11 & 12 just copy-paste the Stages 7, 8 & 9 respectively — same levels, same mechanics, nothing new except for even harder "ball amount and speed" settings. So if you think you can suffer through the Stage 9 and then get relieved — abandon all hope.
I expected much more from the company that made the legendary "Plants vs. Zombies" title. I strongly advice against purchasing this game, even on sale.'),
