	 ('74959712','76561198135517275','3330','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'When I was a child, around the age of 4-5, my parents were working tons and usually left me with my grandparents, usually, they just stuck me on the laptop to play games, one day, my granddad was checking for cheap CD-ROM games at a ''Macro'', and stumbled across a game called ''Zuma Deluxe'', I tried it, and died on 1-2. I then got so scared that I would only watch my granddad play it, he could only get to around stage 5-5, This occurred for around 5-6 years until I finally decided to give it a shot again, and lo and behold, I managed to get to stage 6. 

I got so excited I got my Nan to call my Granddad at work about it, He was proud of me, I was elated. Time passed, I grinded the game for hours and hours, my highest stage was stage 8. I was stuck, and now I wasn''t going around my grandparents nearly as much, I had found new games, new consoles to play, new things to do.

Even still, I continued, Getting the sequel and completing it before I even completed the original,  I persevered, I followed through, I managed to get it on the family mac, and finally, after around 7-8 years of playing, i beat it when i was around 12 or 13, I was so happy, so proud.

But as I completed it, I forget about it for a time, before my father picked it up, maybe it was a way to connect with me, maybe he was having fun, but once again, I watched, I observed, But this time, I helped, I Guided, He managed to get to stage 8, I was proud of him.

A few years later after that, I ended up seeing this game on steam on sale for around 1 quid, I bought it without hesitation and began the grind once more, Reliving what once made me so happy, but sooner or later I felt a feeling of... dissatisfaction? discontentment? I felt like it was so much better, bigger than it actually was, i thought it was just my nostalgia talking again, I put the game down once more after putting around 15 hours into it,

It quietly sat in my steam library, being ignored once again for better, bigger games. But sometimes I felt like playing it, like enjoying it once like when I was a kid.

A few years later, around 2023, I get a girlfriend, shes very similar to me, still probably is, and she noticed this in my library, she wanted to play it, I let her, and she played for hours on end, grinding it when I was at work to make me proud, and I was, and once again, I was in that spot of watching again, of feeling admiration, of joy whenever she won a level, of sadness whenever she got a game over, It was almost like I was a kid again, but this time, genuinely grown up, like i''m truly supporting someone, I once again felt joy, felt like someone was experiencing what I felt all those years ago. 

I still have some of the records she had on here, not wanting to erase that part of history by beating her scores. She only ever got to stage 11. We haven''t talked for a year.

I still come to this game from time to time, whether its nostalgia, training my aim once again, or just wanting to experience it again like I was a child, or an adult, This games been here for me from the very start.

For that, This game has truly become synonymous with me. Godspeed, Sungod and Zuma frog.

As for the game itself, it''s alright I guess, bit short.'),
