	 ('89039735','76561198356967845','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I did not think I would ever be able to edit this review but I am glad I can.  Since Telltale has got back into business they fixed all their old games and I am so glad about it.  this game was legit one of my faves and now I can play it again.  The characters are great and the game play is solid.  If you do not like poker then this game might not be for you BUT if you are at least curious about getting into it then I say go for it.  The AI is about low to medium level and the storytelling just makes it feel great plus the different systems to help you are an amazing detail that makes this game really pop.  

The drinks system
Unlocked after one or two tournaments. You can use your tokens that you win to buy drinks.  These drinks make the AI make some mistakes and even make their tells, will cover next, show more often.  When you learn who should get the drinks and at what point then it gets fun.

The tells system
Each character has a distinct tell that says something about their current hand. Weather it be a scratch to indicate a bluff or not so strong hand to a re-adjustment of their ocular lens to indicate a somewhat strong hand. These tells are here to help you win WAY more often and helps give more life to everyone.  Plus when serving drinks these tells show more often.

The bounty system
Easily the reason you would get this game.  The bounty system shows up around the second game and it gives three challenges that you need to complete to get the bounty opportunity.  After you do all the challenges one of the characters will offer up an item relevant to them and you can win it.  Do not worry if you don''t win it the first time because the next tournament you can try again with a different character and you only win each one time.  In addition to getting a nice trophy in game it gives you an item in other games like Borderlands 2 and Team Fortress 2.

Honestly a 8/10 game for me that I have sunk so long into and will need to get back in to start over that grind to 1 million dollars.'),
