	 ('8386667','76561198000519500','244070','20251230',1,0,0,0,1,'Awesome game! Played it for 4 hours straight on a first install. Graphics are not high quality, but the gameplay does make up for that a lot. This game has got the Sid Meier''s feel of gameplay all over it. A lot of tiny variables you need to account for before making a move. The only thing that bugged me is that there is no option for changing the resolution. The resolution is quite low. I guess that stems from the origin of this game. It was originally created for the iPhone. Apparently changing the resolution may be possible with a config.xml in your User''s appdata folder (C:/Users/[yourusername]/AppData/Local/AcePilot/config.xml). I read that in the description of a youtube screencast here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MdzyFdVxWA4  I did have the folder, but not the xml file. I am too lazy to write something on a trial and error basis or to send an email to the devs, so I am playing it really low res. If the gameplay rocks I do not care about the graphics so for me it is not an issue. I do not know if the devs will implement a possiblity for changing it. I bought the game on sale for €2,50 so it was a cheapy. I bought "Ace Patrol: Pacific Sky" also, but I will play that if I have finished this one. Highly recommended!'),
