	 ('195283794','76561198002816470','2427430','20251230',3,0,0,0,10,'"X-Ray Engine is not responding", The Game.

Just checking graphics and other settings on first launch I crashed twice.
Maxed out graphics @1440p Native FSR, area around Skadovsk and inside has ~140fps and 77 1% low fps, on a 5060Ti, Ryzen 5700X3D, 32gb 4000Mhz CL18 system.

The visuals around Skadovsk don''t look blurry to me, so I don''t know what other reviewers are complaining about really, but I would''ve appreciated MSAA instead of just FXAA. Recommend to just turn off Anti aliasing setting.

Other than that it''s a very terrible "enhancement", the visual enhancements are Reshade tier and the textures look like they were bulk upscaled thru Topaz Gigapixel or something, without any quality control.. The original game runs with ~110 fps more maxed out in the same locations, and most importantly the original didn''t crash 7 times in under an hour.

As an Eastern European, living in a country bordering Russia, I don''t like em''. But what the fuck was the thought process with cutting game content in all 3 games???
Don''t let GSC remake Rocky 4, cuz it''s just easier to hide/delete history than improve on it.

And making the original trilogy more expensive because of this release? Absolutely scummy behavior LOL...

Unless you are a graphics whore or need controller support, the enhanced edition just sucks. Play the original and don''t support GSC, they have severely fallen off in quality since Stalker 2.'),
