	 ('19156072','76561198260039259','386990','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I was completely sold by the idea. Weird and interesting. 

After reading some reviews, I knew I was going to get some pompous writing, but it didn''t really bother me. I was about to get my hands on some romantic poets stuff, so of course there would be some intricate speech; intricate does not mean vacuous, though. And vacuous is all you get most of the time. Line after line of elaborate nothing. You just simply cannot waste so much time around a barren thought. I''m not really asking for more action (which is always nice, but not a must have), but plain coherent dialogue with your expected overdramatic poet statements to spice it up.

As for the characters, they were acceptable. I found Percy Shelley bordering idiocy here and there (and it pissed me off, to be honest), but I liked how the more political aspects of his thought were present. I would have loved more Byron-Shelley moments, but that''s just me. They were ok together. I liked Byron, even though she got tiring. 
I missed some girly Keats in the mix.

Let me tell you that I see nothing wrong with the art. It''s lovely, fitting and there''s nothing really inappropriate about it. 

So, I do recommend the game only if you are crazy enough about your romantic poets. Without that source of unconditional love to back it up, the game does not stand for itself.'),
