	 ('49078268','76561198053606678','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'Fun characters and mechanics, but is lacking in a couple areas. First, the difficulty remains fairly low level with nowhere to go after all the unlocks. In the first game there were settings for how much the characters talked and difficulty. I think these features should have been re implemented in this game. Also animations can be glitchy and dialogue can be repetitive/annoying.
For what the game is, these are fairly trivial complaints. However, there is one major flaw that I can''t get over. 
I used to play Poker Night 2 when I did not really understand poker. The game was perfect then. Now that I understand poker better I often see hands incorrectly called. It has gotten to the point where in each tournament at least two hands are not valued correctly. It seems to happen most often with flushes, however it happens with all types of hands. 
I have had a lot of fun with this game and appreciate it, but I can''t keep playing it. It is too easy to outgrow. I will rate it positively because I had a lot of fun with it, but be wary of its numerous issues.'),
	 ('200678216','76561198076667851','3563710','20251230',5,0,0,0,10,'For $3.00 this game is fun. However, there''s not a lot to do.  You start out with all Iron items unlocked.  Purchasing resources is done by talking to a person outside your shop.  There is no ore to smelt, just ingots you can turn around and make into items.  
Crafting process is very basic (press the space bar when an arrow is in the green part).  

A few quality of life features that would be nice to have: 
Ability to close the shop so you can stock the store - with customers coming in very rapidly, it''s impossible to keep up with the orders.  This makes the weapon/armor shelves useless unfortunately.
Decrease the EXP required to dismiss someone - seems to take 500+ experience to dismiss one person and that''s about half of what you can make in a day (if not more)
Add the ability to see what all customers want instead of just the one in the front of the line.  This would make it easier to bulk smith items.

NOTE: these are obviously just suggestions.  For $3.00 the game is perfectly fine.'),
	 ('7612101','76561197975217935','234710','20251230',34,0,0,0,10,'The Poker Night franchise are really fun poker games, considering poker is not a solitary game you play "by yourself", and for the online poker players this is nice for a change. I enjoy some of the antics from the characters which make for a more genuine "poker with friends" experience. Also, there''s a chance to win items for Team Fortress 2! This game is especially good for novice poker players to get acquainted with how the game is played, and also for the more experience players to just have fun with. 8.5/10'),
	 ('158076513','76561197995957283','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'Zuma was a classic game from Popcap before the dark times (*EA Sports, it''s in the game* plays). Kind of a difficult game to describe, a top-down, precision, puzzle, shooter? Your "launcher" shoots colored orbs at a "train" of differently colored orbs to create 3 or more matches of the color to eliminate them from the track. Once the train reaches the end of the track, you lose and must retry. With a ton of levels, neat power ups, a charming art style, and relaxing music, Zuma is an addictive, blast. If you have played Luxor, then you will enjoy this game. If not, you still might lose track of time playing this.'),
