	 ('29124193','76561197976081787','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'If you are looking for a Poker game with a bit more interaction than Poker Night 2 is definitely that game. It is your average Texas/Omaha Hold ‘em but with characters that have actual personalities. 

There is nothing to say about the actual game mechanics. If you are familiar with the card game, then you know all there is to know about the game. The thing that makes this a different type of card game is that you have 4 opponents that will hold a conversation like in real life card games. Granted you probably never had a talking dog and robots from other worlds play in your card games.

This is the sequel to Poker Night at the Inventory. You have four opponents who have nothing in common having conversations while you play cards. After so many games the conversations will repeat. This is where the game starts to lose a little of its charm. The conversations go from witty, to stupid, all the way to crazy. 

The graphics in the game are pretty well done. They are not top of the line but where needed you can see where they placed great detail. In fact, once you change the theme of each table the room takes on the style of that character’s reality. This will also change up some of the interactions in the game. The only thing I would say is missing is having different characters’ switch in and out.

If you love Texas/Omaha Hold ‘em and want some personality to you game, you definitely need to pick this game up. 
