	 ('11180163','76561198045519076','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,2,'I don''t watch Venture Bros, I''ve never played Sam and Max, or Evil Dead, and I didn''t like Borderlands 2. So basically I just bought it for the poker. The game at first seemed charming but after 45 minutes of play it got stale, the line that were funny, or clever fell flat after I heared them multiple times. I continued playing just for the hell of it, but the game didn''t seem to become any better. In fact, the more I played the worse my luck seemed to get, and the more annoyed I got with the game. I lost multiple all-in hands when I had more than a 90% chance to win, so maybe the game is rigged or maybe just the cosmos hate me.

Overall Poker Night 2 is a fairly meh game with stale repeated dialog, and decent (possibly rigged) poker. That''s all it''s got going for it, dialog and poker, and neither of them are even that good. If you like poker go ahead and buy it, but buy it when it''s on sale.'),
