	 ('31618444','76561198025365699','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'A lot of people bought and played this game specifically for the Team Fortress 2 items that could be unlocked. If that''s your perogative go for it. 

That being said, Poker Night 2 is by all means a great game. It''s poker, so you know what you are getting gameplay wise. The presentation, though, is top notch. Telltale has a nack for creating believable (or at the very least entertaining) characters and this game is no exception. The table banter and character interactions are witty, funny, and just all around enjoyable. Over time some stuff will begin to repeat as is inevitable. But whatever, it''s great.'),
	 ('174817300','76561198060136683','3009850','20251230',8,3,0,0,0,'I''m a huge fan of MDickie games, especially the original hardtime, but I can''t recommend this one.

The original can be summed up as fun chaos. This is chaos, but it''s not fun. There are far too many guards who are absolutely hell bent on arresting you for completely trivial reasons, and with absolutely no warning beforehand. No joke, I got arrested for breaking a bloody chair. 
In the original, if you attacked a guard or an inmate, you were given a warning. In this, you can punch an inmate, and you''ll either get no reaction from anyone, or a blaring alarm announcing you''re wanted for assault. There''s no inbetween.

The even worse thing is, if you commit enough crimes, you''ll get the death sentence (no matter how minor or severe said crime is), which deletes your character permanently with absolutely no warning. You''ll have to make them all over again. In this way, the game effectively prohibits you from trying out the things that makes it fun, like escaping the prison and going on a rampage. I don''t want to try these things because I don''t want to waste my time making another character.

There are issues that others have outlined, like the cramped prison environment and horrid camera controls, but I can live with the former, and the latter is just a feature of MDickie games at this point, so I''m used to it.

If Matt sorts the wanted system out, then I''ll give this a recommend. But for now, it''s just not a very fun game.
'),
