	 ('59878736','76561198086280526','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'This is a complete and total waste of time. In other words, it''s EXCELLENT fun. It''s a perfect game for when you just want to wind down for an hour or two and not have to think too much.

I''m surprised that Steam shows me as having played for only 18 hours. I know that this is understated because I often played it offline on the train on the way home from work (back when I had time for that), where wireless coverage is patchy at best. I''d estimate that my total time played would be at least double the value shown. Why does that matter?

Because it means that I''ve heard a lot of the funnies more than once, though admittedly it''s been over a fair length of time. I bought the game back in April 2016 and have played it on and off since then. Still, while they may not cause an out loud laugh any more, they still raise a smile.

The gameplay? I would not call myself a master poker player but I''ve played several poker games (electronic and not) over the years and while the game is limited to only two variants of poker I find that it emulates the real thing pretty effectively.

Sadly Telltale Games hit the wall in late 2018, so there will probably never be a Poker Night 3. That''s disappointing, but I still plan to get a lot more mileage out of this one for as long as Windows will continue to run it.'),
