	 ('109204019','76561198025823574','3330','20251230',2,0,0,0,1,'One of the best in its genre, a real classic. I played it a lot in my childhood, so it was nice to finally buy it and play it.

First of all, the game has a gigantic difficulty spike around stage 10-11. Other reviews mention stage 8 or 9 as breaking points, for me personally that was still fine. 

During the game I collected I think 20 extra lives. In stage 10, I lost 9 in 3 levels. 
I finished the game (after earning another 2) with 3. Three.

RNG rules the last stages - the line curves back onto itself, blocking shots. There''s been examples of not getting a colour to hit a slow-combo for about 20 shots. The colour variety, and speed of the balls make sure to add up the difficulty and make your mistakes pile up extremely fast.   Fail the same level 4-5 times, then do it finally well under half of the ace time.

I write a negative review to point out this issue. Other reviews mention a high framerate problem, which makes the game run too fast, hence the difficulty - maybe one could limit the framerate through GPU''s program.  But as the game is out of the box, it needs cautionary reviews because the difficulty spike. If you''re okay with that, just buy it. 

(Though seems like it doesn''t run on Mac, despite the requirements. Check old negative reviews)'),
	 ('200689164','76561197970136793','3411440','20251230',6,0,0,0,9,'its cool but could do with some single player bots and some good ones to with a system of how hard you want the cpu to be like easy medium hard and expert etc'),
	 ('28389879','76561198119842810','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,8,'some notes:

Ash will ALWAYS be the first to go all-in. If he makes it passed the first three rounds without busting out then he''s decided to actually play, in which case I would leave the table. 

Brock is an argo player that likes to ride a bluff with moderate raises. 

Sam is the most sensible player of the mix. He''ll play it safe and is usually the last one at the table.

Clap-trap is the wild card who is also looking for the attention and acceptance of the group. He''ll bet sensibly, but if everyone is going all-in, then you can bet that he''ll buckle under the peer pressure and go all in too.'),
	 ('131133276','76561199012426165','3330','20251230',0,0,0,0,8,'please free me from these temples'),
	 ('9691973','76561197976467743','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Thoroughly enjoyable! This game is great after a couple of beverages, on a lonely night. Feels like sitting around with a few friends, only these friends are Brock frikkin'' Samson and Ash! I have to admit how sad I was not to hear Bruce Campbell''s quips, but the voice actor they used did well, none the less.
They created a great atmosphere with this one as even though the characters talk and jibe, it''s rarely annoying.
With so many lines of dialogue, the longevity of this game is extended. I must admit to only expecting a few back and forths, but I feel they really went all out.
The poker side of things is fun, trying to suss out your opponents. I found myself, on more than one occasion, trying to read their tells and listen for bluffs... tried and failed (at least they couldn''t see MY lousy poker face).
There is the sad note however, that there is no multiplayer. Perhaps we''ll see it in a future version?
Anyways, right price, lots of fun, do yourself a favour and have a crack at it.
You''re going to giggle, I promise.'),
