	 ('200390855','76561197997170332','2427430','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'Of all the original S.T.A.L.K.E.R. trilogy games Call of Pripyat/Prypiat is the most refined.
While I do recommend the other entries, I admit they are marginal for various reasons.
This entry is still solid 15 years later and completed it will give you some background lore that makes S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2 Heart of Chernobyl even more interesting.

Some of the voice acting near the end of the game is pretty awful.
But other than that it plays well. 
It has much less of the aggravation that Clear Sky had.  
Most missions aren''t bugged (1 often is , but it wont stop you from moving forward...but you''ll need to work around it if you want to get all the achievements.)
Unlike the original Shadow of Chernobyl you can upgrade weapons and armor and can repair them.

A Solid thumbs up'),
	 ('176734529','76561198336762948','3009850','20251230',7,0,0,0,0,'Within 10 minutes of downloading this game and starting it for the first time, I
 - Created a new character with a customisable shirt
 - Was sentenced to 28 days prison for ''self-indulgence''
 - Was immediately told off by a guard for wearing a different prison outfit, and given a warning
 - Became wanted for committing ''insubordination'' and was mercilessly gunned down by officers, before being arrested
 - Went back to court and was given a warning for disobeying the authorities
 - Was sent back to my prison block, and given a ''warning'' by the arresting officer to change my shirt
 - Was immediately told off by a different officer for wearing a different prison outfit again
 - Became wanted again for committing ''insubordination'', and was almost beaten to death by the prison officers.

Just your average experience from an MDickie game. I do recommend toggling the ''arrest'' button in the settings from ''strict'' to ''moderate'' or ''lenient'', so you won''t be arrested as much for crimes that aren''t your fault. And don''t underestimate the power of a water soaker gun as a weapon, either - it is extremely effective against annoying inmates and officers.

10/10 gameplay, would become a wanted insubordinist any day of the week.'),
