	 ('101135183','76561198063406575','1410000','20251230',1,0,0,0,7,'I so wanted to like this game. I''d been looking for a fun VR parachute sim of some description and was hopeful this was it. Ignoring the couple of "don''t recommend" reviews, I decided to give it a go anyway. I''m glad I did, as I know it''s not for me now. Issues I ran into:

- The settings dialog shows up sideways for some reason; making it hard to read the settings and hard to change them.
- Calibration is a little confusing, but made sense in the end. But...
- ...the tutorial seems to totally ignore the calibration. "Chest height" is above my head in the tutorial. O_o
- The skydiving part... perhaps it''s just me, but it makes no sense. The tutorial doesn''t really describe what you''re doing, how or why, and doing all sorts of things with my hands doesn''t really seem to make an difference. This isn''t helped by the fact that the target rings appear below and *behind* and there doesn''t seem to be a way of turning around to head for them.
- In actual jumps, the calibration does seem to work, but the same issues with how freefall works (or doesn''t) are there too. All I seem to be able to do is fall straight down until I open the chute, or it opens itself.
- The graphics are... not very convincing. Buildings are just textured blocks, often clipping into each other in ways that make no sense. Sure, I get that this isn''t what the game is about, and I''d totally accept this sort of thing in a flight sim (for example), where you''re normally 1,000s of feet in the air; but this game is about being close to the ground a lot. You want it to look good when you smash into a building.
- The BASE jump I tried... you''re in a lift and jump out of that. That''s it. I was expecting to at least be on the roof of a building or something.
- Even if you turn the music 100% off, you still have to listen to it in the BASE jump and it''s stupidly loud.

I see the kernel of a great little sim here. I wanted to like this so much, and I can see many elements of something I wanted. But, really, I''m so sorry, I can''t recommend this. Perhaps if/when it gets a lot more polish?'),
