	 ('142499224','76561197975672153','234710','20251230',2,2,0,0,9,'This game in one word.... Insulting.

Every time you play a game with some sort of "random algorithm" there is constantly a debate these days about how it works.  Is it actually randomly based.  Do odds shift to favor certain things in certain moments or is the game fair.  Let''s say at best, this game can be a test field for the process and give the developers an inside look into tweaking the numbers.  When you get down to 2 players, the cards go to crap.  First hand of every game is usually ok.  Etc.  There is always going to be a single good card (usually an ace) with trash next to it just to get you to go into the pot.  It''s a weird issue and only something you experience with today''s poker "randomness" compared to playing in person.  

Let''s say for a typical hand you have a B grade opening pair of cards.  Low pair of cards or an Ace with something that is the same suit.  Then you go into the flop and a solid 85-95% of the time it''s absolutely trash.  I seriously feel like pot size, number of players, or bet size plays a role into how the cards fall.  It''s a weird issue.  It''s hard to describe, but I cannot help but "feel the algorithm" when it comes to the gameplay.

Now, when we talk about why the game is insulting it''s the overall design choice.  This may have been an issue with the first version as well, but I just don''t recall.  The main issue is that when the player does anything in the game the AI dialog is such that it berates you.  Often.  When you''re skipping through long dialog and trying to enjoy the game, there isn''t idle chatter, it''s a constant stream of the game telling me "you''re an idiot" or something along those lines.

Think about it.  The main line/joke in the game is as follows.

"It''s playing video game poker by itself Sam, it doesn''t have any friends."  

How would you feel playing a game that constantly said this kind of crap to you each time you played?'),
