	 ('195075288','76561199801965062','3009850','20251230',16,3,0,0,10,'10/10

I was sentenced 20 days for drug dealing. Being a complete underdog ( lowest strength, popularity, height, etc.. ) I was anticipating a tough time. To my surprise I had two handfuls of friends within a few days and it seemed like everything was going fine until I met.... <3 Jester <3 We instantly fell in love and wherever I went, he followed. Since I had joined the gang Sure Shot, so did he and quickly rose to become our leader. 

We seemed unstoppable until the 13th day. I was wandering the cell block, when I fell to the ground screaming. A terrible death cry erupted from.. um, me and some kind of humanoid named Nicholas Jester ripped its way out of my body. I lie there helpless, as my newborn sun lets out a klingon battle cry and rampages down the cell block with EVERY SINGLE INMATE following him. As I pull myself together and crawl to my cell, I hear a massive battle behind me and when I turn to look I see what can only be described as a cartoon dogpile of human bodies and fighting sounds...

I see Jester the next day and he thanks me for birthing his son and tells me that he will always be there if I need anything. He keeps pestering me about taking leadership of Sure Shot but I can''t stop thinking about my son. I long for a chapel in this prison, so I could at least take solace there..

Throughout my sentence I had made so many friends that it was reduced down to 18 days. 

On day 19, the guard who I call "papa smurf" stopped me at the stairs and said I was "too productive" to lose, so they were giving me 2 more days... I pass the time, in my posh north block upper floor cell, lifting weights and sleeping. 2 days pass and another guard pulls the same crap, as I''m about to get to the office door... On day 24, just as the buzzer rings, a nice guard who I had befriended previously, asked me if I wanted an escort out of prison and now it is day 25.

Prison does things to a person... I have somehow gained 50 lbs of pure muscle and I look like a complete freak!! At least I am free and I know that my son, Nicholas Jester lives in town somewhere. I plan to venture out into the dangerous, animal filled world to find him today ( and work off some of this muscle mass!! ).

I play a lot of games, specifically looking for games that have actual "life" in them. MDickey has created exactly this. I can''t think of many other games where the NPC''s actually feel alive. I have since purchased every possible MDickey product on steam and am very excited for the next title! If you are still on the fence, I suggest one of the 2d hard time or school games, or if you want a truly awesome experience; The You Testament!

I almost forgot, there is wrestling in these games! The way it all works is really smooth and extremely fun!!!

Cheers and <3 <3 <3 MDickey <3 <3 <3'),
