	 ('62823924','76561197961635679','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,0,'Not for sale anymore anyway, but worth excoriating. The original Poker Night at the Inventory was a fun and funny single player card game. Poker Night 2 is the exact opposite. The dialogue from characters is repetitive and unskippable, leaving you stuck listening to stupid shit that someone who is now unemployed thought was a genius two minutes worth of dialogue. The AI is psychotic (I can''t count the number of games that started with 3 characters going all-in on the first hand). The RNG is stupidly weighted against the player (over and over again, multiple hands in a row where the AI has a 5% chance to win suddenly swing their way on river cards back-to-back-to-back-to-back). And the entire game struggles and groans under TTG''s terrible, out-of-date engine, where even the menu screen lags, making it faster to kill the game in task manager than to cycle through multiple screens just to get to the main menu to quit.'),
