	 ('29774500','76561197961555382','513320','20251230',5,1,0,0,10,'Not what it seems. Amazing demo videos. VR motion sickness gameplay. Walk around with your thumb, they said. It will be fun, they said... Little did I know, I was in for a room-scale no-clip / off-centered clipping adventure where my boundaries were outside the ship... and half in the walls. Wow, you would think they would have fixed some of the issues with this game, or at least tested it with the vive before roomscale was supported. I have asked for a refund... we''ll see.'),
	 ('134215531','76561198048786585','73190','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I''d recommend this game only to a certain rare type of gamer--the kind with a great deal of patience and a love of history (especially this period of history). This is not a game to just pick up and play casually. It requires study (beginning with a close reading of the manual, but not ending there, since not everything is in the manual). It also requires a big time commitment (say a couple years to complete the full campaign). And then it requires attentive, methodical play. There are shorter scenarios that could be enjoyed with less effort, but the game system shines in campaign mode, playing on the world map. Frankly, I bit off more than I could chew when I bought this game. I''m impressed with it; it''s a real gem. But I may never play it again. I''m just not the right kind of gamer for it and don''t have enough time. I''d still heartily recommend it, though, with the above caveats, even though it has some flaws and was never developed to its full potential.'),
