	 ('19309562','76561198097209819','234710','20251230',1,0,0,0,10,'Good enough for getting unique Borderlands 2 unlocks but it gets old FAST.
This is one of those games that deserve a neutral rating but Steam doesn''t have that so I''ll go with positive, just barely.

- The repetitive unskippable dialogue makes playing the game for any length of time infuriating. It may be fun to listen to the characters'' blabbering the first time around but when you hear the same long-winded story that interrupts the flow of the game for the third time in a short play session, it''s not so fun anymore.
- The fact that the AI breaks just about every rule of probability and statistics doesn''t help either. They will do suicidal stuff like going all the way through a high stakes round with nothing but a ten high if they know the flop, turn and river will be stacked in their favour, but will often back out of even the smallest raise if they know you''re going to win.
Even if you fold every suboptimal hand and only play the good ones, the AI will have a better hand [i]suspiciously[/i] often. When you see that they''re willing to go all in with nothing but an unsuited 7-2 with no pairs on the table it tempts you to take risks and call, but when you''re involved in the showdown the turn and river will just magically happen to be two sevens, beating your suited Q-J which you thought was a strong enough hand to keep playing (of course this doesn''t happen ALL the time but it''s much more common than it should be if the cards were dealt randomly). Oh and then you get a full minute of unskippable dialogue which you''ve heard fifteen times before so you can cry before the next hand is dealt.

If you''re getting this for the BL2 skins, those are easy enough to get. Trying to somewhat consistently win after that is just going to frustrate you to no end.'),
