	 ('10277588','76561197995951257','234710','20251230',2,0,0,0,10,'Great design, fun time in poker... but filled with annoyances.

All the characters talk too much! It''s one thing to have some level of small talk by your favorite characters... I mean, that''s why I bought the game! Initial raise gets you a reaction comment. If you all-in, you get 5+ gasp reactions from the group, even if they''ve folded previously, then they''ll fold 80% of the time, then you''ll get a ''player win'' or ''player loss'' razzing from GlaDOS and whomever won or lost. Also, Sam might be playing, but Max constantly interjects... and I hate those two from the first game. The dealer randomly tosses insults you as you are dealt cards, reraise, win or lose hands... and it''s almost always Claptrap at the showdown, so anyone who hates him will hate him on a 1-on-1 level.

The rewards system sucks! Original Poker Night would give you the ''reward'' after you knocked out the one player w/ the item. This one has you complete 3 "challenges" to get a shot at a bounty, then you have to knock out all 4 players. One of the challenges is "Spend 8 perfect tournament''s worth of tokens to unlock the Portal set" so those challenges aren''t fluff either. There''s no reset for them aside from deleting your save. Some folks on the Steam Forums say they have been stuck for over a year on same challenge. 

Even if you were magic, you''d have to do 10+ perfect games to get the unlocks... and they''re time consuming! Until the blinds are 800/1600, these guys fold neatly on most raises like a pair of pleated pants. Oh, and despite having a SHiFT account and Borderlands 2 installed, none of the Borderlands stuff unlocked natively and I had to submit a SHiFT ticket with Gearbox. TF2 stuff unlocks W/O any hitches, as is the norm.

The game looks pretty. I hate to badmouth it... but I bought the game because I liked the characters and wanted the unlocks. Spending a ton of hours to get the unlocks, when I''d rather be in B2 or TF2, and starting to hate the characters I liked before I started playing... honestly made me very unhappy.'),
