	 ('59411234','76561197970638376','1197770','20251230',22,0,0,0,0,'Where to start....  The artwork is well done.  Private areas actually enter areas instead of usual clipping through areas.  The voice acting is phenominal especially the protagonist.  The game play is linear with not much of a guiding story line to make you not realize how linear the game actually is.  The maps have some clipping issues with the character, but I haven''t fallen through the map yet, so that''s good.  You will get armor but I think it''s only for visual purposes because the demons still hurt you the same way.  The bad guys I think are on a timer and then they just pop into battle.  The demons pop in, you kill them and they pop out with no death animation.  The game kind of feels unfinished in some ways by a technical standard.  The controls feel a bit off (feels delayed) but manageable.  "Positions" are scripted throughout the game.

The game is good for what it is, but it sure could use some quality control to make it that much better.  I''d recommend this game if you don''t over-hype yourself by looking at the visuals because there are some flaws, but if you don''t what you are getting into it''s not so bad.'),
