	 ('174826650','76561197994415196','3009850','20251230',0,0,0,0,0,'Sentenced to do hard time of 25 days for climate change. Get RPG-ed the second I enter Cell Block West. Wake up in hospital without my left arm. Fueled with revenge, I take to the yard. Throw basket balls in the hoop to increase my overall stats. Lift weights so I can instill my revenge. Befriend guards, and the doctor to get access to painkillers and steroids. Become the strongest one-armed in prison. Get tasked by a cop to make a tunnel in the cafeteria. Digging by night. Oh sweet freedom only to be run over by gradmna in going need for speed in a police car. I get arrested not for escaping but for animal abuse as a dog died from me being hit by the car landing on the poor dog. Sentenced to 30 days in prison. 
Back in prison fall in love with the very person that shot the RPG. Find knife. Meet him in the bathroom. Stab till I see Red.
Arrested for murder. Death sentence....

11/9 - would shit myself again'),
	 ('33318301','76561198109097495','386990','20251230',0,0,0,0,5,'I bought this game during the Steam Summer Sale, having had this on my wishlist for some time.
I was not disappointed in the story line and the themes that were discussed in the game were depressing (but still enjoyed).

Pros:
+ Artwork was beautiful, and outfits reflected characters personality.
+ Dialogue reflected each character.
+ Options to skip/speed up text through sections.
+ Extras included with the game (inspriation and artwork).
+ Deals with different forms of illness in a somewhat realistic way.

Cons:
- Shorter than expected.
- Some of the conversations between characters can get annoying.
- Music throughout the entire game (it was nice at points).
- No voices for the characters (would have been nice).'),
