	 ('126748490','76561197967971065','500670','20251230',1,0,0,0,2,'A furious bullet hell where the game says the quiet part loud, and the loud part louder. A nonsensical Augenblick studio style opening is all you need for backstory to slay demons by the hundreds. The charm is in the clever simplistic design of a single level and a fire/reload mechanic so simple yet so tight, you''ll be sniffing out the combos for hours. And if you accomplish these combos enough you''ll upgrade your weapon in that run. The bosses are menacing but just as easy to kill as any other enemy (provided you know how) and they often leave a bit of themselves behind as a stage hazard, ramping up the difficulty every minute. The heavy metal ramps with the difficulty too and you''ll be head banging as you coat the stage in gore. A must play for any bullethell or arcade shooter enthusiast that loves unapologetic shittalk and heavy metal.'),
