Pros:  Not many

Cons: 
1) Not Bruce Campbell.  Not even a good fake.  I could fake Ash Williams better than that.  (I have a quality "groovy!")  Pathetic since I''m sure Bruce would have worked for loose change and the for fun of it - especially when this game was being made.

2) The poker is terrible.  The opponents are all maniacs.  It''s like playing against someone who has never played poker but who has watched a lot of movies where poker is played.  Everyone makes huge bets all of the time and the blinds are ridiculously huge.  Plus, it feels like the RNG cheats - but it''s probably just the irritation of having to play against the kind of dweebs who go all in before the flop with trash cards.

3) The banter is pretty fun - the first time.  They just didn''t put even remotely enough effort into it.  I really don''t understand this part.  If Telltale didn''t put a lot of effort into the poker AI and they didn''t put a lot of effort into recording dialog, then what exactly do they expect us to pay them for?  It''s not even like one of their point and click adventures with a TON of art - just the same few loops over and over.  I really really like the stupid crap that these idiot poker characters mumble but there should be a LOT more of it.

If Telltale had fixed any of the things above, then it would have been a fun game.  Same thing is true for the first game (tho the poker might actually be slightly better in that one).  Or they could have added multiplayer and let you spout the same three lines at other real humans...for hours at a time...while playing actual poker.  That would be hilarious.

Anyway...I''m going to go back to pointlessly flinging fake money at Claptrap.  But you...you still have a chance.  This is a positive review but that doesn''t mean you have to play the game.  Just...don''t do it.'),
