	 ('195515074','76561198060817984','2427640','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'If you like Jenga  and tetris youll like this game. Its jenga in reverse but tetris rules. Let me explain:
The main campaign is a series of challenges where in you build skyscrapers to various heights.
Very easy at first but has a progressive difficulty curve. You have to build to a certain height, but you only get
certain pieces, each piece has a height, shape and price. Think box, L shape, pyramid and so on.
So build to 500m with X$. If you fail, the building topples or you just dont get to the height, so you cant just build as you wish. Im currently stuck on #9. There are also 10 additional challenges plus 2 side projects(your choice, mild or hard). 
You unlock each level as you go by. Total being about 22. If you do all of the challenges, you get the option to reset and start from zero again. The music is also very good. Its all electronica with a good vibes.
As you build you see the cute little workers milling about and jumping out of the way as each piece is flown in via helicopter. I recommend it. Its fun, its constructive, especially in the world of indie games saturated with side-scrolling platforms, early access, PvP, open world and so on and so on.

'),
