	 ('59451579','76561199007994241','1197770','20251230',0,0,0,0,2,'Well, it''s one of the best games of this type on Steam so far.
That said, there''s not really much competition either, but the art, humor and voice acting make it entertaining.
Currently in this game you''ll encounter: 
*Decent voice acting (mostly). However the recording quality could be better, and I kept wishing you could click to skip through the lines when I was forced to go through them again sometimes.
*There''s 1 background music loop that can''t be turned off in menu -_-
*Decent looking game world although some of the characters can look a bit low rent (and you can sometimes see body parts clipping through clothes and boots)
*The animations/interactions aren''t bad when the game gets to the part that is the reason you are thinking about buying this, however there was one sequence with obvious clipping, and a few sequences where motion/sound would go way out of sync
*Running around you''ll be colliding with a lot of things you didn''t expect to be solid
*And clipping through things that you''d expect to be solid
*The DoF is making me feel like I forgot to put on my glasses unless camera is right behind Lilly.
*Gear is largely meaningless in terms of game mechanics (in whatever sense you can say there are any game mechanics)
*Leveling up is largely meaningless
*Animations during combat are very rudimentary (enemies mostly appear out of thin air, and when they die they just flop over)
*Movement is generally just clunky and level design is sometimes lazy. In one place I went to explore behind a building and somehow I started walking up an invisible slope, got teleported to the other side of a long bridge I had just crossed. The bridge itself was so crappy I''d constantly bump into edges and wondered if I''d fall off.
*Getting kinda stuck in dialogue after NPC interaction, although temporarily
*Recycled voice acting making some sequences unneccessarily long winded and boring
*Combat is very tedious, and the only real risk of losing comes down to chance, or carelessness. Again there''s no real mechanics or any skill/tactic involved, rather just spam heal potion sometimes, because when you do die, it''s going to be from said combat mechanics being rubbish
*It was never when facing big enemies though, those were easy, it was some random mob that kept popping out of nowhere before I''d realized how tedious dying would be, so I just made sure that I wouldn''t again by occasionally spamming a few health potions (which you will end up with a large surplus of anyway)
*When I died in this way, I discovered my game hadn''t saved. I guess I didn''t kiss the fairy long enough? While the save system is amusing, the poor save system makes dying/going through combat&dialogues even more tedious (although that rarely happens because combat sequences are quite dull and predictable) 
*Running back past some areas, will re-trigger dialogue that you''ve already been through, although you can often skip it
*Some parts of the UI are bugged (like the "distract" move will sometimes actually trigger a heal potion unless you give it an extra tap)

There''s very little actual "game" to be had. I wish they''d either made it actually fun, or just less tedious to deal with, other than for the sake of making a very short game seem longer than it actually is. 
Running around looking for the chest and encountering demons randomly popping out of nowwere, I found myself wishing I could just skip the whole thing just so I could get on with the story.
There''s a bit of humor and I did play through it.
That being said, that took less than 6hrs when not particularly rushing it, and lot of it was very obviously just designed to drag it out.
Is it even supposed to end like that? I honestly don''t even know if that''s the actual end or if it''s bugged and stuck.

There were moments where it had humor and charm, and Lilly sometimes has funny voice acting, but overall it feels rather lazy and sloppily cobbled together.
It''s fun enough I played through it, and not too pricey though, so it''s worth looking at - especially if the devs improved some of the above since I played this early after launch.
I changed my review from negative to positive, just don''t expect too much more than a short, naughty and humorous romp.'),
