	 ('159595094','76561198194987990','513320','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Started out weird, but kinda OK.  Some clunky stuff, some really neat stuff.

Then, about halfway through (based on a youtube playthrough), I found myself throwing apples at targets, and somehow ended up on this roller-coaster sorta path -- black path, with orange arrows -- that twisted and turned upside-down and sideways and branched off and branched off.

I must''ve spent half an hour trying to find some way to get off, but it was incredibly complex, and disorienting, and intersection after intersection after intersection, and I never could find my way back.

This is one of those games that is "sectioned off" -- you can wander around freely for a while, as long as you don''t stray too far away, but every once in a while, when you go through an arch, or a doorway, or cross oper a bridge, or ..., you find that the path behind you is blocked, and you can only move forward.  I think this is why I couldn''t just "go back" and pick up from the point before I entered the maze (and AFAIK there is only one save slot, so I couldn''t just start from a save point like forty-five minutes earlier).

Uninstalled and never looked back.  Kinduva shame, ''cuz it was just starting to get interesting.  Only spent $.79, but I really was hoping to spend a few more hours and have a satisfying conclusion; as it is, I feel like someone cheated me out of part of my life.

Played on a middle-of-the-road PC, with no VR headset (3GB VRAM), and experienced absolutely ZERO glitches, or errors, bug, or technical issues of any kind ...'),
