	 ('197498147','76561198066938128','2427430','20251230',5,0,0,0,10,'Disclaimer: The ''enhanced'' editions kind of suck. They''re not the worst, but there really wasn''t much improvement over the original. This version crashed the most for me out of the three. This review is about the game itself.

Review: Call of Prypiat is by far the most balanced, least annoying, best voice acted, and overall a pretty well thought out experience. It takes a lot of the mechanics introduced in Clear Sky and makes them actually enjoyable and interesting. Hunting for artifacts is much more fun, especially with the svarog. They made a more compact map, that actually isn''t painful to traverse with a lot of unique locations and anomalies to explore. Enemies have balance and are much less likely to one shot you, especially at higher levels with upgraded armor. The upgrade system is great, it adds a lot of depth and progression and allows you to rely less on finding/buying attachments. The characters are more interactive than SoC, and the quest lines are vibrant and very rewarding.

With CoP, it feels like they struck a good balance of the old hardcore survival of SoC, with a new story and mechanics. It definitely feels easier than the previous ones, but with how weak and fragile the Clear Sky protagonist was and how unfun it was to die of bleeding out after falling off a 1 inch step, I don''t think its a bad thing!'),
