	 ('9248844','76561198003233840','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Best dollar I''ve ever spent. This review is coming from someone that is formally a Poker virgin. 
Poker Night 2 is great for beginners & newbies of Texas holdem and Omaha holdem. Veterans/Professional players may want to avoid this game, since it''s too simplistic for practice play (unless you''re interested in the Borderlands 2 and TF2 exclusive items).
The instructions (playrules/general guidelines) are a little vague; so I suggest you do a little bit of reading and youtubing on the internet before you start out this game.  Once you are familiar with the basics, playing this game would be relatively a breeze.
My only complaints are as follow: 
1. There is no multiplayer. 
2. The algorithm is also somewhat unpredictable and unrealistic(?). You could have an excellent hand in the start and lose out completely; due your opponent- sheer 1% luck near the finals or showdowns.  

Overall, yes do buy this game on sale if you are interested in starting out on Poker but are too introverted to do so with friends or in a casino in Vegas.'),
