	 ('113049396','76561198112819846','1785320','20251230',5,0,0,0,0,'It''s a good thing I got this game on sale. I can''t believe it''s not in early access because that''s exactly what the status should be. Dead No-Head is a low-budget third person shooter that is clearly made by a very small indie developer. There is no voice acting, you just read text. There are invisible walls, trees floating off the ground, texture pop-in, frame rate issues, clipping through mountain walls, branches inside bushes can block bullets, you constantly get stuck on just about everything in the environment, and you can even fall out of a map like what happened to me. Bugs aside, the gameplay can get downright frustrating. Enemies rush you fast, so you are constantly running backwards trying to shoot them while they are dodging your shots and then you end up getting stuck in an area and killed easily. There is no manual save and checkpoints are FAR away, so you end up repeating the same lengthy sections over and over again. There is also no map or inventory to manage and you cannot loot bodies because they disappear after you kill them. Many enemies will also stand around and let you shoot them dead if you don''t get too close. The platforming sections are especially frustrating because you must jump then press the sprint key in mid-air. And there are numerous platform jumps to make in this game. Also, if you remap WSAD to the arrow keys, you must still press W to climb up ledges. You also cannot crouch so there really is no good way to sneak up on enemies. I finally gave up on like my third attempt through a set of traps after dying and having to repeat the same lengthy prior combat section only to fall through the map inside a cave to some area out the forest/swamps again and I was not able to get back. In my opinion, this game is CLEARLY not ready and should be placed in early access until some major issues are addressed. I cannot recommend this game at all.'),
