	 ('107497795','76561198002069169','386990','20251230',11,0,0,0,9,'Such a pretty game, but such a dark topic. Asphyxia deals with depression and suicide, so those suffering with poor mental health may wish to avoid this VN until they feel somewhat better. Ebi-hime as usual manages to marry nice visuals with a murky subject, this time it''s friendships between gender-swapped 18th century British authors who''re turned into teen girls going on a field trip. Sounds weird but it really works lol.

The topics covered in Asphyxia can be covered rather flippantly but this is largely due to whichever character is discussing them. You''ll see things like people sick of someone who is always "sad" or "being dramatic", often closely followed by a solid bit of empathy from another character. This is...well I''d say it''s a different sort of VN but truthfully if you''ve dealt with depression before much of what you''ll see within mirrors how people online tend to treat you.

Achievement hunters, you''re looking at roughly 4 hours per story arc with 13-ish hours to completion if you''re a slow reader like I am, closer to 10 if you''re not. There were a couple minor grammar errors when I last played but the game has been updated twice in the time since so they''re likely resolved.

Solid recommend, it''s a decent buy at the current list price but this has been bundled before and tends to go on sale often so waiting wouldn''t hurt.'),
