	 ('195776596','76561198281025441','2427430','20251230',3,0,0,0,10,'S.T.A.L.K.E.R.: Enhanced Edition is, in my opinion, a well-executed visual upgrade tailored for long-time fans and curious newcomers alike. If you already own the original trilogy or are looking to dive into the Zone for the first time — this is a solid opportunity.

🔧 [h3]What’s new?[/h3]
The update mainly brings reworked textures and skyboxes, giving the visuals a modern feel suited for today’s displays. Thankfully, the game runs smoothly even on mid-range systems — no heavy requirements here.

📜 [h3]Story & Gameplay[/h3]
The story and core mechanics remain unchanged — and honestly, that’s a good thing. These are still the classic games we remember, now wrapped in a fresh coat of polish. The developers were transparent about this being a remaster, not a remake — so expectations should be adjusted accordingly.

🧠 [h3]On the criticism of bad reviev bombing[/h3]
I’ve seen some negative reviews, but they often come from people unfamiliar with how game development works — or perhaps from those with misguided expectations. Some even feel like they were written out of [b]"resentment"[/b] rather than insight. 
[code]Or there is a direct assumption that it is to order for a reward.[/code]

🎁 [h3]Free update[/h3]
Let’s not overlook the fact that all three games Enhanced Edition received this visual update and brand-new achievements — completely free of charge. That’s a rare and generous gesture from the devs, and they deserve our appreciation for it!

🌌 [h3]More than a shooter[/h3]
To newcomers: this isn’t just an First Person Shouter. It’s a narrative journey through a hauntingly beautiful disaster — where the Zone itself feels like the true protagonist. A metaphor for human error, wrapped in surreal atmosphere.

[hr][/hr]

✅ [h3]Final thoughts:[/h3]
Highly recommended to all S.T.A.L.K.E.R. fans and anyone seeking to explore one of the most atmospheric game worlds ever created!'),
