	 ('9620643','76561198103736506','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,8,'Normally I think video poker is boring, but just for the dialouge alone, even without the rewards for TF2 and Borderlands 2 make it awesome! After a while, you get bored of hearing the same lines of dialouge which you once found funny, but now find repetitive, so just for that it would have been nice to have a button to skip dialouge, however otherwise it is an awesome game!  One more problem is with the rewards. Players have reported having issues with unlocking the unlocks for Borderlands 2 and TF2. I personally have only had issues with every single Borderlands 2 unlock.'),
	 ('7797794','76561197997636604','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'This game is fun, for what it is. The main focus here is a little less on the actual poker (although despite not being an avid poker player it seems like it has solid enough gameplay), and more on the writing and character interactions. So if you''re a fan of the characters in the game, or Telltale''s writing in general, it''s worth getting (especially on sale) just for the fun character interactions. There are some genuinely funny moments, and I have a thing for silly crossovers, so I definitely felt entertained.

That being said, as a poker game I''m guessing there''s probably better choices out there. If I wasn''t playing for the dialogue and characters I probably would''ve been a little disappointed. The game''s purely single player, which means you''re always playing against AIs with particular, pre-programmed personalities (one character tends to bluff a lot and go all in, one is more cautious, etc). It''s not nearly as exciting as playing against a real person would be, whether you''re playing through a video game or in person. You learn (or look up) the tells and behaviors of each character and then you get a feel for when it''s best to bet or pass. Once you unlock everything, you''ll have probably heard most, if not all of the conversations (many of them more times than you''d like) and then you''ll be ready to put the game aside for a while. I got to that point after playing about 11 hours.

I do feel like the game''s worthwhile overall, since I went into it specifically for the character interaction (with some fun poker on the side). So if that''s what you want, and especially if you pick it up on sale, it''s not a bad purchase. But if you''re looking for a really hardcore, solid poker game, there''s probably a better one available elsewhere.'),
	 ('94535491','76561198001627386','1197770','20251230',2,0,0,0,8,'Silly fun but does require a little skill. For what it is, it''s a well thought out game.'),
	 ('9892098','76561197987097488','234710','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I am a fan of the first Poker Night game due to the content it contains with the characters you play with that when I heard this game came out, I was excited.... until I heard that Claptrap and Brock Sampson were in the game. Don''t get me wrong, I like Brock Sampson but I kinda felt it''s a bit weird for a Adult Swim character to appear in the game instead of say either another valve or telltale characeter. Claptrap, on the other hand, I hated alot from borderlands. Thankfully I can say the game is just as and probably even better than the first game. Even the character issues I have were thankfully proven wrong. The game offers 2 modes, Texas Hold Em or Omaha and there are even more dialogues for the game to have. There''s even main Conversations depending on the character. I''d say it''s worth the moeny to pick the game up. Especially since the game is known to go on sale for a dollar'),
	 ('156978450','76561198099654008','840930','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'So this is not my first Adamvision game and I rolled into it with pretty high expectations for how fun the game would be after loving Diamo XL and Ding Dong XL.  This game definitely met those expectations.  I love that this game doesn''t pretend to be something it''s not.  It''s a true arcade-style games meant to be replayed endlessly, and it''s easy to burn an hour trying to max your PB but at the same time, easy to play for a few minutes and step away from.  The mechanics are simple and picked up in seconds, the game does have a fun-frustration to it if you''re an achievement hunter like me or just shooting for a PB, and it isn''t easily mastered.  I genuinely think this game is perfect at what it is and does.

If you''re like me and you grew up with arcade-style games and score-chasers, I''d strongly recommend you buy not just Bing Bong XL, but the entire Bundle of what this dev has built over the years.  I''ll update my review if I find a stinker, but at this point, I''d be deeply surprised if I did.'),
