	 ('182554767','76561198272092134','3110820','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'I kind of knew what I was getting when I watched the game’s trailer, and it starts with the main character failing to jump on a platform. Like… it’s so bad that I honestly can’t believe this is in the trailer. Still, I like Megaman and wanted to give it a try. Why? Because it was cheap, and I got it for sale even cheaper.

I’ll be honest, there are only three things I can say I really like about this game:

1: I like the main character’s design. I have no idea what her name is, but that’s a whole other issue. 

2: I like the music. I don’t think it’s 10 out of 10 perfect, but I enjoyed it. Clearly, there was a decent amount of effort put in. I like it more than some Megaman soundtracks.

3: The controls feel good. I like jumping around and like the dash jumps feel good.

Everything else isn’t good or just bad. 

Level design feels nonsensical with layouts that make no sense to me.

The art comes off as someone who doesn’t understand pixel art but wasn’t going to let that stop them from making the game. 

The game is buggy. I could only use the start button to progress forward on my controller during cutscenes, but that ended up skipping the cutscenes. So don’t even ask me about the story. I had no choice but to skip it. I also only beat three bosses on normal difficulty, somehow got to the credits, then the game crashed on me. I… have no idea what happened. I was going to keep the game, but a game crash twenty minutes is enough to tell me it''s not worth it.

I gave this review more time than the amount of time I played the game. The bad more than outweighs the good. I really hope they make a second game that keeps the good and throws away the bad, but as it stands… It''s not great.'),
