	 ('50726101','76561198126525466','386990','20251230',3,0,0,0,2,'The art is beautiful and so is the writing style, but each and every character proves themselves to be utterly unlikable. Their treatment of the main character''s depression is bitingly harsh to often unnecessary degrees. It''s almost as if they don''t realize that constantly insulting someone who''s clinically depressed is only going to make their condition worse.

There are some great things about this game, the art style being the best, but I simply can''t recommend it to those who have suffered through depression or have someone in their life who has. This game presents a mindset - even if it doesn''t mean to - that''s extremely harmful.

(Edit [spoilers]: Now that I''ve played the game''s "bad end," Suicide''s Argument, I just want to adjust an earlier statement and say that Georgia is the only character who treats Samantha''s condition with even a modicum of respect and gives some of the best advice in the game... And then it''s treated like fact that Samantha will never be able to take that advice or get better. Like recovery somehow doesn''t exist.)'),
