	 ('40044254','76561198017975705','244070','20251230',0,0,0,0,9,'On the plus side it is a fun little game that is oddly addictive with a sense of satisfaction when you successfully out think your enemy and manage to position yourself for a truly devestating attack. The campaign chugs along over the course of about two hours and provided you don''t think TOO hard about the history it does hold together.

On the down side it can be as buggy as the underside of a rotting log. There is a nasty habit of crashing at the end of a mission which is annoying enough, except for completely illogical reasons the game then forces you to start a new campaign and redo the first tute mission before it will let you access the save game menu.

This is... well... MILDLY ANNOYING. Crashes mostly seem to happen on completing a mission and clicking the ''next'' button, but pressing the ''reply'' to re-watch the last mission as a quick video does seem to make the game a tad more stable. Or maybe I just finally got lucky.

I like this game but be warned, it seems to be very moody with crashing.

So if you want a quick, relatively simple game of air to air combat? Success

If you have better things to do in your life then replay the sodding start tute mission AGAIN cause someone is too lazy to support the game with a quarter decent patch? Avoid'),
	 ('76804825','76561197993531522','1302780','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'Well to my mind, it''s the best lane tower defense game after Plants Vs Zombies. The UI is crisp and clear (albeit mobile-esque), the upgrade and progress system is very well implemented and the abilities and new units get introduced at just the right pace. It''s also very intuitive, with absorbing gameplay and a good mix of enemies. Additionally, they have the balance spot-on in my opinion... up to about Stage 45-46 where you''ll hit a very discernible wall. (Just farm gold and buy a load of "destroy the whole floor" power-ups.)

My only gripe is that there are too many units and no filter feature at the Squad Screen to filter out the units you don''t want / never use. Other than that I recommend this as the go-to game for fans of Plants Vs Zombies who want a change but also wish to keep scratching that lane tower defense itch.

[url=https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCvvMSERiysrh0aUgU7T09TA/videos] 40 Genres / 40 Top Tens - Enjoy! [/url]'),
