	 ('102603683','76561199056765495','1197770','20251230',0,0,0,0,7,'The game is a sexual parody on fairy tales, where the heroine uses carnal skills and power of lust to defeat a “great evil”.
The game has an interesting idea, some lore to justify the world''s current state and hostilities, the magic gem, which converts lust into a weapon. So much potential and so poor implementation. What a disappointment... 

The game is totally linear. There are no side quests, optional locations or else. We are walking through corridor-like locations, fighting demons and seeking “pleasure” along the way.
The entire walkthrough takes 4 hours in total. In the end there is a feeling it would better be put into a movie then a video game, since there is not much of a gameplay.

Graphics is poor. The main character and some other humans have been drawn relatively well, but the buildings, monsters and overall environment have been neglected. The game uses vivid and bright colors, which compensates the visual impression a little bit.
Skeleton models are too basic. Characters look like they have been made from wood - not from flesh. The body proportions seem incorrect. Thus the animations look poor as well. 
Besides overall low animation quality, the sexual scenes use some absurd and unrealistic poses, defying the physics. In total they look rather stupid then lustful.

The game contains some graphical glitches and physics collisions (sometimes you can pass through solid walls, sometimes stuck at the plain road).

Some may say that asking for good graphics and visuals is too much for such a game, but since the game does not actually provide anything else - it is something, which should have been done properly.

Fighting with demons is implemented through the very basic turn-based combat system. Here we can attack, use distraction or a healing potion - these are all available options. I suppose the combat could be done at least a bit more interesting. It would not require too much effort to do so.

We have a magical Gem of Lust, which converts Lilly’s lust energy into a destructive power to break a Demon gates. But its usage is restricted only by the story events. It would be nice if it would be used as a combat mechanic: like we need to accumulate the lust through some carnal actions and then unleash it in a form of magical spell on the enemies.

The only good thing which can be said about this game: it gives you a lot of laughs. The actual story, the jokes - these have been done well.

Sound is good. Music suits the game nicely, and the voice actors did a great job.
However, there are no subtitles for the voiced dialogs. In case English is not your native language, you may have a lot of trouble understanding what the characters say.

I do understand that such a game is a great achievement for a small development team, but knowing what it is, I would not pay my money for it. I have seen products, distributed for free, which give better experience.

Sorry, Lilly, you have tried, but…'),
