	 ('201161265','76561198318712615','2427430','20251230',0,0,0,0,10,'S.T.A.L.K.E.R.: Call of Pripyat was what the first 2 games should have been. This was a vast improvement in all aspects, from gameplay to storyline to open-endedness.
The gameplay is smooth and intuitive. Gone are the weird bugs found in the first two and the controls are more precise.
The story is cool too - you play an outsider coming into the Zone to complete a mission for the military. So in a way you are "starting over" and learning about the Zone as you go, which helps fill in some of the gaps. The dialogue is stilted and silly at times still, but the open world aspect is much more meaningful in this installment. The various outcomes of your missions and who survives/dies affects the ending, and you are given the choice to not end abruptly to tie up loose ends right at the endgame.
In short, the best of the Stalker games within the trilogy of number 1. Highly recommended if you like the Stalker series, and recommended anyways if you enjoy FPS games with some open world flavoring.'),
