	 ('199888454','76561197993703113','2427430','20251230',3,2,0,0,10,'This is the best entry in the original trilogy of STALKER games, but it''s still just not for me. It is atmospheric, the world is vast and detailed, and it should be lauded for its unique take on an open-world shooter game - I can''t help but tune out of these games... There''s just too down-time between meaningful encounters. I suppose I''m just not the kind of guy to get immersed in these worlds, but if you enjoy immersive games, you are likely to really enjoy this.'),
	 ('43424038','76561198202772933','234710','20251230',2,1,0,0,10,'I love this game. The way the characters interact and talk, is worth the entire game all on it''s own. I honestly only bought the game so i could get the tf2 cosmetics, seing as buying both was the same price as a key. I opened the game expecting references from franchises I never have even heard of, seing as I only knew Cl4P-TP and GLaDOS, but I found the dialogue to be interesting, and you feel as if you are part of the conversation, despite being mute. This game also taught me how to play poker. Incredibly addictive and a great time waster, I suggest giving it a try. One downside is, that some lines are repeated consantly by some characters, and with no way to skip that, it can get a bit annoying. 9/10'),
